      ],
      "lineAnnotations": {
        "0": {"synopsis":"The text \"Syntax\" ($0000-$0005): this ROM's name. Nothing jumps here; the machine starts in\nROM 0."},
        "8": {"synopsis":"RST $08: stops with the error code in the byte after the RST, through $2AC8 (ERR_NR = the\ncode). The code in this ROM CALLs $2AC8 directly, with the code byte after the CALL; no RST\n$08 is in it.","comment":"To $2AC8 with the code byte after the RST"},
        "16": {"synopsis":"RST $10: ROM 3's RST $10 (CALL_ROM3), which prints A through the current channel.","comment":"ROM 3's PRINT_A: A printed through the current channel"},
        "24": {"synopsis":"RST $18: ROM 3's RST $18 (CALL_ROM3): the character at CH_ADD.","comment":"ROM 3's GET_CHAR: A = the character at CH_ADD"},
        "32": {"synopsis":"RST $20: ROM 3's RST $20 (CALL_ROM3): the next character at CH_ADD.","comment":"ROM 3's NEXT_SKIP: A = the next character at CH_ADD"},
        "40": {"synopsis":"RST $28: calls the routine in ROM 3 whose address is the word after the RST, then returns\npast the word:\n1. HL = that address; $5B5A = the place after the word, the return point.\n2. CALL_ROM3_GO keeps the address in $5B58, stacks $5B2A (SWAP_HIGH_GO's copy) as the\n   routine's return, then the address, AF and BC, and jumps to $5B10 (SWAP_ROM_HIGH's copy),\n   which flips only the ROM's high bit, so ROM 3 replaces ROM 1, and RETs into the routine.\n3. When the routine returns, $5B2A flips the high bit back and goes on at $5B5A. Keeps every\n   register for the routine.","comment":"HL = the return address, the word's place"},
        "41": {"comment":"A kept"},
        "42": {"comment":"The routine address's low byte"},
        "43": {"comment":"Past the word"},
        "45": {"comment":"$5B5A = the return point after the call"},
        "48": {"comment":"HL = the routine's address"},
        "51": {"comment":"A back"},
        "52": {"comment":"On in CALL_ROM3_GO"},
        "56": {"synopsis":"INT (interrupt mode 1), on each interrupt while this ROM is paged in: adds one to the\nthree-byte FRAMES counter, then reads the keyboard and counts the disk motor's time-out\n(INT_KEYS). Keeps AF, BC, DE and HL; returns with interrupts enabled.","comment":"AF and HL kept"},
        "58": {"comment":"FRAMES' low word"},
        "61": {"comment":"One more"},
        "65": {"comment":"Wrapped to 0?"},
        "67": {"comment":"No"},
        "69": {"comment":"The low word wrapped: FRAMES' third byte ($5C7A)"},
        "72": {"synopsis":"The rest of INT_FRAME: KEYBOARD, then MOTOR_TIMEOUT (unlike ROM 3's INT_KBD_MOTOR, with no\nFLAGS bit 4 test), with BC and DE kept; then the registers back and EI.","comment":"BC and DE kept"},
        "74": {"comment":"The keyboard read"},
        "77": {"comment":"The disk motor's time-out"},
        "80": {"comment":"DE, BC, HL and AF back"},
        "84": {"comment":"Interrupts on again"},
        "86": {"synopsis":"CAT TAB's texts: 'Start: ', $00 (CAT_TAB_TYPE, with EXP) and from $005E 'system', $00 (the\nname of partition type 1); $0065 is a spare $00."},
        "102": {"synopsis":"The NMI handler: when NMIADD ($5CB0) is not zero it jumps there (JP (HL), with AF and HL\nstill on the stack); when it is zero it returns at once (NMI_RETURN).","comment":"AF and HL kept"},
        "104": {"comment":"HL = NMIADD"},
        "107": {"comment":"Is it 0?"},
        "109": {"comment":"Zero: just return"},
        "111": {"comment":"To NMIADD"},
        "112": {"synopsis":"AF and HL back; RETN.","comment":"AF and HL back"},
        "114": {"comment":"Return from the NMI"},
        "116": {"synopsis":"Counts the disk motor's time-out down (the same bytes as ROM 3's MOTOR_TIMEOUT): with bank 7\npaged in (the paging byte $5B5C with bits 0-2 set, to port $7FFD), when the count at $E600\nis not 0 and FRAMES is even, the count goes down by one; when it reaches 0, bit 3 of port\n$1FFD is cleared (its copy at $5B67 too), which turns the motor off. Then port $7FFD gets\n$5B5C back.\nChanges: AF, BC.","comment":"Bank 7 paged in"},
        "126": {"comment":"The count at $E600 (bank 7)"},
        "129": {"comment":"0: nothing to do"},
        "132": {"comment":"FRAMES' low byte"},
        "135": {"comment":"An odd frame: wait"},
        "139": {"comment":"One less"},
        "146": {"comment":"Not yet 0"},
        "148": {"comment":"Port $1FFD"},
        "151": {"comment":"Its copy, bit 3 (the motor) cleared"},
        "161": {"synopsis":"Port $7FFD gets the paging byte $5B5C back.","comment":"The paging byte back"},
        "170": {"synopsis":"CALL_ROM3's second half: the routine's address kept in $5B58; the stack gets SWAP_HIGH_GO's\ncopy ($5B2A) as the routine's return, the routine's address, AF and BC; then, with\ninterrupts off, SWAP_ROM_HIGH's copy at $5B10 pages ROM 3 in and RETs into the routine with\nevery register as it was.","comment":"The routine's address kept"},
        "173": {"comment":"SWAP_HIGH_GO's copy at $5B2A"},
        "176": {"comment":"... as the routine's return; HL back"},
        "177": {"comment":"HL stacked"},
        "178": {"comment":"HL = the routine's address"},
        "181": {"comment":"The routine's address on top, HL back"},
        "182": {"comment":"AF and BC stacked, as SWAP_ROM_HIGH wants them"},
        "184": {"comment":"No interrupts while the ROMs change"},
        "185": {"comment":"SWAP_ROM_HIGH's copy: ROM 3 in, RET to the routine"},
        "188": {"synopsis":"Key table, main: 39 bytes, the code of each key but CAPS SHIFT, by READ_KEYS's key number: B\nH Y 6 5 T G V, N J U 7 4 R F C, M K I 8 3 E D X, SYMBOL SHIFT ($0E) L O 9 2 W S Z, SPACE\nENTER ($0D) P 0 1 Q A. KEY_MAIN_CODE reads it at $00BC + key number. The key tables after it\nrun to $0144; each is indexed from its start less its first code."},
        "227": {"synopsis":"Key table, E mode letters: 26 tokens for A-Z, read from $00A2 + the letter: READ BIN LPRINT\nDATA TAN SGN ABS SQR CODE VAL LEN USR PI INKEY$ PEEK TAB SIN INT RESTORE RND CHR$ LLIST COS\nEXP STR$ LN (spelt as ROM 3's KEYWORD_TABLE has them)."},
        "253": {"synopsis":"Key table, E mode letters with a shift key: 26 bytes for A-Z, read from $00BC + the letter:\n~ BRIGHT PAPER \\ ATN { } CIRCLE IN VAL$ SCREEN$ ATTR INVERSE OVER OUT, $7F for P, ASN VERIFY\n| MERGE ] FLASH ACS INK [ BEEP."},
        "279": {"synopsis":"Key table, CAPS SHIFT digits: 10 control codes for 0-9, read from $00E7 + the digit: $0C $07\n$06 $04 $05 $08 $0A $0B $09 $0F, the manual's DELETE, EDIT, CAPS LOCK, TRUE VIDEO, INV.\nVIDEO, the four cursor keys (5 left, 6 down, 7 up, 8 right) and GRAPHICS. In G mode, 0 and 9\ngive these codes too."},
        "289": {"synopsis":"Key table, SYMBOL SHIFT letters: 26 bytes for A-Z, read from $00E0 + the letter: STOP * ?\nSTEP >= TO THEN ^ AT - + = . , ; \" <= < NOT > OR / <> ` AND :."},
        "315": {"synopsis":"Key table, E mode SYMBOL SHIFT digits: 10 tokens for 0-9, read from $010B + the digit:\nFORMAT, DEF FN, FN, LINE, OPEN #, CLOSE #, MOVE, ERASE, POINT, CAT. READ_KEYS follows."},
        "325": {"synopsis":"Scans the keyboard: reads the eight half-rows (port $FE with B = $FE, $FD, ... $7F) and\ncollects up to two keys down as key numbers, E the last found and D the one before ($FF for\nnone). A key number is $2F less the half-row number less 8 x (bit + 1): CAPS SHIFT is $27,\nSYMBOL SHIFT $18 (Klive's key matrix: row 0 bit 0, row 7 bit 1). Returns NZ at once on a\nthird key. At the end Z means the keys are usable: fewer than two, or two with CAPS SHIFT or\nSYMBOL SHIFT as one of them (then in D).\nExit: DE = the key numbers.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"L = $2F: the first half-row's key number"},
        "327": {"comment":"No keys yet"},
        "330": {"comment":"B = $FE: the first half-row"},
        "333": {"synopsis":"Reads one half-row: A = its five key bits, 1 for a key down.","comment":"The half-row's bits"},
        "335": {"comment":"1 for a key down"},
        "336": {"comment":"Five keys"},
        "338": {"comment":"A key down in this half-row?"},
        "340": {"comment":"H = the keys down"},
        "341": {"comment":"A = the half-row's number"},
        "342": {"synopsis":"One more key found: NZ out at once when D already held one (three keys)."},
        "343": {"comment":"A third key: not usable"},
        "344": {"synopsis":"Finds the key's column: 8 off the number per bit shifted out of H."},
        "346": {"comment":"The next key into the carry"},
        "348": {"comment":"Until the key down"},
        "350": {"comment":"D = the key before"},
        "351": {"comment":"E = this key"},
        "352": {"comment":"More keys in the half-row"},
        "354": {"synopsis":"The next half-row, L one lower, until B's 0 bit has gone round.","comment":"The next half-row's number"},
        "355": {"comment":"The next half-row"},
        "357": {"comment":"Until all eight"},
        "359": {"comment":"A second key in D?"},
        "361": {"comment":"No: Z, done"},
        "362": {"comment":"CAPS SHIFT?"},
        "364": {"comment":"Z: usable"},
        "365": {"comment":"SYMBOL SHIFT?"},
        "367": {"comment":"Z: usable"},
        "368": {"comment":"D and E swapped: the shift key into D"},
        "371": {"comment":"Z when it is SYMBOL SHIFT; NZ: two keys, no shift"},
        "374": {"synopsis":"Reads the keyboard, from INT_KEYS on every interrupt, and keeps the two key sets of KSTATE\n(4 bytes each: the main code or $FF when unused, a release counter, the repeat counter, the\ndecoded code):\n1. READ_KEYS; nothing when it reports NZ (three keys, or two without a shift key).\n2. Each set in use counts its release counter down; at 0 the set is freed (KBD_SET_LOOP).\n3. KEY_MAIN_CODE turns the scan into a main code; none for no key or a shift key alone.\n4. A code a set already holds is a key still held: KBD_REPEAT. A new one goes into a free\n   set, the second one first, and is decoded (KBD_NEW_KEY); with both sets in use it is\n   ignored. A new or repeated key goes into LAST_K, with FLAGS bit 5 set.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL; KSTATE, LAST_K, FLAGS.","comment":"The keys down"},
        "377": {"comment":"Not usable"},
        "378": {"comment":"HL = KSTATE's first set"},
        "381": {"synopsis":"One key set: in use (bit 7 of its first byte clear)? Then its release counter one down, and\nthe set freed ($FF) when it reaches 0."},
        "386": {"comment":"Its release counter down"},
        "390": {"comment":"Freed"},
        "392": {"synopsis":"After the set at $5C00, the one at $5C04.","comment":"A = L: which set?"},
        "393": {"comment":"The second set next"},
        "399": {"comment":"No usable key?"},
        "406": {"comment":"Held in the first set?"},
        "409": {"comment":"DE = the first set"},
        "413": {"comment":"Held in the second set?"},
        "416": {"comment":"The second set free?"},
        "420": {"comment":"HL = the first set"},
        "421": {"comment":"The first set free? Neither: the key is ignored"},
        "424": {"synopsis":"A new key into the free set at HL: its main code, release counter 5, repeat counter REPDEL,\nthen the code KEY_DECODE gives for MODE (C), FLAGS (D) and the shift key (B).","comment":"E = the main code"},
        "425": {"comment":"Into the set"},
        "427": {"comment":"Release counter 5"},
        "430": {"comment":"Repeat counter REPDEL"},
        "435": {"comment":"C = MODE"},
        "438": {"comment":"D = FLAGS"},
        "442": {"comment":"A = the decoded code"},
        "446": {"comment":"Into the set"},
        "447": {"synopsis":"LAST_K = A, and FLAGS bit 5 set: a key is waiting."},
        "455": {"synopsis":"A key still held: its release counter back to 5, and the repeat counter one down; at 0 it is\nset to REPPER and the set's decoded code goes into LAST_K again (KBD_STORE_KEY)."},
        "456": {"comment":"Release counter 5 again"},
        "459": {"comment":"Repeat counter down"},
        "460": {"comment":"Not yet"},
        "461": {"comment":"REPPER from now on"},
        "466": {"comment":"A = the set's decoded code"},
        "469": {"synopsis":"Turns READ_KEYS's key numbers into a main code: E is the key, D the shift key ($FF for\nnone).\nExit: carry and A = the key's code from KEYS_MAIN; no carry for no key, CAPS SHIFT alone\n($27) or SYMBOL SHIFT alone; B = the shift key, D = 0.\nChanges: AF, B, D, HL.","comment":"B = the shift key"},
        "470": {"comment":"D = 0 for the index"},
        "472": {"comment":"A = the key"},
        "473": {"comment":"No key, or CAPS SHIFT alone?"},
        "476": {"comment":"SYMBOL SHIFT as the key"},
        "480": {"comment":"... with no other: none"},
        "483": {"synopsis":"A = KEYS_MAIN's code for key number E; carry set.","comment":"HL = KEYS_MAIN"},
        "486": {"comment":"+ the key number"},
        "488": {"comment":"Carry: a key"},
        "490": {"synopsis":"Turns a main code into the code the key gives: E = the main code, B = the shift key ($FF\nnone, $27 CAPS SHIFT, $18 SYMBOL SHIFT), C = MODE (0 K/L/C, 1 E, 2 G), D = FLAGS (bit 3 set:\nL mode). Letters ($41-$5A):\n1. MODE 0, no shift or CAPS SHIFT: a keyword token in K mode (KD_K_TOKEN); in L mode the\n   capital, or the small letter when neither CAPS SHIFT nor CAPS LOCK (FLAGS2 bit 3) is on.\n   SYMBOL SHIFT: KEYS_SYM_LETTERS.\n2. MODE 1: KEYS_E_LETTERS, or KEYS_E_SHIFTED with either shift key (KD_E_LETTER).\n3. MODE 2: the letter + $4F, A to U giving $90-$A4. Digits go to KD_DIGIT; the other codes\n   come back as they are.\nExit: A = the code.\nChanges: AF, BC, D, HL.","comment":"A = the main code"},
        "491": {"comment":"Below \":\": a digit, space, ENTER or SYMBOL SHIFT"},
        "495": {"comment":"MODE - 1"},
        "496": {"comment":"MODE 0?"},
        "499": {"comment":"MODE 1?"},
        "501": {"comment":"MODE 2: A-U to $90-$A4"},
        "504": {"synopsis":"A letter in E mode: KEYS_E_LETTERS with no shift key, KEYS_E_SHIFTED with either."},
        "507": {"comment":"No shift key ($FF + 1 = 0)?"},
        "510": {"comment":"Either: KEYS_E_SHIFTED"},
        "513": {"synopsis":"A = the byte at HL + E: the key's entry in the table chosen (HL is the table's start less\nthe first code).","comment":"DE = the code"},
        "518": {"synopsis":"A letter in K, L or C mode: with SYMBOL SHIFT (B bit 0 clear) from KEYS_SYM_LETTERS;\notherwise a token in K mode, a letter in L mode.","comment":"HL for KEYS_SYM_LETTERS"},
        "521": {"comment":"SYMBOL SHIFT ($18, bit 0 clear)?"},
        "525": {"comment":"FLAGS bit 3 clear: K mode?"},
        "529": {"comment":"CAPS LOCK: the capital"},
        "534": {"comment":"CAPS SHIFT: the capital"},
        "536": {"comment":"Otherwise the small letter"},
        "539": {"synopsis":"K mode: the letter + $A5, a keyword token (A gives $E6, NEW)."},
        "542": {"synopsis":"Codes below $3A: below \"0\" (space, ENTER, SYMBOL SHIFT's $0E) as they are; digits by MODE.\nMODE 1 (E): SYMBOL SHIFT from KEYS_E_SYM_DIGIT; otherwise 0-7 give $10-$17, or $18-$1F with\nCAPS SHIFT, and 8, 9 (KD_E_8_9).","comment":"Below '0': as it is"},
        "545": {"comment":"MODE - 1"},
        "546": {"comment":"MODE 0?"},
        "549": {"comment":"MODE 2?"},
        "551": {"comment":"HL for KEYS_E_SYM_DIGIT"},
        "554": {"comment":"SYMBOL SHIFT (bit 5 clear)?"},
        "558": {"comment":"8 or 9?"},
        "562": {"comment":"0-7: $10-$17"},
        "566": {"comment":"... or $18-$1F with CAPS SHIFT"},
        "569": {"synopsis":"8 and 9 in E mode: 2 and 3, or 0 and 1 with CAPS SHIFT.","comment":"8 and 9 become 2 and 3"},
        "571": {"comment":"No shift: done"},
        "573": {"comment":"Less 2: 0 and 1"},
        "576": {"synopsis":"A digit in G mode: 0 and 9 from KEYS_CAPS_DIGITS; 1-8 give the block graphics $81-$87 and\n$80 (for 8), or with CAPS SHIFT the same XOR $0F ($8E-$88, $8F).","comment":"HL for KEYS_CAPS_DIGITS"},
        "579": {"comment":"9?"},
        "583": {"comment":"0?"},
        "587": {"comment":"1-8 become 1-7 and 0"},
        "589": {"comment":"$80-$87"},
        "591": {"comment":"No shift: done"},
        "593": {"comment":"CAPS SHIFT: the inverse block"},
        "596": {"synopsis":"A digit in K, L or C mode: the digit with no shift key; with CAPS SHIFT from\nKEYS_CAPS_DIGITS; with SYMBOL SHIFT the character $10 below it (1 \"!\", 3 \"#\" ... 9 \")\"),\nexcept 2 (\"@\", KD_AT_SIGN) and 0 (\"_\").","comment":"No shift: the digit itself"},
        "598": {"comment":"CAPS SHIFT (bit 5 of B + 1 set)?"},
        "605": {"comment":"SYMBOL SHIFT: the character $10 below"},
        "607": {"comment":"2: \"@\""},
        "611": {"comment":"0: \"_\""},
        "614": {"comment":"\"_\""},
        "617": {"synopsis":"SYMBOL SHIFT + 2: \"@\"."},
        "620": {"synopsis":"FORMAT (class $0E; its word at $0FA9 in the syntax table):\n1. FORMAT LPRINT goes to FORMAT_LPRINT, FORMAT LINE to FORMAT_LINE and FORMAT TO to\n   FORMAT_TO (a hard disk).\n2. Otherwise FORMAT \"A:\" or \"B:\" formats the disk in that drive: the name must be two\n   characters, a drive letter A or B (either case) and ':' (error $4E, Invalid drive,\n   otherwise); checking ends there ($10B0).\n3. Bank 7 and its stack ($2B73). Without a disk interface ($5B66 bit 4 clear) it is error\n   $4C (+2A does not support format); drive B needs $5B66 bit 5 (error $4B, Drive B: is not\n   present).\n4. The drive's parameter block (+3DOS DRIVE_FIND) and the disk's format (DISK_IDENTIFY): a\n   disk in format 0 asks first (FORMAT_ASK; A abandons), another format is formatted at\n   once; of the +3DOS errors only 5 and 9 (an unformatted disk) go on.\n5. Format 0 set (FORMAT_SELECT) and tracks 0-39 formatted (TRACK_FORMAT), each with nine\n   sectors (FMT_ID_FIELDS) filled with $E5.\nA +3DOS error is reported through $0E99.","comment":"ROM 3's GET_CHAR: the character after FORMAT"},
        "623": {"comment":"LPRINT?"},
        "625": {"comment":"FORMAT LPRINT"},
        "628": {"comment":"LINE?"},
        "633": {"comment":"TO? FORMAT TO, a hard disk"},
        "638": {"synopsis":"FORMAT \"x:\": the drive's name.","comment":"ROM 3's CLASS_A: the name, a string"},
        "641": {"comment":"Checking ends here"},
        "644": {"comment":"ROM 3's STK_FETCH: DE = the name, BC = its length"},
        "647": {"comment":"Two characters?"},
        "651": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "653": {"comment":"Report: Invalid drive (error $4E)","synopsis":"Stops with error $4E (Invalid drive): FORMAT's name is not two characters; FORMAT LPRINT's\nbad letters come here too (from $0404, $0417, $0424, $0444)."},
        "657": {"synopsis":"The second character must be ':'.","comment":"The second character"},
        "660": {"comment":"':'?"},
        "662": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "664": {"comment":"Report: Invalid drive (error $4E)"},
        "668": {"synopsis":"The first must be A or B, in either case.","comment":"The first, as a capital"},
        "671": {"comment":"A?"},
        "675": {"comment":"B?"},
        "679": {"comment":"Report: Invalid drive (error $4E)"},
        "683": {"synopsis":"Running on bank 7's stack: the unit (0 for A, 1 for B) and the drives present ($5B66 bits 4\nand 5).","comment":"Bank 7 and its stack"},
        "686": {"comment":"A = the unit: 0 for A, 1 for B"},
        "688": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "689": {"comment":"A disk interface? ($5B66 bit 4)"},
        "694": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "696": {"comment":"Bank 0 and the machine stack"},
        "699": {"comment":"Report: +2A does not support format (error $4C)"},
        "703": {"synopsis":"A disk interface: drive A is there; drive B needs $5B66 bit 5.","comment":"The unit back"},
        "704": {"comment":"Drive A?"},
        "707": {"comment":"B: kept again"},
        "708": {"comment":"Drive B present? ($5B66 bit 5)"},
        "715": {"comment":"Bank 0 and the machine stack"},
        "718": {"comment":"Report: Drive B: is not present (error $4B)"},
        "722": {"synopsis":"Drive B present: the unit back.","comment":"The unit back"},
        "723": {"synopsis":"The drive's parameter block (+3DOS DRIVE_FIND), then the disk's format (DISK_IDENTIFY).","comment":"The unit kept for the tracks"},
        "724": {"comment":"C = the unit, kept"},
        "726": {"comment":"A = the drive letter"},
        "728": {"comment":"Onto +3DOS's stack ($3213)"},
        "731": {"comment":"+3DOS DRIVE_FIND: IX = the drive's parameter block"},
        "736": {"comment":"Back to this ROM's stack ($324B)"},
        "739": {"comment":"Found?"},
        "741": {"comment":"Bank 0 and the machine stack"},
        "744": {"comment":"Report the +3DOS error in A (byte $FF)"},
        "748": {"synopsis":"+3DOS DISK_IDENTIFY for unit C: which format is on the disk.","comment":"C = the unit"},
        "749": {"comment":"Onto +3DOS's stack"},
        "752": {"comment":"+3DOS DISK_IDENTIFY: A = the disk's format"},
        "757": {"comment":"Back to this ROM's stack"},
        "760": {"comment":"No format found?"},
        "762": {"comment":"A format other than 0: formatted without asking"},
        "765": {"comment":"Format 0: ask first"},
        "768": {"comment":"Any key but A: go on"},
        "770": {"comment":"A: abandoned; bank 0 and the machine stack"},
        "773": {"comment":"Done"},
        "774": {"synopsis":"DISK_IDENTIFY failed: errors 5 (missing address mark) and 9 (unsuitable media) mean a disk\nto format; the others are reported.","comment":"Error 5: missing address mark?"},
        "778": {"comment":"Error 9: unsuitable media?"},
        "782": {"comment":"Bank 0 and the machine stack"},
        "785": {"comment":"Report the +3DOS error in A"},
        "789": {"synopsis":"Formats: the drive's block again (DRIVE_FIND), set for format 0 (FORMAT_SELECT).","comment":"The unit"},
        "790": {"comment":"Kept again"},
        "791": {"comment":"A = the drive letter"},
        "793": {"comment":"Onto +3DOS's stack"},
        "796": {"comment":"+3DOS DRIVE_FIND again"},
        "801": {"comment":"Back to this ROM's stack"},
        "804": {"comment":"Found?"},
        "806": {"comment":"Bank 0 and the machine stack"},
        "809": {"comment":"Report the +3DOS error in A"},
        "813": {"synopsis":"Format 0 into the drive's block (+3DOS FORMAT_SELECT).","comment":"Format 0"},
        "814": {"comment":"Onto +3DOS's stack"},
        "817": {"comment":"+3DOS FORMAT_SELECT: the block set for format 0"},
        "822": {"comment":"Back to this ROM's stack"},
        "825": {"comment":"Done?"},
        "827": {"comment":"Bank 0 and the machine stack"},
        "830": {"comment":"Report the +3DOS error in A"},
        "834": {"synopsis":"C = the unit; tracks 0 to 39.","comment":"C = the unit"},
        "836": {"comment":"Track 0"},
        "837": {"synopsis":"One track: its ID fields (FMT_ID_FIELDS), then +3DOS TRACK_FORMAT with the filler $E5.","comment":"D = the track"},
        "838": {"comment":"Its nine ID fields at $ED11"},
        "841": {"comment":"Filler byte $E5"},
        "843": {"comment":"The fields are in bank 7"},
        "845": {"comment":"HL = the ID fields"},
        "848": {"comment":"The track kept"},
        "849": {"comment":"Onto +3DOS's stack"},
        "852": {"comment":"+3DOS TRACK_FORMAT"},
        "857": {"comment":"Back to this ROM's stack"},
        "860": {"comment":"Formatted?"},
        "862": {"comment":"Bank 0 and the machine stack"},
        "865": {"comment":"Report the +3DOS error in A"},
        "869": {"synopsis":"The next track, up to 39.","comment":"The track back"},
        "870": {"comment":"The next"},
        "871": {"comment":"Past track 39?"},
        "875": {"comment":"Bank 0 and the machine stack"},
        "878": {"comment":"Done"},
        "879": {"synopsis":"Writes the ID fields TRACK_FORMAT takes for track D at $ED11-$ED34 (bank 7, paged in): nine\nof four bytes, the track (D), head 0, the sector (1-9) and size code 2, filled backwards\nfrom sector 9's at $ED31.\nChanges: B, HL.","comment":"Nine sectors"},
        "881": {"comment":"HL = the last field's last byte"},
        "884": {"synopsis":"One field, backwards: size code 2, the sector (B), head 0, the track.","comment":"Size code 2"},
        "887": {"comment":"The sector, B"},
        "889": {"comment":"Head 0"},
        "892": {"comment":"The track, D"},
        "894": {"comment":"The next field down"},
        "897": {"synopsis":"Asks before formatting a disk in format 0: prints MSG_FORMATTED through ROM 3's PRINT_A,\nwaits for a key (FLAGS bit 5), then clears the lower screen (ROM 3's CLS_LOWER).\nExit: Z when the key was A (either case).\nChanges: AF.","comment":"HL = the text"},
        "900": {"synopsis":"One character, up to the $00.","comment":"The $00 at its end?"},
        "904": {"comment":"ROM 3's PRINT_A"},
        "907": {"comment":"The next"},
        "910": {"synopsis":"No key waiting yet (FLAGS bit 5 cleared).","comment":"No key yet"},
        "914": {"synopsis":"Until a key arrives.","comment":"A key?"},
        "920": {"comment":"LAST_K, as a capital"},
        "925": {"comment":"A?"},
        "927": {"comment":"The answer and HL kept"},
        "929": {"comment":"ROM 3's CLS_LOWER"},
        "932": {"comment":"Back"},
        "935": {"synopsis":"FORMAT_ASK's text: \"Disk is already formatted.\", ENTER, \"A to abandon, other key continue\",\n$00."},
        "995": {"synopsis":"FORMAT LPRINT \"x\" or FORMAT LPRINT \"x\";\"y\": printer options. Each string must be one letter\n(either case; error $4E, Invalid drive, through FORMAT_BAD_DRIVE otherwise), and each letter\nsets an option: R sets and C clears $5B66 bit 3; E sets and U clears $5B66 bit 2. The second\nstring may only be E or U. Checking ends after the strings ($10B0).","comment":"Past LPRINT"},
        "998": {"comment":"ROM 3's CLASS_A: the first string"},
        "1001": {"comment":"ROM 3's GET_CHAR: the character after it"},
        "1004": {"comment":"';'?"},
        "1006": {"comment":"No: the statement must end here"},
        "1009": {"comment":"No ';': the first string alone"},
        "1011": {"comment":"Past ';'"},
        "1014": {"comment":"ROM 3's CLASS_A: the second string"},
        "1017": {"comment":"The statement must end here"},
        "1020": {"comment":"ROM 3's STK_FETCH: the second string"},
        "1023": {"comment":"One character?"},
        "1026": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "1028": {"comment":"No: error $4E (FORMAT_BAD_DRIVE)"},
        "1031": {"synopsis":"The second string's letter: E sets $5B66 bit 2.","comment":"Its letter, as a capital"},
        "1034": {"comment":"HL = $5B66"},
        "1037": {"comment":"E?"},
        "1041": {"comment":"E: bit 2 set"},
        "1043": {"comment":"On to the first string"},
        "1045": {"synopsis":"U clears bit 2; any other letter is report C.","comment":"U?"},
        "1047": {"comment":"Any other: error $4E (FORMAT_BAD_DRIVE)"},
        "1050": {"comment":"U: bit 2 cleared"},
        "1052": {"synopsis":"The first string: one letter.","comment":"ROM 3's STK_FETCH: the first string"},
        "1055": {"comment":"One character?"},
        "1058": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "1060": {"comment":"No: error $4E (FORMAT_BAD_DRIVE)"},
        "1063": {"synopsis":"Its letter: R sets $5B66 bit 3.","comment":"Its letter, as a capital"},
        "1066": {"comment":"HL = $5B66"},
        "1069": {"comment":"R?"},
        "1073": {"comment":"R: bit 3 set"},
        "1076": {"synopsis":"C clears $5B66 bit 3.","comment":"C?"},
        "1080": {"comment":"C: bit 3 cleared"},
        "1083": {"synopsis":"E sets $5B66 bit 2.","comment":"E?"},
        "1087": {"comment":"E: bit 2 set"},
        "1090": {"synopsis":"U clears $5B66 bit 2; any other letter is error $4E (FORMAT_BAD_DRIVE).","comment":"U?"},
        "1092": {"comment":"Any other: error $4E (FORMAT_BAD_DRIVE)"},
        "1095": {"comment":"U: bit 2 cleared"},
        "1098": {"synopsis":"ERASE \"name\" (its word at $0FB3 in the syntax table, after classes $0A and $0C): deletes the\nfiles the name matches (+3DOS FILE_DELETE).\n1. An empty name is error $2C (Bad filename).\n2. A name with a '*' or '?' asks first, on the lower screen (ROM 3's CHAN_OPEN, stream $FD):\n   \"Erase \", the name, \" ? (Y/N)\"; N clears the lower screen and returns without deleting,\n   Y goes on, other keys wait again.\n3. The lower screen cleared (ROM 3's CLS_LOWER); the name goes to $ED01 in bank 7, ended by\n   $FF, and FILE_DELETE runs on bank 7's stack.\nA +3DOS error is reported through $0E99.","comment":"ROM 3's STK_FETCH: DE = the name, BC = its length"},
        "1101": {"comment":"Empty?"},
        "1105": {"comment":"Report: Bad filename (error $2C)"},
        "1109": {"synopsis":"A name: does it have a wildcard?","comment":"The length and the name kept"},
        "1111": {"comment":"HL = the name"},
        "1113": {"comment":"The length kept"},
        "1114": {"comment":"A '*' in it?"},
        "1118": {"comment":"The length back"},
        "1119": {"comment":"Yes: ask"},
        "1121": {"comment":"HL = the name again"},
        "1123": {"comment":"The length kept"},
        "1124": {"comment":"A '?' in it?"},
        "1128": {"comment":"The length back"},
        "1129": {"comment":"Yes: ask"},
        "1131": {"comment":"No wildcard: no question"},
        "1133": {"synopsis":"A wildcard: the question goes to the lower screen (ROM 3's CHAN_OPEN with A = $FD, stream\n-3), the name and its length kept round it.","comment":"The name and length kept"},
        "1135": {"comment":"Stream $FD: the lower screen"},
        "1137": {"comment":"ROM 3's CHAN_OPEN"},
        "1140": {"comment":"Back"},
        "1142": {"synopsis":"A wildcard: \"Erase \", the name, \" ? (Y/N)\".","comment":"\"Erase \""},
        "1148": {"comment":"The name"},
        "1151": {"comment":"\" ? (Y/N)\""},
        "1157": {"synopsis":"Waits for a key: N returns, Y deletes, other keys wait again.","comment":"FLAGS: no key yet"},
        "1162": {"synopsis":"Until a key arrives (FLAGS bit 5).","comment":"A key?"},
        "1166": {"comment":"Taken"},
        "1168": {"comment":"LAST_K, as a capital"},
        "1173": {"comment":"N?"},
        "1177": {"comment":"N: the lower screen cleared (ROM 3's CLS_LOWER)"},
        "1180": {"comment":"N: the name and length dropped, nothing deleted"},
        "1183": {"synopsis":"Y deletes; another key waits again.","comment":"Y?"},
        "1187": {"comment":"Other keys: again"},
        "1189": {"synopsis":"Deletes: the lower screen cleared, the name to $ED01 in bank 7, +3DOS FILE_DELETE.","comment":"ROM 3's CLS_LOWER"},
        "1192": {"comment":"The name and its length back"},
        "1194": {"comment":"To $ED01 in bank 7"},
        "1198": {"comment":"... copied ($3F63)"},
        "1201": {"comment":"Bank 7 and its stack"},
        "1204": {"comment":"$FF after the name"},
        "1207": {"comment":"HL = the name"},
        "1210": {"comment":"Onto +3DOS's stack"},
        "1213": {"comment":"+3DOS FILE_DELETE"},
        "1218": {"comment":"Back to this ROM's stack"},
        "1221": {"comment":"Bank 0 and the machine stack"},
        "1224": {"comment":"Deleted: done"},
        "1225": {"comment":"Report the +3DOS error in A"},
        "1229": {"synopsis":"Prints the text at HL, ended by a $00, through ROM 3's PRINT_A (the same job as\nCAT_TEXT_OUT).\nExit: HL at the $00.\nChanges: AF, HL.","comment":"The $00 at its end?"},
        "1232": {"comment":"Past the character"},
        "1233": {"comment":"ROM 3's PRINT_A"},
        "1236": {"comment":"The next"},
        "1238": {"synopsis":"Prints BC characters from DE through ROM 3's PRINT_A.\nExit: BC = 0, DE past them.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE.","comment":"The next character"},
        "1239": {"comment":"ROM 3's PRINT_A"},
        "1242": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "1243": {"comment":"One less"},
        "1244": {"comment":"All printed?"},
        "1253": {"synopsis":"MOVE \"a\" TO \"b\" (from MOVE_ENTRY at $389C, which has taken TO, the second name and the\nstatement's end): renames the file a to b (+3DOS FILE_RENAME); a second string starting with\n'+' or '-' changes the file's attributes instead (MOVE_ATTRIB).","comment":"ROM 3's STK_FETCH: the second string"},
        "1256": {"comment":"Empty?"},
        "1260": {"comment":"Report: Bad filename (error $2C)"},
        "1264": {"synopsis":"Its first character: '+' or '-' is an attribute change; otherwise the new name.","comment":"Its first character"},
        "1265": {"comment":"'+'?"},
        "1270": {"comment":"'-'?"},
        "1275": {"comment":"To $ED01 in bank 7"},
        "1279": {"comment":"... copied ($3F63)"},
        "1282": {"comment":"Bank 7 and its stack"},
        "1285": {"comment":"$FF after it"},
        "1288": {"comment":"DE = the place after it"},
        "1289": {"comment":"Bank 0 and the machine stack"},
        "1292": {"comment":"Kept for the old name"},
        "1293": {"comment":"ROM 3's STK_FETCH: the first string, the old name"},
        "1296": {"comment":"Empty?"},
        "1300": {"comment":"Report: Bad filename (error $2C)"},
        "1304": {"synopsis":"The old name after the new one in bank 7, then FILE_RENAME.","comment":"HL = its place in bank 7, kept"},
        "1306": {"comment":"DE = there, HL = the name"},
        "1307": {"comment":"Copied ($3F63)"},
        "1310": {"comment":"Bank 7 and its stack"},
        "1313": {"comment":"$FF after it"},
        "1316": {"comment":"Bank 0 and the machine stack"},
        "1319": {"comment":"HL = the old name"},
        "1320": {"comment":"DE = the new name"},
        "1323": {"comment":"Bank 7 and its stack"},
        "1326": {"comment":"Onto +3DOS's stack"},
        "1329": {"comment":"+3DOS FILE_RENAME"},
        "1334": {"comment":"Back to this ROM's stack"},
        "1337": {"comment":"Bank 0 and the machine stack"},
        "1340": {"comment":"Renamed: done"},
        "1341": {"comment":"Report the +3DOS error in A"},
        "1345": {"synopsis":"MOVE \"name\" TO \"+x\" or \"-x\": x is P, S or A (either case), the attribute of the first,\nsecond or third type letter (+3DOS ATTRIB_SET's bits 2, 1, 0 of D and E); '+' sets it, '-'\nclears it. The second string must be two characters and a known letter (error $47, Invalid\nattribute, otherwise); the first is the file's name (error $2C when empty), to $ED01 in bank\n7.","comment":"Two characters?"},
        "1349": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "1351": {"comment":"Report: Invalid attribute (error $47)"},
        "1355": {"synopsis":"B = the sign; the letter, as a capital, must be P, S or A.","comment":"B = '+' or '-'"},
        "1357": {"comment":"The letter"},
        "1359": {"comment":"As a capital"},
        "1361": {"comment":"P?"},
        "1365": {"comment":"S?"},
        "1369": {"comment":"A?"},
        "1373": {"comment":"Report: Invalid attribute (error $47)"},
        "1377": {"synopsis":"The sign and the letter kept; the file's name, which must not be empty.","comment":"The sign kept"},
        "1378": {"comment":"The letter kept"},
        "1379": {"comment":"ROM 3's STK_FETCH: the file's name"},
        "1382": {"comment":"Empty?"},
        "1386": {"comment":"Report: Bad filename (error $2C)"},
        "1390": {"synopsis":"The name to $ED01 in bank 7, $FF after it; then the letter's bit.","comment":"To $ED01 in bank 7"},
        "1394": {"comment":"... copied ($3F63)"},
        "1397": {"comment":"Bank 7 and its stack"},
        "1400": {"comment":"$FF after it"},
        "1403": {"comment":"Bank 0 and the machine stack"},
        "1406": {"comment":"No bits yet"},
        "1409": {"comment":"C = the letter's bit"},
        "1411": {"comment":"The letter"},
        "1412": {"comment":"P?"},
        "1416": {"comment":"P: bit 2 (type letter 1)"},
        "1420": {"synopsis":"S: bit 1.","comment":"S?"},
        "1424": {"comment":"S: bit 1 (type letter 2)"},
        "1428": {"synopsis":"A: bit 0 (type letter 3).","comment":"A: bit 0"},
        "1430": {"synopsis":"A = the sign (from the BC pushed): '+' puts the bit in D (to set), '-' in E (to clear).","comment":"A = the sign"},
        "1431": {"comment":"'+'?"},
        "1435": {"comment":"D: to set"},
        "1438": {"synopsis":"'-': the bit in E, to clear.","comment":"E: to clear"},
        "1439": {"synopsis":"+3DOS ATTRIB_SET on the name at $ED01.","comment":"HL = the name"},
        "1442": {"comment":"Bank 7 and its stack"},
        "1445": {"comment":"Onto +3DOS's stack"},
        "1448": {"comment":"+3DOS ATTRIB_SET"},
        "1453": {"comment":"Back to this ROM's stack"},
        "1456": {"comment":"Bank 0 and the machine stack"},
        "1459": {"comment":"Set: done"},
        "1460": {"comment":"Report the +3DOS error in A"},
        "1464": {"synopsis":"CAT (class $0E; its word at $0FB6 in the syntax table): CAT [#n,] [\"name\"] [EXP] lists the\ndisk files matching the name (all of the default drive without one), 64 at a time through\n+3DOS CATALOGUE, then the free space; CAT [#n] TAB [EXP] lists the hard disk partitions\n(CAT_TAB) and CAT [#n] ASN the drive letters (CAT_ASN):\n1. '#' and a stream (ROM 3's STREAM_ALTER), then ',' and a name, or the statement's end,\n   EXP,\n   TAB or ASN (report C otherwise, CAT_STREAM_MORE); without '#', stream 2 when running.\n2. The name (ROM 3's CLASS_A) and EXP ($5B66 bit 6: system files too, and the attributes\n   shown); checking ends here ($10B0). A letter A-Z before a ':' in the name is the drive\nfor\n   the free space, kept at $5C0B (0 for the default). A name of \"T:\" goes to $3423.\n3. The name to $ED01 in bank 7, ended by $FF; each file printed as name.type, with PRT, SYS\n   and ARC for EXP, and its size in K (CAT_LIST); \"No files found\" when none (CAT_NO_FILES).\n4. The free space (CAT_FREE).\nA +3DOS error is reported through $0E99.","comment":"No EXP yet ($5B66 bit 6)"},
        "1469": {"comment":"ROM 3's STREAM_ALTER: '#' and a stream?"},
        "1472": {"comment":"No '#'"},
        "1474": {"comment":"The character after the stream"},
        "1478": {"comment":"','?"},
        "1482": {"comment":"ENTER: no name"},
        "1486": {"comment":"':': no name"},
        "1490": {"comment":"EXP: no name"},
        "1494": {"comment":"TAB, ASN or report C (CAT_STREAM_MORE)"},
        "1498": {"synopsis":"Past the ',': the name.","comment":"Past the ','"},
        "1499": {"comment":"The name"},
        "1501": {"synopsis":"No '#': stream 2 when running.","comment":"Stream 2"},
        "1503": {"comment":"Running?"},
        "1509": {"comment":"ROM 3's STREAM_SELECT"},
        "1512": {"synopsis":"ENTER or ':' next: no name (CAT_ALL); EXP, TAB, ASN or a name at CAT_MORE.","comment":"The character at CH_ADD"},
        "1516": {"comment":"ENTER?"},
        "1520": {"comment":"':'?"},
        "1524": {"comment":"EXP, ASN, TAB or a name (CAT_MORE)"},
        "1528": {"synopsis":"The name, a string, and EXP after it.","comment":"ROM 3's CLASS_A: the name"},
        "1531": {"comment":"ROM 3's GET_CHAR: what follows"},
        "1534": {"comment":"EXP?"},
        "1538": {"comment":"EXP: $5B66 bit 6 set"},
        "1543": {"comment":"Past EXP"},
        "1546": {"synopsis":"Checking ends here; running, a drive letter A-Z before a ':' in the name kept at $5C0B.","comment":"Checking ends here"},
        "1549": {"comment":"ROM 3's STK_FETCH: DE = the name, BC = its length"},
        "1552": {"comment":"The length kept"},
        "1553": {"comment":"HL = the name"},
        "1555": {"comment":"A ':' in it?"},
        "1559": {"comment":"No"},
        "1561": {"comment":"Back to the character before the ':'"},
        "1563": {"comment":"The drive letter, as a capital"},
        "1566": {"comment":"Below A?"},
        "1570": {"comment":"Above Z?"},
        "1574": {"comment":"$5C0B = the letter"},
        "1577": {"comment":"On"},
        "1579": {"synopsis":"No drive letter in the name: $5C0B = 0, the default drive.","comment":"$5C0B = 0: the default drive"},
        "1583": {"synopsis":"BC = the length again.","comment":"The length back"},
        "1584": {"comment":"On"},
        "1586": {"synopsis":"No name: EXP may still follow; BC = 0 and $5C0B = 0.","comment":"ROM 3's GET_CHAR"},
        "1589": {"comment":"EXP?"},
        "1593": {"comment":"EXP: $5B66 bit 6 set"},
        "1598": {"comment":"Past EXP"},
        "1601": {"synopsis":"Checking ends here; an empty name, the default drive.","comment":"Checking ends here"},
        "1610": {"synopsis":"A name of two characters, T and ':' (either case): the tape, at $3423.","comment":"Two characters?"},
        "1614": {"comment":"No"},
        "1616": {"comment":"The second"},
        "1619": {"comment":"':'?"},
        "1623": {"comment":"The first, as a capital"},
        "1626": {"comment":"T?"},
        "1630": {"comment":"\"T:\": to $3423"},
        "1633": {"synopsis":"The name to $ED01 in bank 7 (nothing copied when empty).","comment":"To $ED01"},
        "1637": {"comment":"The length kept"},
        "1638": {"comment":"Empty?"},
        "1640": {"comment":"Then nothing copied"},
        "1642": {"comment":"... copied ($3F63)"},
        "1645": {"synopsis":"$FF after the name in bank 7; the buffer's first slot at $ED11 cleared (12 bytes).","comment":"The length back"},
        "1646": {"comment":"HL = the name's end"},
        "1650": {"comment":"Bank 7 and its stack"},
        "1653": {"comment":"$FF after it"},
        "1655": {"comment":"The buffer's first slot"},
        "1661": {"comment":"12 bytes"},
        "1667": {"synopsis":"One page of the catalogue: B = 64 slots, C = 1 with EXP (system files too); then CAT_CALL.\nCAT_LIST comes back here for the names after a full page, with the last name in the first\nslot.","comment":"B = 64 slots"},
        "1669": {"comment":"EXP?"},
        "1676": {"comment":"Yes: every entry, system files too"},
        "1678": {"synopsis":"+3DOS CATALOGUE with DE = the buffer and HL = the name.","comment":"DE = the buffer"},
        "1681": {"comment":"HL = the name"},
        "1684": {"comment":"Onto +3DOS's stack"},
        "1687": {"comment":"+3DOS CATALOGUE"},
        "1692": {"comment":"Back to this ROM's stack"},
        "1695": {"comment":"An error?"},
        "1698": {"comment":"HL = the second slot, the first new name"},
        "1701": {"comment":"B = the new names"},
        "1702": {"comment":"None?"},
        "1704": {"comment":"No: list them"},
        "1706": {"comment":"None: \"No files found\""},
        "1709": {"synopsis":"An error from +3DOS: $17 (nothing matched) is \"No files found\"; the others are reported\nthrough $0E99.","comment":"$17: no file matched?"},
        "1711": {"comment":"\"No files found\""},
        "1714": {"comment":"Bank 0 and the machine stack"},
        "1717": {"comment":"Report the +3DOS error in A"},
        "1721": {"synopsis":"Prints the new names, one a line, from the second slot on (bank 7 paged in between prints):\nthe 8 name letters, '.', the 3 type letters (bit 7 off), EXP's attributes, then the size in\nK.","comment":"The slot count kept"},
        "1722": {"synopsis":"One file: A = the names left.","comment":"The names left kept"},
        "1723": {"comment":"8 letters"},
        "1725": {"synopsis":"One name letter, without its attribute bit.","comment":"The letter, bit 7 off"},
        "1728": {"comment":"Bank 0 and the machine stack"},
        "1731": {"comment":"ROM 3's PRINT_A"},
        "1734": {"comment":"Bank 7 and its stack"},
        "1737": {"comment":"The next"},
        "1740": {"comment":"Bank 0 and the machine stack"},
        "1743": {"comment":"'.'"},
        "1748": {"comment":"No attributes yet ($5B5E)"},
        "1752": {"comment":"3 type letters"},
        "1754": {"synopsis":"One type letter; its bit 7 (an attribute) noted in $5B5E: bit 3 for the first (PROT), 2 for\nthe second (SYS), 1 for the third (ARC).","comment":"Bank 7 and its stack"},
        "1757": {"comment":"The letter"},
        "1758": {"comment":"Its attribute set?"},
        "1762": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "1764": {"comment":"HL = the attribute byte"},
        "1767": {"comment":"The first letter?"},
        "1772": {"comment":"Bit 3: PROT"},
        "1776": {"synopsis":"The second letter: bit 2, SYS.","comment":"The second?"},
        "1780": {"comment":"Bit 2: SYS"},
        "1784": {"synopsis":"The third: bit 1, ARC.","comment":"Bit 1: ARC"},
        "1786": {"synopsis":"The letter back, bit 7 off.","comment":"Back"},
        "1788": {"comment":"Bit 7 off"},
        "1790": {"synopsis":"The letter printed.","comment":"Bank 0 and the machine stack"},
        "1793": {"comment":"ROM 3's PRINT_A"},
        "1796": {"comment":"The next"},
        "1797": {"comment":"All 3?"},
        "1799": {"comment":"HL kept"},
        "1800": {"comment":"EXP?"},
        "1805": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "1806": {"comment":"No: no attributes"},
        "1808": {"comment":"The attributes noted"},
        "1811": {"comment":"HL kept"},
        "1812": {"comment":"Four spaces"},
        "1815": {"comment":"PROT?"},
        "1819": {"comment":"... or \" PRT\""},
        "1822": {"synopsis":"The first field printed; then \" SYS\" or four spaces.","comment":"Printed"},
        "1827": {"comment":"Four spaces"},
        "1830": {"comment":"SYS?"},
        "1834": {"comment":"... or \" SYS\""},
        "1837": {"synopsis":"The second field printed; then \" ARC\" or four spaces.","comment":"Printed"},
        "1842": {"comment":"Four spaces"},
        "1845": {"comment":"ARC?"},
        "1849": {"comment":"... or \" ARC\""},
        "1852": {"synopsis":"The third field printed.","comment":"Printed"},
        "1855": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "1856": {"synopsis":"A space, the size in K (its word, up to 3 digits with blanks before), \"K\" and ENTER; then\nthe next slot.","comment":"A space"},
        "1861": {"comment":"HL kept"},
        "1862": {"comment":"Bank 7 and its stack"},
        "1865": {"comment":"The size's low byte"},
        "1866": {"comment":"Its high byte"},
        "1869": {"comment":"Bank 0 and the machine stack"},
        "1872": {"comment":"HL = the size"},
        "1873": {"comment":"Blanks before the digits"},
        "1875": {"comment":"Printed (NUM_OUT_3)"},
        "1878": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "1879": {"comment":"Past the size: the next slot"},
        "1881": {"comment":"\"K\""},
        "1886": {"comment":"ENTER"},
        "1889": {"comment":"Bank 7 and its stack"},
        "1892": {"comment":"The names left"},
        "1893": {"comment":"One less"},
        "1894": {"comment":"More?"},
        "1897": {"comment":"B = the slots filled"},
        "1898": {"comment":"A full buffer (64)?"},
        "1899": {"comment":"A full buffer (64 slots)?"},
        "1901": {"comment":"No: all listed"},
        "1903": {"comment":"The last slot ($F044)"},
        "1906": {"comment":"... into the first"},
        "1912": {"comment":"Copied"},
        "1914": {"comment":"$ED1C (bank 7) not 0: a later page"},
        "1916": {"comment":"The names after it"},
        "1919": {"synopsis":"All listed: ENTER, then the free space.","comment":"Bank 0 and the machine stack"},
        "1922": {"comment":"ENTER","synopsis":"ENTER, then the free space (CAT_FREE); also after \"No files found\"."},
        "1925": {"comment":"Bank 7 and its stack"},
        "1928": {"synopsis":"The drive: the one at $5C0B, or else +3DOS's default (DRIVE_DEFAULT with $FF).","comment":"The drive letter"},
        "1931": {"comment":"A drive given?"},
        "1934": {"comment":"$FF: read the default"},
        "1936": {"comment":"Onto +3DOS's stack"},
