        "1944": {"comment":"Back to this ROM's stack"},
        "1947": {"comment":"An error?"},
        "1950": {"synopsis":"+3DOS DRIVE_FREE for drive A; its count in HL printed with \"K free\".","comment":"Onto +3DOS's stack"},
        "1953": {"comment":"+3DOS DRIVE_FREE: HL = the free space"},
        "1958": {"comment":"Back to this ROM's stack"},
        "1961": {"comment":"An error?"},
        "1964": {"comment":"Bank 0 and the machine stack"},
        "1967": {"comment":"No blanks before the digits"},
        "1969": {"comment":"HL printed (NUM_OUT_3)"},
        "1972": {"comment":"\"K free\", ENTER"},
        "1978": {"comment":"ENTER"},
        "1981": {"comment":"Done"},
        "1982": {"synopsis":"No file matched: \"No files found\" (MSG_NO_FILES) printed when $ED1C in bank 7 is 0 (the\nfirst\npage, so nothing listed yet), then CAT_DONE_ENTER.","comment":"$ED1C 0: nothing listed yet?"},
        "1986": {"comment":"Bank 0 and the machine stack"},
        "1989": {"comment":"\"No files found\", ENTER"},
        "1995": {"comment":"ENTER and the free space"},
        "1998": {"synopsis":"Prints A (RST $10) in bank 0 on the machine stack, then back to bank 7 and its stack.\nChanges: AF.","comment":"Bank 0 and the machine stack"},
        "2001": {"comment":"A printed"},
        "2002": {"synopsis":"Back to bank 7 and its stack (BANK7_STACK), the end of the three PRINT_x_BANK0 routines.","comment":"Bank 7 and its stack"},
        "2005": {"comment":"Done"},
        "2006": {"synopsis":"Prints the $00-ended text at HL (CAT_TEXT_OUT) in bank 0 on the machine stack, then back to\nbank 7 and its stack.\nExit: HL at the $00.\nChanges: AF, HL.","comment":"Bank 0 and the machine stack"},
        "2009": {"comment":"The text (CAT_TEXT_OUT)"},
        "2012": {"comment":"Back to bank 7"},
        "2014": {"synopsis":"Prints HL as a number (NUM_OUT_5, E the blank before the digits, $FF none) in bank 0 on the\nmachine stack, then back to bank 7 and its stack.\nChanges: AF, BC, E.","comment":"Bank 0 and the machine stack"},
        "2017": {"comment":"HL printed (NUM_OUT_5)"},
        "2020": {"comment":"Back to bank 7"},
        "2022": {"synopsis":"Prints the text at HL, ended by a $00, through ROM 3's PRINT_A (the same job as\nERASE_TEXT_OUT).\nExit: HL at the $00.\nChanges: AF, HL.","comment":"The $00 at its end?"},
        "2025": {"comment":"ROM 3's PRINT_A"},
        "2028": {"comment":"The next"},
        "2031": {"synopsis":"Prints ENTER ($0D) through ROM 3's PRINT_A.\nChanges: AF.","comment":"ENTER"},
        "2033": {"comment":"ROM 3's PRINT_A"},
        "2037": {"synopsis":"Prints HL (0-65535) as five digits through ROM 3's DIGIT_OUT, a zero before the first digit\nprinted as E (a space blanks it); the units always (ROM 3's PRINT_A_DIGIT). Keeps HL.\nChanges: AF, BC, E.","comment":"HL kept"},
        "2038": {"comment":"Ten thousands"},
        "2041": {"comment":"ROM 3's DIGIT_OUT"},
        "2044": {"comment":"Thousands"},
        "2047": {"comment":"ROM 3's DIGIT_OUT"},
        "2050": {"comment":"On"},
        "2052": {"synopsis":"Prints HL (0-999) as three digits, as NUM_OUT_5 does. Keeps HL.\nChanges: AF, BC, E.","comment":"HL kept"},
        "2053": {"synopsis":"Hundreds, tens and units.","comment":"Hundreds"},
        "2056": {"comment":"ROM 3's DIGIT_OUT"},
        "2059": {"comment":"Tens (B stays $FF)"},
        "2061": {"comment":"ROM 3's DIGIT_OUT"},
        "2064": {"comment":"The units"},
        "2065": {"comment":"... always printed: ROM 3's PRINT_A_DIGIT"},
        "2068": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "2070": {"synopsis":"CAT's blank attribute field: a spare $00, then from $0817 four spaces and a $00, printed in\nplace of \" PRT\", \" SYS\" or \" ARC\"."},
        "2076": {"synopsis":"CAT's PROT field: a spare $00, then from $081D \" PRT\" and a $00."},
        "2082": {"synopsis":"CAT's \" SYS\", $00."},
        "2087": {"synopsis":"CAT's \" ARC\", $00."},
        "2092": {"synopsis":"Saves a block to tape: ROM 3's SA_BYTES entered at $04C6, past its own stacking of\nTAPE_RETURN; SA_TAPE_RETURN, stacked here first, runs ROM 3's TAPE_RETURN instead when the\nsave is over.\nEntry: A = the flag byte, IX = the start, DE = the length.\nExit: as TAPE_RETURN (carry: success).","comment":"SA_TAPE_RETURN"},
        "2095": {"comment":"... as the return"},
        "2096": {"comment":"ROM 3's SA_BYTES, from $04C6"},
        "2099": {"comment":"To SA_TAPE_RETURN"},
        "2100": {"synopsis":"ROM 3's TAPE_RETURN: the border back, interrupts on, SPACE held is report D; keeps AF.","comment":"ROM 3's TAPE_RETURN"},
        "2103": {"comment":"Back to SA_BYTES's caller"},
        "2104": {"synopsis":"Loads a block from the device in $5B5E: A = the flag byte, IX = the start, DE = the length,\ncarry set (load).\n1. Tape ('T'): ROM 3's LD_BYTES (LD_TAPE_POP).\n2. Disk: DE bytes of file 0, already open, read into bank 0 at IX (+3DOS FILE_READ), then\n   file 0 closed (CLOSE_FILE). Reading past the file's end is error $31 (End of file found);\n   other +3DOS errors are reported through $0E99.\nWith carry clear on disk it jumps to LD_DISK_DONE, whose pops take three words this path\nnever pushed; every caller sets carry for disk.\nExit: carry set. Keeps BC, DE, HL on disk.","comment":"The flag and carry kept"},
        "2105": {"comment":"The device"},
        "2108": {"comment":"Tape?"},
        "2110": {"comment":"Yes: ROM 3's LD_BYTES"},
        "2113": {"comment":"Disk: the flag and carry back"},
        "2114": {"comment":"No carry (verify): to LD_DISK_DONE"},
        "2116": {"comment":"HL, DE, BC kept"},
        "2119": {"comment":"File 0"},
        "2121": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "2123": {"comment":"HL = the start"},
        "2126": {"comment":"Bank 7 and its stack"},
        "2129": {"comment":"Onto +3DOS's stack"},
        "2132": {"comment":"+3DOS FILE_READ: DE bytes of file 0 to HL"},
        "2137": {"comment":"Back to this ROM's stack"},
        "2140": {"comment":"Bank 0 and the machine stack"},
        "2143": {"comment":"Read: close the file"},
        "2145": {"comment":"$19: the file's end?"},
        "2147": {"comment":"No: report the error"},
        "2149": {"comment":"Report: End of file found (error $31)"},
        "2153": {"synopsis":"File 0 closed (+3DOS CLOSE_FILE).","comment":"File 0"},
        "2155": {"comment":"Bank 7 and its stack"},
        "2158": {"comment":"Onto +3DOS's stack"},
        "2161": {"comment":"+3DOS CLOSE_FILE"},
        "2166": {"comment":"Back to this ROM's stack"},
        "2169": {"comment":"Bank 0 and the machine stack"},
        "2172": {"comment":"An error?"},
        "2174": {"synopsis":"Carry set: loaded; BC, DE, HL back.","comment":"Carry: success"},
        "2175": {"comment":"BC, DE, HL back"},
        "2179": {"synopsis":"Reports the +3DOS error in A ($0EB6).","comment":"Report the +3DOS error in A"},
        "2183": {"synopsis":"Tape: the flag and carry back, then LD_TAPE.","comment":"The flag and carry back"},
        "2184": {"synopsis":"ROM 3's LD_BYTES: A = the flag byte, IX = the start, DE = the length; carry to load, clear\nto verify.\nExit: carry set on success.","comment":"ROM 3's LD_BYTES"},
        "2187": {"comment":"Done"},
        "2188": {"synopsis":"SAVE, LOAD, VERIFY and MERGE (from the JP at $115A; T_ADDR's low byte - $9F tells which: 0\nSAVE, 1 LOAD, 2 VERIFY, 3 MERGE): the 48K ROM's TAPE_COMMAND with the +3's devices:\n1. The name (a string, CLASS_A through $1128); checking goes straight on to what follows\n   (SE_KIND).\n2. A 17-byte header in the workspace (34 for the others), IX at it: 11 spaces, $FF at IX + 1\n   (no name).\n3. LOAD \"*\" boots the disk in drive A (+3DOS BOOT_DISK; error $3B, Disk is not bootable).\n4. A name starting with T: or a letter A-P and ':' (either case) names the device; without\n   one SAVE uses the drive at $5B7A, the others the one at $5B79. The device letter goes to\n   $5B5E. The letter and ':' alone set that default instead (and, for a disk drive, +3DOS's\n   default through DRIVE_DEFAULT; with ASN after it the letter is also written into the\n   hard disk, SE_DEFAULT_ASN) and end the command.\n5. Disk: VERIFY does nothing; an empty name is report F; the name goes to $ED01 in bank 7,\n   ended by $FF, and its first 10 characters into the header. Tape: as the 48K ROM (SAVE\n   needs 1-10 characters, report F; the others cut a longer name to 10).\n6. DATA, SCREEN$, CODE, or a program with or without LINE fill in the header (SE_KIND on),\n   then SE_SAVE_OR_LOAD.","comment":"The top word dropped"},
        "2189": {"comment":"T_ADDR's low byte - $9F: which command"},
        "2194": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "2197": {"comment":"CLASS_A: the name, a string ($1128)"},
        "2200": {"comment":"Checking?"},
        "2204": {"comment":"Yes: on to what follows"},
        "2207": {"comment":"17 bytes"},
        "2210": {"comment":"SAVE?"},
        "2216": {"comment":"34 for the others"},
        "2218": {"synopsis":"The header's room (ROM 3's WORK_ROOM), IX at it; 11 spaces.","comment":"ROM 3's WORK_ROOM: DE = the room"},
        "2221": {"comment":"IX = it"},
        "2224": {"comment":"11 bytes"},
        "2226": {"comment":"Spaces"},
        "2228": {"synopsis":"One space.","comment":"One space"},
        "2232": {"comment":"No name yet: $FF"},
        "2236": {"comment":"ROM 3's STK_FETCH: DE = the name, BC = its length"},
        "2239": {"comment":"Both kept"},
        "2241": {"comment":"One character?"},
        "2246": {"comment":"'*'?"},
        "2251": {"comment":"LOAD \"*\": bank 7 and its stack"},
        "2254": {"comment":"Onto +3DOS's stack"},
        "2257": {"comment":"+3DOS BOOT_DISK: returns only on failure"},
        "2262": {"comment":"Back to this ROM's stack"},
        "2265": {"comment":"Bank 0 and the machine stack"},
        "2268": {"comment":"$23: not bootable?"},
