        "2306": {"comment":"SAVE's drive"},
        "2309": {"comment":"SAVE: that one"},
        "2311": {"comment":"The others' drive"},
        "2314": {"synopsis":"$5B5E = the device.","comment":"The device"},
        "2317": {"comment":"On"},
        "2319": {"synopsis":"A device in the name: $5B5E = its letter; the name only \"x:\" sets the default\n(SE_DOS_DEFAULT\non), a longer one goes on at SE_DEVICE_NAME.","comment":"$5B5E = the device"},
        "2322": {"comment":"Two characters?"},
        "2326": {"comment":"No: a name follows"},
        "2328": {"comment":"Only the device: A = its letter"},
        "2331": {"synopsis":"A disk drive (not T) becomes +3DOS's default too (DRIVE_DEFAULT); then SE_KEEP_DEFAULT.","comment":"Tape?"},
        "2335": {"comment":"Bank 7 and its stack"},
        "2338": {"comment":"Onto +3DOS's stack"},
        "2341": {"comment":"+3DOS DRIVE_DEFAULT"},
        "2346": {"comment":"Back to this ROM's stack"},
        "2349": {"comment":"Bank 0 and the machine stack"},
        "2352": {"comment":"Set?"},
        "2354": {"comment":"Report the +3DOS error in A"},
        "2358": {"synopsis":"The letter kept as the default: SAVE's ($5B7A) for SAVE, the others' ($5B79) otherwise.","comment":"SAVE?"},
        "2362": {"comment":"A = the letter"},
        "2365": {"comment":"SAVE: $5B7A"},
        "2367": {"comment":"The others' default"},
        "2370": {"comment":"On"},
        "2372": {"synopsis":"SAVE's default drive ($5B7A) set.","comment":"SAVE's default"},
        "2375": {"synopsis":"ASN after the drive: the letter also written into the hard disk, byte $10 of the bytes kept\nfor entry 0 of unit 0's partition table (ROM 2's PART_BYTE_SET, $00D6, with A = 0, BC = 0,\nL = $10, H = the letter). Without ASN nothing more.","comment":"D = the letter, E = byte $10"},
        "2378": {"comment":"ROM 3's GET_CHAR: ASN next?"},
        "2383": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "2384": {"comment":"H = the letter, L = $10"},
        "2385": {"comment":"Unit 0, entry 0"},
        "2388": {"comment":"Bank 7 and its stack"},
        "2391": {"comment":"Onto +3DOS's stack"},
        "2394": {"comment":"ROM 2's PART_BYTE_SET"},
        "2399": {"comment":"Back to this ROM's stack"},
        "2402": {"comment":"Bank 0 and the machine stack"},
        "2405": {"synopsis":"The length and name dropped: the command ends.","comment":"The length and name dropped"},
        "2408": {"synopsis":"A device and a name: a disk drive goes on at SE_DEVICE; for T: the \"T:\" is skipped and the\nname goes to SE_NAME_CHECK.","comment":"Tape?"},
        "2413": {"comment":"No: a disk name"},
        "2415": {"comment":"The length and name back"},
        "2417": {"comment":"Past \"T:\""},
        "2419": {"comment":"Two characters less"},
        "2421": {"comment":"To the length test"},
        "2423": {"synopsis":"Tape: the name as the 48K ROM takes it (SE_TAPE_NAME). Disk: VERIFY does nothing; MERGE and\nLOAD go on with SE_DISK_NAME.","comment":"Tape?"},
        "2427": {"comment":"VERIFY?"},
        "2434": {"comment":"VERIFY on disk: the length and name dropped, done"},
        "2437": {"synopsis":"Disk: an empty name is report F.","comment":"Empty?"},
        "2441": {"comment":"Report F: Invalid file name (error $0E)"},
        "2445": {"synopsis":"The whole name to $ED01 in bank 7, $FF after it; the header takes its first 10 characters.","comment":"To $ED01 in bank 7"},
        "2449": {"comment":"... copied ($3F63)"},
        "2452": {"comment":"The length dropped"},
        "2453": {"comment":"10 characters for the header"},
        "2456": {"comment":"Bank 7 and its stack"},
        "2459": {"comment":"$FF after the name"},
        "2462": {"comment":"Bank 0 and the machine stack"},
        "2465": {"comment":"On"},
        "2467": {"synopsis":"Tape: BC = the length.","comment":"The length"},
        "2468": {"synopsis":"DE = the name: 1-10 characters are copied as they are.","comment":"DE = the name"},
        "2469": {"comment":"HL = -10","synopsis":"The name's length checked: 1-10 characters are copied as they are."},
        "2472": {"comment":"Length - 1"},
        "2473": {"comment":"Carry when longer than 10, or empty"},
        "2475": {"comment":"Up to 10: copied as it is"},
        "2477": {"comment":"SAVE?"},
        "2481": {"comment":"No: on"},
        "2483": {"comment":"Report F: Invalid file name (error $0E)"},
        "2487": {"synopsis":"An empty name keeps the $FF; a longer one is cut to 10.","comment":"Empty?"},
        "2489": {"comment":"Then the $FF stays"},
        "2491": {"comment":"Cut to 10"},
        "2494": {"synopsis":"The name copied after the type byte.","comment":"HL = IX"},
        "2497": {"comment":"Past the type byte"},
        "2498": {"comment":"DE = there, HL = the name"},
        "2499": {"comment":"Copied"},
        "2501": {"synopsis":"What follows the name: DATA, SCREEN$, CODE, or else a program.","comment":"ROM 3's GET_CHAR: what follows the name"},
        "2502": {"comment":"DATA?"},
        "2506": {"comment":"MERGE?"},
        "2511": {"comment":"Then report C"},
        "2515": {"comment":"ROM 3's LOOK_VARS: the array"},
        "2518": {"comment":"C bit 7: an array"},
        "2520": {"comment":"Found"},
        "2522": {"comment":"Not found: HL = 0"},
        "2525": {"comment":"LOAD?"},
        "2529": {"comment":"Then a new array"},
        "2531": {"comment":"Report 2: Variable not found (error $01)"},
        "2535": {"synopsis":"The array must be followed by '(' (report C); its length into the header.","comment":"NZ: report C ($1124)"},
        "2538": {"comment":"Checking?"},
        "2542": {"comment":"Yes: no header"},
        "2544": {"comment":"The array's length"},
        "2546": {"comment":"... into the header"},
        "2550": {"comment":"Its high byte"},
        "2554": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "2555": {"synopsis":"The array's name byte at IX + 14.","comment":"The name byte at IX + 14"},
        "2558": {"comment":"Type 1"},
        "2560": {"comment":"A string array?"},
        "2564": {"comment":"Type 2"},
        "2565": {"synopsis":"Type 1 (numbers) or 2 (strings, C bit 6).","comment":"The type"},
        "2568": {"synopsis":"Past ')', the statement ends.","comment":"DE = the array's place"},
        "2570": {"comment":"')'?"},
        "2572": {"comment":"No: report C, at SE_DATA_FOUND"},
        "2574": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "2575": {"comment":"The statement must end ($10B0)"},
        "2578": {"comment":"HL = the array's place"},
        "2579": {"comment":"On"},
        "2582": {"synopsis":"SCREEN$: 6912 ($1AE4) bytes from $4000, type 3. Not for MERGE.","comment":"SCREEN$?"},
        "2586": {"comment":"MERGE?"},
        "2591": {"comment":"Then report C"},
        "2595": {"comment":"The statement must end"},
        "2598": {"comment":"Length $1AE4"},
        "2606": {"comment":"Start $4000"},
        "2615": {"comment":"Type 3"},
        "2617": {"synopsis":"CODE: start and length; SAVE needs both; for the others a missing one is 0, taken from the\nfile. Not for MERGE.","comment":"CODE?"},
        "2621": {"comment":"MERGE?"},
        "2626": {"comment":"Then report C"},
        "2630": {"comment":"The statement's end? ($0E93)"},
        "2633": {"comment":"No: a start"},
        "2635": {"comment":"SAVE?"},
        "2639": {"comment":"Needs a start: report C"},
        "2642": {"comment":"ROM 3's USE_ZERO: start 0"},
        "2645": {"comment":"And length 0"},
        "2647": {"synopsis":"The start (ROM 3's CLASS_6, through $113D).","comment":"CLASS_6: the start"},
        "2651": {"comment":"A ','?"},
        "2655": {"comment":"No: SAVE?"},
        "2659": {"comment":"Needs a length: report C"},
        "2662": {"synopsis":"No length: 0.","comment":"ROM 3's USE_ZERO: length 0"},
        "2665": {"comment":"On"},
        "2667": {"synopsis":"',' and the length.","comment":"Past the ','"},
        "2670": {"comment":"CLASS_6: the length"},
        "2673": {"synopsis":"The length and start into the header (ROM 3's TAKE_WORD twice); HL = the start.","comment":"The statement must end"},
        "2676": {"comment":"ROM 3's TAKE_WORD: BC = the length"},
        "2679": {"comment":"Into IX + 11"},
        "2685": {"comment":"ROM 3's TAKE_WORD: BC = the start"},
        "2688": {"comment":"Into IX + 13"},
        "2694": {"comment":"HL = the start"},
        "2696": {"synopsis":"Type 3, then SE_SAVE_OR_LOAD.","comment":"Type 3"},
        "2700": {"comment":"On"},
        "2702": {"synopsis":"A program: LINE (SAVE only) or nothing; without LINE the header's line is $80xx (no\nauto-run).","comment":"LINE?"},
        "2706": {"comment":"Not LINE: an ASN passed over, the end ($24C7)"},
        "2709": {"comment":"No auto-run","synopsis":"No LINE: the header's line high byte $80, no auto-run (from SE_SKIP_ASN)."},
        "2713": {"comment":"On"},
        "2715": {"synopsis":"LINE n: the auto-run line into the header (SAVE only, else report C).","comment":"SAVE?"},
        "2719": {"comment":"No: report C"},
        "2722": {"comment":"Past LINE"},
        "2725": {"comment":"CLASS_6: the line"},
        "2728": {"comment":"The statement must end"},
        "2731": {"comment":"ROM 3's TAKE_WORD: BC = the line"},
        "2734": {"comment":"Into IX + 13"},
        "2740": {"synopsis":"Type 0: the length (E_LINE - PROG - 1, the program and its variables) and the program's own\nlength (VARS - PROG) into the header; HL = PROG.","comment":"Type 0: a program"},
        "2744": {"comment":"HL = E_LINE"},
        "2747": {"comment":"DE = PROG"},
        "2751": {"comment":"One less"},
        "2752": {"comment":"The length"},
        "2754": {"comment":"Into IX + 11"},
        "2760": {"comment":"HL = VARS"},
        "2763": {"comment":"Less PROG: the program's own length"},
        "2765": {"comment":"Into IX + 15"},
        "2771": {"comment":"HL = PROG"},
        "2772": {"synopsis":"SAVE goes to $0D6D; the others go on with HL the destination kept, IX at the header's second\nhalf, and the device in $5B5E choosing tape or disk.","comment":"SAVE?"},
        "2776": {"comment":"Yes: $0D6D"},
        "2779": {"comment":"The destination kept"},
        "2780": {"comment":"IX to the second half, for the header read"},
        "2785": {"comment":"The device"},
        "2788": {"comment":"Tape ($5B5E = 'T')?"},
        "2790": {"comment":"No: a disk file"},
        "2792": {"synopsis":"Tape: reads headers (17 bytes, flag 0, ROM 3's LD_BYTES through $0899) into the second half\n(IX) until one of the wanted type and name arrives; each one's kind and name are printed on\nthe upper screen (SCR_CT = 3), the kinds from ROM 3's TAPE_MESSAGES at $09C0. Then\nLOAD_CONTROL with HL = the start stacked at $0ADB.","comment":"IX kept: the header's second half"},
        "2794": {"comment":"17 bytes, flag 0, loading (carry)"},
        "2799": {"comment":"ROM 3's LD_BYTES through $0899"},
        "2802": {"comment":"IX back"},
        "2804": {"comment":"Failed: the next header"},
        "2806": {"comment":"Stream -2, the upper screen"},
        "2808": {"comment":"ROM 3's STREAM_SELECT"},
        "2811": {"comment":"SCR_CT = 3: no scroll prompt for a while"},
        "2815": {"comment":"C = $80: another type"},
        "2817": {"comment":"The wanted type?"},
        "2825": {"comment":"C = $F6 (-10): the wanted type"},
        "2827": {"synopsis":"A type over 3 is skipped; otherwise its kind printed (ROM 3's PRINT_MESSAGE).","comment":"A type over 3 is skipped"},
        "2831": {"comment":"ROM 3's TAPE_MESSAGES from $09C0: the kinds"},
        "2834": {"comment":"BC kept"},
        "2835": {"comment":"ROM 3's PRINT_MESSAGE: \"Program: \", \"Bytes: \""},
        "2839": {"comment":"DE = the header (before its name)"},
        "2842": {"comment":"HL = the wanted name (IX - 16)"},
        "2846": {"comment":"10 characters"},
        "2848": {"comment":"A wanted name of $FF (any)?"},
        "2852": {"comment":"Counts as all 10 matches"},
        "2855": {"synopsis":"The name: each character printed; C counts the matches up to 0; a wanted name of $FF (any)\ncounts as all 10.","comment":"The header's next character"},
        "2857": {"comment":"The same as the wanted one?"},
        "2861": {"comment":"One more match"},
        "2862": {"synopsis":"Prints the character.","comment":"ROM 3's PRINT_A: the character shown"},
        "2865": {"comment":"Ten characters"},
        "2867": {"comment":"C not 0: type or name not the wanted ones"},
        "2871": {"comment":"ENTER after the name"},
        "2873": {"comment":"ROM 3's PRINT_A"},
        "2876": {"comment":"HL = the start (stacked at $0ADB)"},
        "2877": {"comment":"On with the header in place"},
        "2880": {"synopsis":"LOAD and MERGE from a disk: the file named at $ED01 (bank 7) opened as file 0 for reading\n(ROM 2's OPEN_BY_NAME; no file is +3DOS's error), its header's type checked against the\nwanted one (HEADER_BYTES; another type is error code $1D) and copied with the 6 bytes after\nit (length, start, second word) into the second half (IX, $3F8A). VERIFY opens nothing and\ngoes straight on to LOAD_CONTROL. Errors go through FILE_ERROR.","comment":"VERIFY (T_ADDR 2)?"},
        "2885": {"comment":"Yes: no file opened"},
        "2887": {"comment":"IX kept"},
        "2889": {"comment":"File 0, read mode"},
        "2893": {"comment":"D = 0: none is an error; E = 1: opened with its header"},
        "2897": {"comment":"HL = the name, at $ED01 in bank 7"},
        "2900": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "2903": {"comment":"Ready for +3DOS ($3213)"},
        "2906": {"comment":"ROM 2's OPEN_BY_NAME (DOS_JUMPS $0106)"},
        "2911": {"comment":"Back from +3DOS ($324B)"},
        "2914": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "2917": {"comment":"Opened?"},
        "2919": {"comment":"No: +3DOS's error reported (FILE_ERROR, code $FF)"},
        "2923": {"synopsis":"Opened: its header bytes.","comment":"File 0"},
        "2925": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "2928": {"comment":"Ready for +3DOS"},
        "2931": {"comment":"ROM 2's HEADER_BYTES: IX = its 8 header bytes"},
        "2936": {"comment":"Back from +3DOS"},
        "2939": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "2942": {"comment":"IX = the wanted header's second half again"},
        "2944": {"comment":"HL = the file's header bytes"},
        "2945": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "2948": {"comment":"The file's type"},
        "2949": {"comment":"Bank 0 (keeps A)"},
        "2952": {"comment":"The wanted type?"},
        "2957": {"comment":"No: error code $1D (FILE_ERROR)"},
        "2961": {"synopsis":"The wanted type: it and the 6 bytes after it into the second half.","comment":"The type into the second half"},
        "2964": {"comment":"DE = IX + 11: length, start, second word"},
        "2973": {"comment":"HL = the file's length, start and second word"},
        "2974": {"comment":"6 bytes"},
        "2977": {"comment":"Copied from bank 7 to bank 0 ($3F8A)"},
        "2980": {"comment":"HL = the start"},
        "2981": {"synopsis":"The header is in (tape or disk): CODE, and VERIFY of anything, go to LOAD_CODE_DATA; LOAD of\na program or an array to LOAD_PROG_ARRAY; MERGE to MERGE_LOAD.\nEntry: IX = the header found, IX - 17 = the wanted header, HL = the wanted start.","comment":"CODE (type 3)?"},
        "2988": {"comment":"T_ADDR - 1: 0 LOAD, 1 VERIFY, 2 MERGE"},
        "2992": {"comment":"LOAD: a program or an array"},
        "2995": {"comment":"MERGE?"},
        "3000": {"synopsis":"VERIFY, and LOAD of CODE: a wanted length (when not 0) shorter than the file's is error code\n$4F; a longer one is report R except for CODE; the start is the wanted one, or the header's\nwhen 0. Then LOAD_BLOCK, verifying for VERIFY from tape; a disk VERIFY returns without\nreading anything.","comment":"The start kept"},
        "3001": {"comment":"HL = the wanted length"},
        "3007": {"comment":"DE = the file's length"},
        "3013": {"comment":"A wanted length of 0?"},
        "3017": {"comment":"Shorter than the file's?"},
        "3019": {"comment":"Yes: error code $4F"},
        "3021": {"comment":"The same: fine"},
        "3023": {"comment":"Longer: only CODE may be"},
        "3028": {"comment":"Not CODE: report R"},
        "3030": {"synopsis":"HL: the wanted start, or the header's.","comment":"HL = the wanted start"},
        "3031": {"comment":"0?"},
        "3035": {"comment":"Then the header's start"},
        "3041": {"synopsis":"IX = the start; carry for load, clear for VERIFY.","comment":"IX = the start"},
        "3044": {"comment":"VERIFY?"},
        "3049": {"comment":"Carry: load"},
        "3050": {"comment":"Not VERIFY: load"},
        "3052": {"comment":"No carry: verify"},
        "3053": {"comment":"Tape?"},
        "3058": {"comment":"Yes: verified from tape"},
        "3060": {"comment":"A disk VERIFY reads nothing"},
        "3061": {"synopsis":"A = $FF: the data block's flag.","comment":"The data block's flag"},
        "3063": {"synopsis":"Loads (carry) or verifies DE bytes at IX through $0838 (the open file or the tape); failing\nis report R.","comment":"Loads or verifies DE bytes at IX ($0838)"},
        "3066": {"comment":"Done when it worked"},
        "3067": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $1A (report R, \"Tape loading error\") through FILE_ERROR, which closes\na disk file first.","comment":"Error code $1A (report R), through FILE_ERROR"},
        "3071": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $4F through FILE_ERROR: a wanted length shorter than the file's.","comment":"Error code $4F, through FILE_ERROR"},
        "3075": {"synopsis":"LOAD of a program or an array: room is checked for the new length (ROM 3's TEST_ROOM,\nagainst the old array's when there is one).","comment":"DE = the new length"},
        "3081": {"comment":"The old item's place kept (0 for none)"},
        "3082": {"comment":"Is there an old one?"},
        "3086": {"comment":"None: HL = the length + 3"},
        "3092": {"synopsis":"The old length: only a longer new one needs more room.","comment":"HL = the old length"},
        "3098": {"comment":"HL = new - old - 1"},
        "3102": {"comment":"Not longer: no room test"},
        "3104": {"synopsis":"TEST_ROOM for the difference + 5.","comment":"5 more"},
        "3108": {"comment":"ROM 3's TEST_ROOM (report 4)"},
        "3113": {"synopsis":"A program: LOAD_PROGRAM. An array: the old one removed (ROM 3's RECLAIM), and a new one made\nat the end of the variables (LOAD_NEW_ARRAY).","comment":"HL = the old item again"},
        "3114": {"comment":"A program (type 0)?"},
        "3120": {"comment":"An old array?"},
        "3124": {"comment":"BC = its length; HL = its name byte"},
        "3129": {"comment":"Plus 3 for the name and length"},
        "3132": {"comment":"IX kept in X_PTR"},
        "3136": {"comment":"ROM 3's RECLAIM: the old array removed"},
        "3139": {"comment":"IX back"},
        "3143": {"synopsis":"The new array's name, length and room (ROM 3's MAKE_ROOM); then LOAD_BLOCK into it.","comment":"HL = the end of the variables (E_LINE - 1)"},
        "3147": {"comment":"BC = the new length"},
        "3153": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "3154": {"comment":"Plus 3 for the name and length"},
        "3157": {"comment":"The name byte from the wanted header"},
        "3161": {"comment":"ROM 3's MAKE_ROOM"},
        "3164": {"comment":"The name byte"},
        "3167": {"comment":"The length"},
        "3173": {"comment":"IX = the array's data"},
        "3176": {"comment":"Load, flag $FF"},
        "3179": {"comment":"Into LOAD_BLOCK"},
        "3182": {"synopsis":"The program and variables replaced: the old ones removed (ROM 3's RECLAIM_DE_HL from PROG to\nE_LINE - 1), room made for the new length, VARS set from the header's program length; an\nauto-run line (below $4000) goes into NEWPPC, NSPPC = 0. Then LOAD_BLOCK.","comment":"DE = PROG"},
        "3183": {"comment":"HL = the end of the variables"},
        "3187": {"comment":"IX kept in X_PTR"},
        "3191": {"comment":"BC = the new length"},
        "3198": {"comment":"ROM 3's RECLAIM_DE_HL: old program and variables gone"},
        "3202": {"comment":"The place kept"},
        "3204": {"comment":"ROM 3's MAKE_ROOM for the new length"},
        "3207": {"comment":"IX back"},
        "3211": {"comment":"HL = PROG"},
        "3212": {"comment":"BC = the program's length, without variables"},
        "3218": {"comment":"VARS"},
        "3222": {"comment":"The auto-run line's high byte"},
        "3225": {"comment":"$4000 or more: none"},
        "3230": {"comment":"NEWPPC = the line"},
        "3236": {"comment":"NSPPC = 0: its first statement"},
        "3240": {"synopsis":"LOAD_BLOCK into the room.","comment":"DE = the length"},
        "3241": {"comment":"IX = PROG"},
        "3243": {"comment":"Load, flag $FF"},
        "3246": {"comment":"Into LOAD_BLOCK"},
        "3249": {"synopsis":"MERGE: the program is loaded into the workspace (ROM 3's WORK_ROOM, with an $80 after it),\nthen its lines (MERGE_LINES) and variables (MERGE_VARS) are put into place one by one, each\nreplacing one with the same number or name.","comment":"BC = the length"},
        "3256": {"comment":"One more for the $80"},
        "3257": {"comment":"ROM 3's WORK_ROOM"},
        "3260": {"comment":"The end marker"},
        "3262": {"comment":"HL = the room's start"},
        "3263": {"comment":"DE = the length"},
        "3264": {"comment":"The start, twice"},
        "3266": {"comment":"IX = the start"},
        "3268": {"comment":"Load, flag $FF"},
        "3271": {"comment":"The program into the workspace"},
        "3274": {"comment":"HL = the merged program"},
        "3275": {"comment":"DE = PROG"},
        "3279": {"synopsis":"The next merged line, until the variables start (bits 6-7).","comment":"The variables yet (bits 6-7)?"},
        "3284": {"synopsis":"Compares the merged line's number with the program's: a bigger one moves on through the\nprogram (ROM 3's NEXT_ITEM).","comment":"The line numbers' high bytes"},
        "3286": {"comment":"The same?"},
        "3290": {"comment":"The low bytes"},
        "3292": {"synopsis":"Both pointers back to the lines' starts.","comment":"Both back to the lines' starts"},
        "3294": {"comment":"The program's line not lower: put it in here"},
        "3297": {"comment":"ROM 3's NEXT_ITEM: the next program line"},
        "3302": {"comment":"Compared with it"},
        "3304": {"synopsis":"Puts the line in (MERGE_ENTER): Z replaces the one with the same number.","comment":"Z: replaces the line with the same number"},
        "3307": {"comment":"The next merged line"},
        "3309": {"synopsis":"The merged variables, one by one, until $80.","comment":"The variable's first byte"},
        "3311": {"comment":"The end of the merged variables?"},
        "3314": {"comment":"The merged variable kept"},
        "3315": {"comment":"HL = VARS"},
        "3318": {"synopsis":"Looks for a variable with the same first byte in the program's.","comment":"The program's variable"},
        "3319": {"comment":"The end?"},
        "3323": {"comment":"The same first byte?"},
        "3326": {"synopsis":"The next one (ROM 3's NEXT_ITEM)."},
        "3327": {"comment":"ROM 3's NEXT_ITEM: the next variable"},
        "3331": {"comment":"HL = it"},
        "3334": {"synopsis":"A long name ($A0 type): the letters must match too.","comment":"A long-named number ($A0)?"},
        "3338": {"comment":"No: the same"},
        "3340": {"comment":"DE = the merged variable"},
        "3342": {"comment":"The program's kept"},
        "3343": {"synopsis":"Letter by letter, to the one with bit 7.","comment":"The next letter"},
        "3346": {"comment":"The same?"},
        "3349": {"comment":"The last letter (bit 7)?"},
        "3352": {"comment":"All the same"},
        "3355": {"synopsis":"Not the same: on.","comment":"Different: on"},
        "3358": {"synopsis":"The same: A = $FF, so Z (replace).","comment":"A = $FF: Z after the INC (replace)"},
        "3360": {"synopsis":"Puts the variable in (MERGE_ENTER).","comment":"DE = the program's place, HL = the merged variable"},
        "3362": {"comment":"Z: replace"},
        "3363": {"comment":"Carry: a variable"},
        "3364": {"comment":"Put in"},
        "3367": {"comment":"The next merged variable"},
        "3369": {"synopsis":"Puts the item at HL (in the workspace) into the program before DE: with Z the item at DE is\nremoved first (replace). Room is made (ROM 3's MAKE_ROOM, PROG kept), the item copied from\nthe workspace, then removed from there (ROM 3's RECLAIM).\nEntry: carry for a variable, clear for a line.\nExit: DE = past the item put in.","comment":"Insert only?"},
        "3371": {"comment":"The flags kept"},
        "3372": {"comment":"X_PTR = the merged item"},
        "3376": {"comment":"ROM 3's NEXT_ITEM: the old item's end"},
        "3379": {"comment":"ROM 3's RECLAIM: the old item removed"},
        "3383": {"comment":"HL = the merged item"},
        "3386": {"comment":"The flags back"},
        "3387": {"synopsis":"Inserts: the item's length (ROM 3's NEXT_ITEM), the room.","comment":"The flags kept"},
        "3388": {"comment":"The place kept"},
        "3389": {"comment":"ROM 3's NEXT_ITEM: BC = the merged item's length"},
        "3392": {"comment":"X_PTR = the merged item"},
        "3395": {"comment":"PROG kept; HL = the place"},
        "3399": {"comment":"The length kept"},
        "3400": {"comment":"A variable?"},
        "3403": {"comment":"A line: room before the place"},
        "3404": {"comment":"ROM 3's MAKE_ROOM"},
        "3410": {"synopsis":"A variable: room at HL.","comment":"ROM 3's MAKE_ROOM at HL"},
        "3413": {"synopsis":"PROG back, the item copied and removed from the workspace.","comment":"HL = the room"},
        "3414": {"comment":"BC = the length"},
        "3415": {"comment":"PROG back as it was"},
        "3420": {"comment":"DE = the merged item (moved by MAKE_ROOM)"},
        "3426": {"comment":"HL = the item, DE = the room"},
        "3427": {"comment":"Copied into the program"},
        "3429": {"comment":"HL = the item"},
        "3431": {"comment":"DE kept"},
        "3432": {"comment":"ROM 3's RECLAIM: removed from the workspace"},
        "3437": {"synopsis":"SAVE once the header is made (from $0AD8): tape goes to SAVE_TAPE. A disk:\n1. The file named at $ED01 (bank 7) opened as file 0 for reading and writing (ROM 2's\n   OPEN_BY_NAME: created with a header; an old one of that name becomes .BAK).\n2. The type and the 6 bytes after it (length, start, second word) copied into its header\n   (HEADER_BYTES, $3F63).\n3. The DE bytes from the start written from bank 0 (FILE_WRITE; nothing for a length of 0),\n   and the file closed (CLOSE_FILE).\nAny +3DOS error is reported through FILE_ERROR.\nEntry: IX = the header, HL = the start.","comment":"Tape?"},
        "3442": {"comment":"Yes: SAVE_TAPE"},
        "3445": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "3448": {"comment":"The start kept"},
        "3449": {"comment":"File 0, read and write"},
        "3453": {"comment":"D = 1: created with a header; E = 3: an old one to .BAK"},
        "3457": {"comment":"HL = the name at $ED01"},
        "3460": {"comment":"IX kept"},
        "3462": {"comment":"Ready for +3DOS"},
        "3465": {"comment":"ROM 2's OPEN_BY_NAME (DOS_JUMPS $0106)"},
        "3470": {"comment":"Back from +3DOS"},
        "3473": {"comment":"Opened?"},
        "3475": {"comment":"No: bank 0 and +3DOS's error (code $FF)"},
        "3482": {"synopsis":"Opened: its header bytes.","comment":"File 0"},
        "3484": {"comment":"Ready for +3DOS"},
        "3487": {"comment":"ROM 2's HEADER_BYTES: IX = its 8 header bytes"},
        "3492": {"comment":"Back from +3DOS"},
        "3495": {"comment":"Got them?"},
        "3497": {"comment":"No: bank 0 and +3DOS's error (code $FF)"},
        "3504": {"synopsis":"The type, length, start and second word into the file's header; then the data.","comment":"IX = the header; HL = the file's header bytes"},
        "3507": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "3510": {"comment":"The type"},
        "3513": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "3516": {"comment":"Into the file's header"},
        "3518": {"comment":"DE = the file's bytes after it; HL = IX + 11"},
        "3526": {"comment":"6 bytes: length, start, second word"},
        "3529": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "3532": {"comment":"Copied from bank 0 to bank 7 ($3F63)"},
        "3535": {"comment":"File 0"},
        "3537": {"comment":"C = 0: the data in bank 0"},
        "3539": {"comment":"DE = the length"},
        "3545": {"comment":"Nothing to write?"},
        "3547": {"comment":"Bank 7 (keeps the flags)"},
        "3550": {"comment":"Yes: straight to closing"},
        "3552": {"comment":"HL = the start"},
        "3553": {"comment":"Ready for +3DOS"},
        "3556": {"comment":"ROM 2's FILE_WRITE (DOS_JUMPS $0115)"},
        "3561": {"comment":"Back from +3DOS"},
        "3564": {"comment":"Written?"},
        "3566": {"comment":"No: bank 0 and +3DOS's error (code $FF)"},
        "3573": {"synopsis":"The file closed.","comment":"File 0"},
        "3575": {"comment":"Ready for +3DOS"},
        "3578": {"comment":"ROM 2's CLOSE_FILE (DOS_JUMPS $0109)"},
        "3583": {"comment":"Back from +3DOS"},
        "3586": {"comment":"Closed?"},
        "3588": {"comment":"No: bank 0 and +3DOS's error (code $FF)"},
        "3595": {"synopsis":"Bank 0; done.","comment":"Bank 0"},
        "3599": {"synopsis":"SAVE to tape: \"Start tape, then press any key.\" in the lower screen (ROM 3's TAPE_MESSAGES),\na key (ROM 3's WAIT_KEY), the header (17 bytes, flag 0, through $082C), a gap of 50\ninterrupts, then the data (flag $FF).\nEntry: IX = the header; the start on the stack.","comment":"The start kept"},
        "3600": {"comment":"Stream -3, the lower screen"},
        "3602": {"comment":"ROM 3's STREAM_SELECT"},
        "3605": {"comment":"Message 0: \"Start tape, then press any key.\""},
        "3609": {"comment":"ROM 3's PRINT_MESSAGE from TAPE_MESSAGES ($09A1)"},
        "3612": {"comment":"TV_FLAG bit 5: the lower screen cleared at a key"},
        "3616": {"comment":"ROM 3's WAIT_KEY"},
        "3619": {"comment":"The header: 17 bytes from IX, flag 0"},
        "3625": {"comment":"Saved through $082C (ROM 3's SA_BYTES)"},
        "3630": {"comment":"50 interrupts: a second's gap"},
        "3632": {"synopsis":"The gap: 50 HALTs."},
        "3635": {"comment":"DE = the length"},
        "3641": {"comment":"Flag $FF: the data"},
        "3643": {"comment":"IX = the start"},
        "3645": {"comment":"Saved through $082C"},
        "3648": {"synopsis":"Printed by LOADER_DISK_END through PRINT_FF_TEXT, $FF-ended: AT 0,0, PAPER 0, INK 7, BRIGHT\n0, \"Insert tape and press PLAY\", ENTER, \"To cancel - press BREAK twice\"."},
        "3731": {"synopsis":"Z when A is ENTER or ':' (from $0A46).","comment":"ENTER?"},
        "3734": {"comment":"':'?"},
        "3737": {"synopsis":"Stops with a report after a file command failed; the byte after the CALL is the error code,\n$FF for +3DOS's error in A.\n1. Not on tape ($5B5E is not 'T'): file 0 closed in bank 7 (ROM 2's CLOSE_FILE), or\n   abandoned when that fails (CLOSE_NO_WRITE).\n2. The code: the byte after the CALL; for $FF, +3DOS's error 0-9 becomes code $3D-$46 and 10\n   up code A + $18.\n3. CALL $2AC8 and the code are built on the stack and run there, so $2AC8 reads the code as\n   the byte after its CALL and stops with that report.\nEntry: A = +3DOS's error (with code $FF).","comment":"+3DOS's error kept"},
        "3738": {"comment":"Tape?"},
        "3743": {"comment":"Yes: no file to close"},
        "3745": {"comment":"File 0"},
        "3747": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "3750": {"comment":"Ready for +3DOS"},
        "3753": {"comment":"ROM 2's CLOSE_FILE (DOS_JUMPS $0109)"},
        "3758": {"comment":"Back from +3DOS"},
        "3761": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "3764": {"comment":"Closed?"},
        "3766": {"comment":"No: abandoned instead"},
        "3774": {"comment":"ROM 2's CLOSE_NO_WRITE (DOS_JUMPS $010C)"},
        "3782": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "3785": {"synopsis":"The code: the byte after the CALL, or +3DOS's error turned into one.","comment":"A = +3DOS's error again"},
        "3786": {"comment":"HL = the code byte after the CALL","synopsis":"FILE_ERROR without closing file 0: A = the +3DOS error, the byte after the CALL the code\n($FF: A's, turned into one as FILE_ERROR_CODE does). Called by the hard disk commands at\n$3738, $3824, $38DE, $3940 and $3D8B."},
        "3787": {"comment":"E = the code"},
        "3788": {"comment":"Not $FF (bit 7 clear): taken as it is"},
        "3792": {"comment":"+3DOS error 0-9?"},
        "3796": {"comment":"Codes $3D-$46"},
        "3800": {"synopsis":"Error 10 up: + $18.","comment":"10 up: + $18"},
        "3802": {"synopsis":"E = the code.","comment":"E = the code"},
        "3803": {"synopsis":"CALL $2AC8 and the code byte built on the stack and run there.","comment":"CD 4C 2C E built on the stack: CALL $2AC8 and the code"},
        "3813": {"comment":"HL = the stack, where those bytes are"},
        "3817": {"comment":"Run there: $2AC8 stops with report E"},
        "3818": {"synopsis":"Syntax offsets: 50 bytes, one for each command keyword in token order, $CE (DEF FN) to $FF\n(COPY), each the distance from its own byte to the keyword's entry in SYNTAX_ENTRIES. Read\nby STMT_KEYWORD."},
        "3868": {"synopsis":"Each command's syntax entry, read item by item by SYNTAX_ITEM: a byte from $20 is a\ncharacter or token the line must have next; one below $20 is an operand class (CLASS_TABLE).\nClasses 0, 3 and 5 are followed by the address of the command's routine in ROM 3, classes\n$0C-$0E by one in this ROM; classes 2, 7 and $0B end the entry themselves. Entries share\nbytes: SAVE, LOAD, VERIFY and MERGE are each one $0B (CLASS_B tells them apart by T_ADDR),\nINK to OVER each one $07 (CLASS_7 likewise).\nIn this ROM: IF IF_CMD, GO SUB GO_SUB_CMD, GO TO GO_TO_ENTRY, RETURN RETURN_ENTRY, FOR\nFOR_CMD,\nNEXT NEXT_ENTRY, PRINT $217B, INPUT $218F, DIM DIM_ENTRY, REM REM_CMD, NEW NEW_ENTRY, RUN\nRUN_CMD, LIST LIST_CMD, CLEAR CLEAR_CMD, READ READ_CMD, DATA DATA_CMD, DRAW $2280, COPY\n$21AA,\nLPRINT $2177, LLIST LLIST_CMD, CIRCLE $2270, DEF FN DEF_FN_CMD, FORMAT $026C, MOVE\nMOVE_ENTRY\n(class $0A, then class $0E), ERASE $044A, CAT $05B8, OPEN # OPEN_STREAM_CMD, CLOSE #\nCLOSE_STREAM_CMD, SPECTRUM SPECTRUM_ENTRY ($0FB8), PLAY $23DB ($0FBB). In ROM 3: STOP, POKE,\nRANDOMIZE, CONTINUE, CLS, PLOT, PAUSE, RESTORE, BEEP, OUT, BORDER; LET is class 1, '=',\nclass\n2. The two bytes at $0FAF are not part of any entry."},
        "4030": {"synopsis":"Checks the edit line's syntax (from $252F, $2535): FLAGS bit 7 cleared (check, do not run),\nthe line number read (ROM 3's EDIT_LINE_NO), SUBPPC = 0, ERR_NR = $FF, then the statements\none by one (STMT_START). A syntax error raises its report.","comment":"FLAGS bit 7 cleared: checking"},
        "4034": {"comment":"ROM 3's EDIT_LINE_NO: the line's number"},
        "4037": {"comment":"SUBPPC = 0"},
        "4041": {"comment":"ERR_NR = $FF: no report"},
        "4047": {"synopsis":"The statement loop: past the ':' (or THEN) to the next statement.","comment":"Past the ':' or THEN"},
        "4048": {"synopsis":"One statement, checked or run (FLAGS bit 7):\n1. The workspace and calculator stack emptied (ROM 3's CLEAR_WS), SUBPPC + 1 (128 statements\n   is report C).\n2. ENTER ends the line (LINE_END); another ':' is an empty statement.\n3. STMT_RET stacked as the return; the keyword: $CE-$FF through SYNTAX_OFFSETS, $A3\n   (SPECTRUM) and $A4 (PLAY) their own entries; anything else is report C. Its entry is read\n   by SYNTAX_ITEM.","comment":"ROM 3's CLEAR_WS: workspace and calculator stack emptied"},
        "4051": {"comment":"SUBPPC + 1"},
        "4054": {"comment":"128 statements: report C"},
        "4057": {"comment":"The statement's first character"},
        "4058": {"comment":"B = 0 for the table offsets"},
        "4060": {"comment":"ENTER: the line ends"},
        "4065": {"comment":"An empty statement?"},
        "4069": {"comment":"STMT_RET: where the command returns to"},
        "4073": {"comment":"The keyword kept"},
        "4074": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "4076": {"comment":"A command keyword ($CE-$FF)?"},
        "4080": {"comment":"Back to the character"},
        "4082": {"comment":"SPECTRUM ($A3)?"},
        "4089": {"comment":"PLAY ($A4)?"},
        "4096": {"comment":"Anything else: report C"},
        "4099": {"synopsis":"A keyword from $CE: its entry from SYNTAX_OFFSETS.","comment":"C = its index"},
        "4100": {"comment":"Its offset in SYNTAX_OFFSETS"},
        "4104": {"comment":"HL = its entry"},
        "4108": {"synopsis":"SYNTAX_ITEM again from T_ADDR: the return address every item leaves.","comment":"HL = the entry's next item"},
        "4111": {"synopsis":"Reads the entry's next item at HL, T_ADDR following it: below $20 an operand class, its\nroutine from CLASS_TABLE entered with A = the line's current character, NZ, and SYNTAX_NEXT\nas its return; otherwise a character the line must have next (SYNTAX_CHAR).","comment":"The item"},
        "4113": {"comment":"T_ADDR past it"},
        "4116": {"comment":"SYNTAX_NEXT: where each item returns to"},
        "4120": {"comment":"The item kept"},
        "4121": {"comment":"A character to match ($20 up)?"},
        "4125": {"comment":"A class: its offset in CLASS_TABLE"},
        "4132": {"comment":"HL = the class's routine"},
        "4133": {"comment":"Jumped to through the RET"},
        "4134": {"comment":"A = the line's current character"},
        "4135": {"comment":"NZ (B was 0)"},
        "4137": {"synopsis":"The character or keyword (in C) must be the line's next, else report C; then past it.","comment":"The line's character"},
        "4138": {"comment":"The one wanted?"},
        "4142": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "4144": {"synopsis":"Where a command returns to: BREAK tested by $2AE7 (which raises report L itself, so the\nreport L at $1035 is never reached); then, with no jump (NSPPC bit 7 set), the next\nstatement (STMT_NEXT); otherwise the jump: to the edit line (NEWPPC's bit 15 set,\nRUN_EDIT_LINE) or a program line (LINE_NEW).","comment":"BREAK? ($2AE7 raises report L itself)"},
        "4147": {"comment":"Always carry back: the report below is never reached"},
        "4149": {"comment":"Error code $14 (report L), never reached"},
        "4153": {"synopsis":"A jump pending (NSPPC bit 7 clear)?","comment":"A jump pending (NSPPC bit 7 clear)?"},
        "4160": {"comment":"NEWPPC"},
        "4163": {"comment":"A program line (bit 15 clear)?"},
        "4167": {"synopsis":"Runs the edit line as a direct command (from $1380, $1436, $25C8): PPC = $FFFE, HL = WORKSP\n- 1 (so the line after it is none), DE = E_LINE - 1, from statement NSPPC (NEXT_LINE).","comment":"PPC = $FFFE: the edit line"},
        "4173": {"comment":"HL = the end of the edit line (WORKSP - 1)"},
        "4177": {"comment":"DE = E_LINE - 1"},
        "4182": {"comment":"From statement NSPPC"},
        "4187": {"synopsis":"Goes to line NEWPPC, statement NSPPC: the line found (ROM 3's FIND_LINE) when it is there; a\nmissing line asked for with a statement stops with report N; a missing line otherwise runs\nthe next one, and past the program ends with report 0.","comment":"ROM 3's FIND_LINE: line NEWPPC or the next"},
        "4190": {"comment":"A = the statement wanted"},
        "4193": {"comment":"Z: the line is there"},
        "4195": {"comment":"A statement of a missing line?"},
        "4199": {"comment":"Past the program (bits 6-7)?"},
        "4203": {"comment":"No: the next line"},
        "4205": {"comment":"Error code $FF (report 0): the program ends"},
        "4209": {"synopsis":"REM (class $0E): the return to SYNTAX_NEXT dropped and the rest of the line skipped\n(LINE_END).","comment":"The return to SYNTAX_NEXT dropped"},
        "4210": {"synopsis":"The end of a line: when checking, done. When running, the next line (NXTLIN), from its first\nstatement, unless it is past the program (bits 6-7 of its first byte), which returns, ending\nthe run.","comment":"Checking?"},
        "4215": {"comment":"HL = the next line"},
        "4218": {"comment":"Past the program?"},
        "4222": {"comment":"Statement 0"},
        "4223": {"synopsis":"Runs the line at HL from statement A (at least 1): PPC = its number, NXTLIN = the line after\nit.","comment":"At least 1"},
        "4227": {"comment":"The line's number, high byte first"},
        "4230": {"comment":"PPC"},
        "4234": {"comment":"DE = the line's length"},
        "4238": {"comment":"HL = the next line"},
        "4241": {"synopsis":"NXTLIN = HL, CH_ADD = DE (before the text), NSPPC = $FF; statement D: the first at once\n(STMT_LOOP), a later one found by ROM 3's FIND_STATEMENT, or report N when the line has\nfewer.","comment":"NXTLIN"},
        "4244": {"comment":"CH_ADD = before the text"},
        "4248": {"comment":"D = the statement"},
        "4251": {"comment":"NSPPC = $FF: no jump"},
        "4255": {"comment":"SUBPPC = the statement - 1"},
        "4259": {"comment":"The first: straight on"},
        "4263": {"comment":"ROM 3's FIND_STATEMENT"},
        "4266": {"comment":"Found?"},
        "4268": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $16 (report N, \"Statement lost\").","comment":"Error code $16 (report N)"},
        "4272": {"synopsis":"The end of a statement's operands. Running: returns, and the command's routine runs.\nChecking: the two returns are dropped and the statement must end here (STMT_NEXT).","comment":"Running?"},
        "4276": {"comment":"Running: back, and the command runs"},
        "4277": {"comment":"Checking: SYNTAX_NEXT's return and the command's dropped"},
        "4279": {"synopsis":"After a statement: ENTER ends the line (LINE_END), ':' starts the next (STMT_LOOP), anything\nelse is report C.","comment":"The statement's next character"},
        "4280": {"comment":"ENTER: the line ends"},
        "4284": {"comment":"':': the next statement"},
        "4289": {"comment":"Anything else: report C"},
        "4292": {"synopsis":"Operand classes: 15 bytes, one for each class 0-$0E, each the distance from its own byte to\nthe class's routine (CLASS_0 to CLASS_E). Read by SYNTAX_ITEM."},
        "4307": {"synopsis":"Class $0D, an optional number (RUN, CLEAR: ROM 3's FETCH_NUM), then as class $0C.","comment":"ROM 3's FETCH_NUM: a number, or none"},
        "4310": {"synopsis":"Class $0C: no more operands; Z set, then CLASS_E.","comment":"Z: the statement ends here"},
        "4311": {"synopsis":"Class $0E: the command's routine in this ROM, whose address follows at T_ADDR, runs now,\nwhen checking and when running; class $0C enters with Z, which ends the statement first\n(STATEMENT_END).","comment":"SYNTAX_NEXT's return dropped"},
        "4312": {"comment":"Z: the statement must end"},
        "4316": {"comment":"BC = the routine's address after the class"},
        "4323": {"comment":"Jumps to it"},
        "4325": {"synopsis":"Class 3, an optional number (RANDOMIZE, RESTORE): ROM 3's FETCH_NUM, then as class 0.","comment":"ROM 3's FETCH_NUM: a number, or none"},
        "4328": {"synopsis":"Class 0: no more operands; Z set, then CLASS_5.","comment":"Z: the statement ends here"},
        "4329": {"synopsis":"Class 5: the command's routine in ROM 3, whose address follows at T_ADDR, runs now (class 0\nends the statement first): under it $5B2A, $5B5A = CLASS_5_BACK, then SWAP_ROM_HIGH at $5B10\npages ROM 3 in and returns into the routine; its RET reaches $5B2A, which pages ROM 1 back\nand goes on at CLASS_5_BACK.","comment":"SYNTAX_NEXT's return dropped"},
        "4330": {"comment":"Z: the statement must end"},
        "4334": {"comment":"BC = the ROM 3 routine's address"},
        "4341": {"comment":"HL kept"},
        "4342": {"comment":"$5B5A = CLASS_5_BACK, where $5B2A goes on"},
        "4348": {"comment":"Under the routine: $5B2A, which pages ROM 1 back"},
        "4353": {"comment":"The routine's address on top"},
        "4356": {"comment":"AF and BC as SWAP_ROM_HIGH takes them"},
        "4359": {"comment":"SWAP_ROM_HIGH at $5B10: ROM 3 in, return into the routine"},
        "4362": {"synopsis":"Back from ROM 3: returns.","comment":"Back in ROM 1"},
        "4363": {"synopsis":"Class 1: ROM 3's CLASS_1 (a variable to assign to).","comment":"ROM 3's CLASS_1: the variable to assign to"},
        "4367": {"synopsis":"Class 2: the value assigned (ROM 3's VAL_FETCH) and the statement's end; the entry ends\nhere.","comment":"SYNTAX_NEXT's return dropped"},
        "4368": {"comment":"ROM 3's VAL_FETCH: the value assigned"},
        "4371": {"comment":"The statement must end"},
        "4375": {"synopsis":"Class 4: ROM 3's CLASS_4 (a FOR or NEXT variable).","comment":"ROM 3's CLASS_4: the FOR or NEXT variable"},
        "4379": {"comment":"Past the '#'","synopsis":"Past the current character (ROM 3's NEXT_SKIP), then two numbers (CLASS_8). Called at $354D\nfor GO TO #."},
        "4380": {"synopsis":"Class 8: ROM 3's CLASS_8 (two numbers separated by ',').","comment":"ROM 3's CLASS_8: two numbers"},
        "4384": {"synopsis":"Class 6: ROM 3's CLASS_6 (a number).","comment":"ROM 3's CLASS_6: a number"},
        "4388": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $0B (report C, \"Nonsense in BASIC\").","comment":"Error code $0B (report C)"},
        "4392": {"synopsis":"Class $0A: ROM 3's CLASS_A (a string). Also called from $0895.","comment":"ROM 3's CLASS_A: a string"},
        "4396": {"synopsis":"Class 7, INK to OVER as statements: when running, the temporary colours from the permanent\nones (ROM 3's COLOURS_TO_TEMP); the item set by ROM 3's COL_TEMP_ITEM, with A from T_ADDR's\nlow byte - $D2 (the keyword's token, as each entry is one byte); the statement's end; then\nthe permanent colours from the temporary ones: ATTR_P and MASK_P, and P_FLAG's permanent\nbits.","comment":"Running?"},
        "4400": {"comment":"TV_FLAG bit 0: the upper screen"},
        "4404": {"comment":"Checking: no colours copied"},
        "4406": {"comment":"ROM 3's COLOURS_TO_TEMP"},
        "4409": {"synopsis":"The item.","comment":"SYNTAX_NEXT's return dropped"},
        "4410": {"comment":"T_ADDR's low byte - $D2: the keyword's token"},
        "4415": {"comment":"ROM 3's COL_TEMP_ITEM"},
        "4418": {"comment":"The statement must end"},
        "4421": {"comment":"ATTR_T and MASK_T to ATTR_P and MASK_P"},
        "4427": {"comment":"P_FLAG"},
        "4430": {"comment":"The temporary bits to the permanent ones"},
        "4438": {"synopsis":"Class 9: ROM 3's CLASS_9 (PLOT, DRAW, CIRCLE).","comment":"ROM 3's CLASS_9: PLOT, DRAW, CIRCLE's numbers"},
        "4442": {"synopsis":"Class $0B, the tape and disk commands SAVE, LOAD, VERIFY and MERGE: on at $088C.","comment":"$088C: SAVE, LOAD, VERIFY, MERGE"},
        "4445": {"synopsis":"IF (class $0E): when running, the condition taken off the calculator stack: false (0, ROM\n3's IS_ZERO) skips the rest of the line (LINE_END); true runs it, THEN acting as ':'\n(STMT_START).","comment":"SYNTAX_NEXT's return dropped"},
        "4446": {"comment":"Running?"},
        "4452": {"comment":"STKEND - 5: the condition taken off"},
        "4462": {"comment":"ROM 3's IS_ZERO: false?"},
        "4465": {"comment":"False: the rest of the line skipped"},
        "4468": {"synopsis":"True, or checking: the rest of the line as statements.","comment":"True or checking: THEN acts as ':'"},
        "4471": {"synopsis":"FOR (class $0E, after the variable, '=', the value, TO and the limit): STEP and its number\n(CLASS_6), or 1 stacked when there is none; the statement's end; then ROM 3's FOR_VALUES\ndoes the rest.","comment":"STEP?"},
        "4475": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "4476": {"comment":"Its number"},
        "4479": {"comment":"The statement must end"},
        "4484": {"synopsis":"No STEP: the statement's end, and 1 as a small integer onto the calculator stack (STKEND\nmoved).","comment":"The statement must end"},
        "4487": {"comment":"No STEP: 1 as a small integer onto the calculator stack"},
        "4505": {"comment":"STKEND past it"},
        "4508": {"synopsis":"ROM 3's FOR_VALUES.","comment":"ROM 3's FOR_VALUES"},
        "4512": {"synopsis":"Past the ',' to the next variable.","comment":"Past the ','"},
        "4513": {"synopsis":"READ (class $0E): for each variable (CLASS_1), when running, the next DATA item: after a ','\nat DATADD, or the first of the next DATA statement (ROM 3's LOOK_PROG for $E4); none is\nreport E. It is evaluated with the variable's type (ROM 3's VAL_FETCH), DATADD moves past\nit, and CH_ADD comes back to the READ statement (kept in X_PTR).","comment":"The variable"},
        "4516": {"comment":"Running?"},
        "4522": {"comment":"CH_ADD kept in X_PTR"},
        "4526": {"comment":"HL = DATADD"},
        "4529": {"comment":"After a ',' there?"},
        "4534": {"comment":"No: the next DATA statement"},
        "4536": {"comment":"ROM 3's LOOK_PROG"},
        "4539": {"comment":"Found?"},
        "4541": {"comment":"Error code $0D (report E)"},
        "4545": {"synopsis":"The item at HL: CH_ADD there, evaluated and assigned (ROM 3's VAL_FETCH); DATADD = past it;\nCH_ADD back from X_PTR.","comment":"Past the ',' or DATA"},
        "4550": {"comment":"ROM 3's VAL_FETCH: the item assigned"},
        "4553": {"comment":"DATADD past it"},
        "4557": {"comment":"CH_ADD back from X_PTR"},
        "4560": {"comment":"X_PTR's high byte 0"},
        "4568": {"synopsis":"A ',' and another variable, or the statement's end.","comment":"Another ','?"},
        "4573": {"comment":"The statement must end"},
        "4577": {"synopsis":"DATA (class $0E): checking, each item is an expression (ROM 3's SCAN_EXPR) up to the end of\nthe statement; running, the statement is skipped (DATA_RUN).","comment":"Running?"},
        "4583": {"synopsis":"One item, then ',' and the next.","comment":"ROM 3's SCAN_EXPR: an item"},
        "4586": {"comment":"A ','? If not, the statement must end"},
        "4591": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "4594": {"synopsis":"Running: A = DATA's token, then DATA_SKIP_A.","comment":"DATA's token"},
        "4596": {"synopsis":"ROM 3's DATA_SKIP: the statement whose keyword is A skipped (DEF FN comes here too).","comment":"ROM 3's DATA_SKIP: the statement skipped"},
        "4600": {"synopsis":"RUN (class $0D): GO TO line n (ROM 3's GO_TO_CMD), RESTORE to the first line (ROM 3's\nRESTORE_BC with BC = 0), then CLEAR_RUN with 0.","comment":"ROM 3's GO_TO_CMD: line n"},
        "4603": {"comment":"Line 0 for RESTORE"},
        "4606": {"comment":"ROM 3's RESTORE_BC: from the start"},
        "4609": {"comment":"CLEAR with 0"},
        "4611": {"synopsis":"CLEAR (class $0D): CLEAR_RUN with BC = n (ROM 3's TAKE_WORD).","comment":"ROM 3's TAKE_WORD: BC = n"},
        "4614": {"synopsis":"The variables removed (ROM 3's RECLAIM_DE_HL from VARS to E_LINE - 1), the screen cleared\n(ROM 3's CLS_CMD); the new RAMTOP (BC, or the old one for 0) must be above STKEND + 50 and\nnot above P_RAMT, else report M; then the machine stack starts again under it, with the GO\nSUB end marker and the error address, ERR_SP pointing at it.","comment":"0?"},
        "4618": {"comment":"Then RAMTOP as it is"},
        "4622": {"synopsis":"The new RAMTOP kept; the variables and screen cleared; the limits tested.","comment":"The new RAMTOP kept"},
        "4623": {"comment":"From VARS"},
        "4627": {"comment":"To E_LINE - 1"},
        "4631": {"comment":"ROM 3's RECLAIM_DE_HL: the variables removed"},
        "4634": {"comment":"ROM 3's CLS_CMD"},
        "4637": {"comment":"STKEND + 50"},
        "4644": {"comment":"DE = the new RAMTOP"},
        "4645": {"comment":"Not above it?"},
        "4649": {"comment":"P_RAMT"},
        "4653": {"comment":"Not above it?"},
        "4657": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $15 (report M, \"RAMTOP no good\").","comment":"Error code $15 (report M)"},
        "4661": {"synopsis":"RAMTOP = DE; the return, the error address and the marker taken off the stack, then put back\nunder the new RAMTOP, ERR_SP following.","comment":"RAMTOP"},
        "4665": {"comment":"The return"},
        "4666": {"comment":"The error address"},
        "4667": {"comment":"The marker"},
        "4668": {"comment":"The stack from the new RAMTOP"},
        "4675": {"comment":"ERR_SP at the error address"},
        "4681": {"synopsis":"GO SUB (class $0C): the place to return to kept below the ERR_SP slot (the next statement,\nSUBPPC + 1, one byte, and the line, PPC), the error address back on top and ERR_SP at it;\nthen GO TO (ROM 3's GO_TO_CMD), and room for 20 more bytes must be left (ROM 3's TEST_ROOM,\nreport 4).","comment":"The return"},
        "4682": {"comment":"SUBPPC + 1: the statement after"},
        "4686": {"comment":"Under the error address; one byte only"},
        "4688": {"comment":"PPC"},
        "4693": {"comment":"The error address back"},
        "4694": {"comment":"ERR_SP"},
        "4699": {"comment":"ROM 3's GO_TO_CMD"},
        "4702": {"comment":"20 bytes"},
        "4705": {"comment":"ROM 3's TEST_ROOM (report 4)"},
        "4709": {"synopsis":"RETURN (from RETURN_ENTRY, after the statement's end): the statement and line GO SUB kept\ntaken from below the ERR_SP slot, the error address and ERR_SP moved up, NEWPPC and NSPPC\nset for the jump. The end marker ($3E) instead is report 7.","comment":"The return"},
        "4710": {"comment":"The error address"},
        "4711": {"comment":"The line; D = the statement"},
        "4713": {"comment":"The end marker ($3E): no GO SUB?"},
        "4717": {"comment":"Back to the statement byte"},
        "4720": {"comment":"ERR_SP"},
        "4725": {"comment":"NEWPPC"},
        "4728": {"comment":"NSPPC"},
        "4732": {"synopsis":"No GO SUB: the stack as it was, error code 6 (report 7, \"RETURN without GOSUB\").","comment":"The stack as it was"},
        "4734": {"comment":"Error code 6 (report 7)"},
        "4738": {"synopsis":"DEF FN (class $0E): running, the statement is skipped (DATA_SKIP_A with DEF FN's token).\nChecking: a letter (and '$'), '(', the parameters (each a letter, maybe with '$'), ')', '='\nand an expression of the name's type (report C otherwise). After each parameter 6 bytes are\nmade (ROM 3's MAKE_ROOM) with the marker $0E first, room for its value.","comment":"Running?"},
        "4742": {"comment":"No: checking"},
        "4744": {"comment":"DEF FN's token"},
        "4746": {"comment":"Skipped as DATA is"},
        "4749": {"synopsis":"Checking: the name, a letter (ROM 3's ALPHA) and maybe '$'.","comment":"A number function so far"},
        "4753": {"comment":"ROM 3's ALPHA: a letter?"},
        "4759": {"comment":"'$'?"},
        "4763": {"comment":"A string function"},
        "4768": {"synopsis":"'(' must follow; ')' at once means no parameters.","comment":"'('?"},
        "4772": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "4773": {"comment":"')' at once: no parameters"},
        "4777": {"synopsis":"A parameter: a letter, maybe '$'.","comment":"ROM 3's ALPHA: a letter?"},
        "4780": {"synopsis":"Not a letter: report C.","comment":"No: report C"},
        "4784": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "4785": {"comment":"'$'?"},
        "4791": {"synopsis":"The 6 bytes: room made (ROM 3's MAKE_ROOM), $0E first; then ',' and the next parameter.","comment":"HL = past the parameter"},
        "4792": {"comment":"6 bytes"},
        "4795": {"comment":"ROM 3's MAKE_ROOM"},
        "4800": {"comment":"The marker $0E"},
        "4802": {"comment":"','?"},
        "4809": {"synopsis":"')', '=' and the expression, of the name's type.","comment":"')'?"},
        "4814": {"comment":"'='?"},
        "4819": {"comment":"FLAGS kept: the name's type"},
        "4823": {"comment":"ROM 3's SCAN_EXPR"},
        "4826": {"comment":"The expression's type the same?"},
        "4832": {"synopsis":"Report C when the syntax is wrong; otherwise the statement's end.","comment":"No: report C"},
        "4835": {"comment":"The statement must end"},
        "4840": {"synopsis":"The menu's Loader (ROM 0 calls it through $3E80): $EC0E = $FF; then\n1. With a disk drive ($5B66 bit 4): no disk error routine (ROM 2's SET_ERR_HOOK with A = 0,\n   the old one kept), the disk booted (BOOT_DISK); then LOAD \"disk\" (LOAD_DISK_LINE) put\n   into the edit line and run as a command (RUN_EDIT_LINE), coming back at LOADER_DISK_END.\n2. Without one, or when LOAD \"disk\" itself stops with a report: LOAD \"\" (LOAD_LINE) run the\n   same way, coming back at LOADER_TAPE_END.\nThe run: the lower screen cleared as needed (ROM 3's CLS_LOWER, ROM 0's CLEAR_LOW_3),\nTV_FLAG bit 3 cleared, SCR_CT, FLAGS bit 7 (running), NSPPC = 1, $3E00 and ERROR_TO_ROM1\n($5B3A) on the stack with ERR_SP at it, and $5B6C the place to come back to.","comment":"Bank 7"},
        "4843": {"comment":"$EC0E = $FF"},
        "4853": {"comment":"No: the tape"},
        "4856": {"comment":"A = 0: no error routine"},
        "4857": {"comment":"Ready for +3DOS"},
        "4860": {"comment":"ROM 2's SET_ERR_HOOK (DOS_JUMPS $014E)"},
        "4865": {"comment":"Back from +3DOS"},
        "4868": {"comment":"The old routine kept"},
        "4869": {"comment":"Ready for +3DOS"},
        "4872": {"comment":"ROM 2's BOOT_DISK (DOS_JUMPS $012A)"},
        "4877": {"comment":"Back from +3DOS"},
        "4880": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "4883": {"comment":"ROM 3's CLEAR_EDIT_WS"},
        "4886": {"comment":"7 bytes at E_LINE"},
        "4892": {"comment":"ROM 3's MAKE_ROOM"},
        "4895": {"comment":"LOAD \"disk\" into them"},
        "4907": {"comment":"CH_ADD = E_LINE"},
        "4913": {"comment":"$22B1: the screen cleared when FLAGS2 bit 0 asks"},
        "4916": {"comment":"TV_FLAG bit 6 set?"},
        "4922": {"comment":"No: ROM 3's CLS_LOWER"},
        "4925": {"synopsis":"TV_FLAG bit 6 cleared; lines 21-23 cleared when $EC0D bit 6 is clear and $EC0E is 0.","comment":"TV_FLAG bit 6 cleared"},
        "4929": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "4932": {"comment":"$EC0D bit 6 set?"},
        "4939": {"comment":"$EC0E 0?"},
        "4945": {"comment":"ROM 0's CLEAR_LOW_3: lines 21-23 cleared"},
        "4950": {"synopsis":"Bank 0; the run set up.","comment":"Bank 0"},
        "4953": {"comment":"TV_FLAG bit 3 cleared"},
        "4958": {"comment":"SCR_CT = 25 - the line in S_POSN"},
        "4966": {"comment":"FLAGS bit 7: running"},
        "4970": {"comment":"NSPPC = 1"},
        "4974": {"comment":"$3E00, then ERROR_TO_ROM1 ($5B3A), on the stack"},
        "4982": {"comment":"ERR_SP at it"},
        "4986": {"comment":"$5B6C = $1383: where the run comes back"},
        "4992": {"comment":"Runs the line"},
        "4995": {"synopsis":"Where LOAD \"disk\" comes back to: the old disk error routine back (SET_ERR_HOOK with A =\n$FF). No report, or one from a program line: the run's end ($25CB). A report from LOAD\n\"disk\" itself: 'T' the default LOAD drive ($5B79), INSERT_TAPE_MSG in the lower screen, then\nLOADER_TAPE.","comment":"Bank 7"},
        "4998": {"comment":"The old error routine"},
        "4999": {"comment":"A = $FF: put back"},
        "5001": {"comment":"Ready for +3DOS"},
        "5004": {"comment":"ROM 2's SET_ERR_HOOK (DOS_JUMPS $014E)"},
        "5009": {"comment":"Back from +3DOS"},
        "5012": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "5015": {"comment":"A report?"},
        "5020": {"comment":"No: the run's end ($25CB)"},
        "5023": {"comment":"The report from the edit line (PPC $FFFE)?"},
        "5034": {"comment":"No: the run's end"},
        "5037": {"comment":"The default LOAD drive 'T'"},
        "5042": {"comment":"TV_FLAG bit 0: the lower screen"},
        "5047": {"comment":"\"Insert tape and press PLAY\""},
        "5053": {"comment":"TV_FLAG bit 0 cleared, bit 6 set"},
        "5060": {"comment":"Then LOAD \"\""},
        "5062": {"synopsis":"No disk drive: bank 0.","comment":"Bank 0"},
        "5065": {"synopsis":"LOAD \"\" (LOAD_LINE) into the edit line and run, coming back at LOADER_TAPE_END.","comment":"ROM 3's CLEAR_EDIT_WS"},
        "5068": {"comment":"3 bytes at E_LINE"},
        "5074": {"comment":"ROM 3's MAKE_ROOM"},
        "5077": {"comment":"LOAD \"\" into them"},
        "5089": {"comment":"CH_ADD = E_LINE"},
        "5095": {"comment":"$22B1: the screen cleared when FLAGS2 bit 0 asks"},
        "5098": {"comment":"TV_FLAG bit 6 set?"},
        "5104": {"comment":"No: ROM 3's CLS_LOWER"},
        "5107": {"synopsis":"TV_FLAG bit 6 cleared; lines 21-23 cleared when $EC0D bit 6 is clear and $EC0E is 0.","comment":"TV_FLAG bit 6 cleared"},
        "5111": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "5114": {"comment":"$EC0D bit 6 set?"},
        "5121": {"comment":"$EC0E 0?"},
        "5127": {"comment":"ROM 0's CLEAR_LOW_3: lines 21-23 cleared"},
        "5132": {"synopsis":"Bank 0; the run set up.","comment":"Bank 0"},
        "5135": {"comment":"TV_FLAG bit 3 cleared"},
        "5140": {"comment":"SCR_CT = 25 - the line in S_POSN"},
        "5148": {"comment":"FLAGS bit 7: running"},
        "5152": {"comment":"NSPPC = 1"},
        "5156": {"comment":"$3E00, then ERROR_TO_ROM1 ($5B3A), on the stack"},
        "5164": {"comment":"ERR_SP at it"},
        "5168": {"comment":"$5B6C = $1439: where the run comes back"},
        "5174": {"comment":"Runs the line"},
        "5177": {"synopsis":"Where LOAD \"\" comes back to: after a report, with a disk drive, 'A' is the default LOAD\ndrive again ($5B79); then the run's end ($25CB).","comment":"A report?"},
        "5182": {"comment":"No: the run's end ($25CB)"},
        "5185": {"comment":"A disk drive?"},
        "5190": {"comment":"No: the run's end"},
        "5193": {"comment":"The default LOAD drive back to 'A'"},
        "5201": {"synopsis":"Runs LLIST as a command (ROM 0's print menu item calls it through $3E80): the edit line\nemptied (ROM 3's CLEAR_EDIT_WS), LLIST's token ($E1) put into it, then entered (checked and\nrun) at $24F0.","comment":"ROM 3's CLEAR_EDIT_WS"},
        "5204": {"comment":"1 byte at E_LINE"},
        "5210": {"comment":"ROM 3's MAKE_ROOM"},
        "5213": {"comment":"LLIST's token"},
        "5218": {"comment":"Entered: checked and run ($24F0)"},
        "5221": {"synopsis":"SPECTRUM (class $0C): to 48 BASIC for good: channel P takes channel S's routines\n(CHANS_P_FROM_S), FLAGS bit 4 cleared; the stack from ERR_SP with ROM 3's REPORT ($1303)\nunder $0013 and $0008; the paging copy $5B5C = $20; then SWAP_ROM_HIGH pages ROM 3 in and\nreturns to its RST $08 (ERROR_1) with $0013's byte $FF as the code: report 0, and ROM 3's\nREPORT goes on in 48 BASIC.","comment":"Channel P's routines from channel S's"},
        "5224": {"comment":"The stack from ERR_SP"},
        "5228": {"comment":"The error address dropped"},
        "5229": {"comment":"ROM 3's REPORT, under the two below"},
        "5233": {"comment":"$0013 in ROM 3, whose byte $FF is the code: 0 OK"},
        "5237": {"comment":"ROM 3's ERROR_1 ($0008): where the swap returns"},
        "5241": {"comment":"The paging copy $5B5C = $20 (paging locked)"},
        "5246": {"comment":"AF and BC as SWAP_ROM_HIGH takes them"},
        "5248": {"comment":"No interrupts while paging"},
        "5249": {"comment":"FLAGS bit 4 cleared: 48 BASIC"},
        "5253": {"comment":"SWAP_ROM_HIGH at $5B10: ROM 3 in"},
        "5256": {"synopsis":"The menu's 48 BASIC (ROM 0 calls it through $3E80): GO_48_CODE copied to $6000 and its\naddress stacked, the disk motor off ($5B67 bit 3, port $1FFD), FLAGS bit 4 cleared, the\npaging copy $30; then SWAP_ROM_HIGH pages ROM 3 in and returns to $6000, which locks the\npaging (port $7FFD = $30) and jumps to ROM 3's $0000: the 48K ROM starts from the beginning.","comment":"$6000: where SWAP_ROM_HIGH returns"},
        "5260": {"comment":"GO_48_CODE copied to $6000"},
        "5271": {"comment":"Disk motor off ($5B67 bit 3, port $1FFD)"},
        "5286": {"comment":"The paging byte $30: ROM bit set, paging locked"},
        "5289": {"comment":"FLAGS bit 4 cleared: 48 BASIC"},
        "5293": {"comment":"The paging copy"},
        "5296": {"comment":"AF and BC as SWAP_ROM_HIGH takes them"},
        "5298": {"comment":"SWAP_ROM_HIGH: ROM 3 in, on at $6000"},
        "5301": {"synopsis":"Copied to $6000 by GO_48_BASIC and run there (15 bytes, with the three letters after it):\nport $7FFD = $30 (bank 0, ROM bit set, paging locked), then $0000 in ROM 3.","comment":"Run at $6000: bank 0, ROM 3, paging locked"},
        "5306": {"comment":"No interrupts while paging"},
        "5310": {"comment":"ROM 3's start ($0000)"},
        "5313": {"synopsis":"Three letters, \"CJL\", copied to $6000 with GO_48_CODE but never run."},
        "5316": {"synopsis":"Copies channel S's output and input addresses (CHANS + 5) over channel P's (CHANS + 15);\nFLAGS2 bit 3 and FLAGS bit 4 cleared.","comment":"CHANS + 5: channel S's output and input"},
        "5323": {"comment":"CHANS + 15: channel P's"},
        "5329": {"comment":"4 bytes"},
        "5334": {"comment":"FLAGS2 bit 3 cleared"},
        "5338": {"comment":"FLAGS bit 4 cleared"},
        "5343": {"synopsis":"LOAD \"\" as tokens ($EF, '\"', '\"'), copied into the edit line by LOADER_TAPE."},
        "5346": {"synopsis":"DIM (class $0E): DIM #s,v sets the numeric variable v to the 32-bit value the channel of\nstream s gives for function 4 with B = 2 (STREAM_VALUE); without '#' the ordinary DIM at\n$2297.","comment":"ROM 3's GET_CHAR: '#'?"},
        "5349": {"comment":"No: the ordinary DIM"},
        "5352": {"comment":"The stream and the variable"},
        "5355": {"comment":"B = 2"},
        "5357": {"comment":"The value assigned"},
        "5360": {"synopsis":"Copies BC bytes from DE onto the machine stack (SP lowered by BC) and runs them there with\nROM 3 paged in: RST $28 to ROM 3's $250E, a JP (HL) with HL at the copy, so an RST $28 in\nthe copy reaches ROM 3's calculator. Then the bytes are dropped. Used for the calculator\ncode at $2B44 and $3DB3.\nEntry: DE = the code, BC = its length.","comment":"HL = -BC"},
        "5366": {"comment":"HL = SP - BC: the room"},
        "5368": {"comment":"SP lowered"},
        "5369": {"comment":"The length and the start kept"},
        "5371": {"comment":"DE = the room, HL = the code"},
        "5372": {"comment":"Copied"},
        "5374": {"comment":"HL = the copy"},
        "5375": {"comment":"Run there (ROM 3's JP (HL) at $250E)"},
        "5378": {"comment":"HL = the length"},
        "5380": {"comment":"SP raised past the copy"},
        "5382": {"synopsis":"NEXT (class $0E): NEXT #s,v sets the numeric variable v to the byte the channel of stream s\ngives for function 2 (ROM 2's ROM0_392D_2, $005C); without '#' a FOR variable (ROM 3's\nCLASS_4), the statement's end and ROM 3's NEXT at $1DAB.","comment":"ROM 3's GET_CHAR: '#'?"},
        "5385": {"comment":"Yes: NEXT_STREAM"},
        "5387": {"comment":"ROM 3's CLASS_4: the variable"},
        "5390": {"comment":"The statement's end"},
        "5393": {"comment":"ROM 3's NEXT"},
        "5397": {"synopsis":"NEXT #s,v: the stream and the variable (STREAM_AND_VAR), the channel's byte from ROM 2's\nROM0_392D_2 ($005C) stacked (ROM 3's STACK_A) and assigned (ROM 3's LET at $2AFF).","comment":"The stream and the variable"},
        "5400": {"comment":"ROM 2's ROM0_392D_2: A = the byte"},
        "5405": {"comment":"ROM 3's STACK_A"},
        "5408": {"comment":"Assigned (ROM 3's LET)"},
        "5412": {"synopsis":"Prints the text at HL through ROM 3's PRINT_A, up to the $FF that ends it.","comment":"The end ($FF)?"},
        "5416": {"comment":"ROM 3's PRINT_A"},
        "5419": {"comment":"The next"},
        "5422": {"synopsis":"LOAD \"disk\" as tokens ($EF, then '\"disk\"'), copied into the edit line by LOADER_RUN."},
        "5429": {"synopsis":"LLIST (class $0E): LIST to stream 3 (the printer).","comment":"Stream 3"},
        "5433": {"synopsis":"LIST (class $0E): stream 2 (or LLIST's 3), TV_FLAG = 0; when running, that stream (ROM 3's\nSTREAM_SELECT); a '#' stream instead (ROM 3's STREAM_ALTER), then ';' or ',' and the line\nnumber, or none; or the line number alone; the statement's end; then ROM 3's LIST_CMD from\n$1825 lists.","comment":"Stream 2"},
        "5435": {"synopsis":"The stream in A; TV_FLAG = 0.","comment":"TV_FLAG = 0"},
        "5439": {"comment":"ROM 3's SYNTAX_Z: checking?"},
        "5444": {"comment":"ROM 3's STREAM_SELECT"},
        "5447": {"synopsis":"'#' and a stream (ROM 3's STREAM_ALTER), or the line number at once.","comment":"ROM 3's GET_CHAR"},
        "5450": {"comment":"ROM 3's STREAM_ALTER: '#' and a stream?"},
        "5453": {"comment":"No: the line number alone, or none"},
        "5455": {"comment":"ROM 3's GET_CHAR"},
        "5458": {"comment":"';'?"},
        "5462": {"comment":"','?"},
        "5466": {"synopsis":"Past the separator; the line number (CLASS_6).","comment":"ROM 3's NEXT_SKIP: past it"},
        "5469": {"comment":"The line number"},
        "5474": {"synopsis":"No number: 0 (ROM 3's USE_ZERO).","comment":"ROM 3's USE_ZERO: 0"},
        "5479": {"synopsis":"An optional number (ROM 3's FETCH_NUM).","comment":"ROM 3's FETCH_NUM: a line number or none"},
        "5482": {"synopsis":"The statement's end, then ROM 3's LIST_CMD from $1825.","comment":"The statement must end"},
        "5485": {"comment":"ROM 3's LIST_CMD from $1825"},
        "5489": {"synopsis":"Plays B strings (on the calculator stack) together, interrupts off (from $23F7, PLAY's\nroutine):\n1. Room in the workspace for a 55-byte block per string and a 60-byte shared one (ROM 3's\n   WORK_ROOM): IY at the shared one, IX at the top string's.\n2. Each string's block from the top down (PLAY_SET_STRING): the defaults, its place and end\n   (ROM 3's STK_FETCH, the last string first), its address into IY's list, its bit in IY +\n   16 cleared.\n3. Then (from $15F0) the tempo bytes at IY + 39 and IY + 40, the 13 bytes from $161D copied\n   to IY + 43, and the AY set up (register 7 = $F8, registers 11 and 12 = $FF).\nEntry: B = the number of strings.","comment":"Interrupts off while playing"},
        "5490": {"comment":"The count kept"},
        "5491": {"comment":"55 bytes a string"},
        "5494": {"comment":"60 shared"},
        "5497": {"synopsis":"55 bytes for each string.","comment":"One string's 55 more"},
        "5500": {"comment":"BC = the room"},
        "5502": {"comment":"ROM 3's WORK_ROOM"},
        "5505": {"comment":"No interrupts"},
        "5506": {"comment":"IY = the shared block"},
        "5509": {"comment":"IX = the room's end"},
        "5512": {"comment":"IY + 16 = $FF: no string yet"},
        "5516": {"synopsis":"The next string's block, from the top down: the octave 60, no MIDI channel, volume 15,\nlength 5, IX + 10, 11, 23, 24 and 33 = 0, IX + 22 = $FF; its place and end (ROM 3's\nSTK_FETCH); its address into IY's list; its bit into IY + 16; its number at IX + 2.","comment":"IX down 55 bytes: the next block"},
        "5521": {"comment":"Octave 60"},
        "5525": {"comment":"No MIDI channel"},
        "5529": {"comment":"Volume 15"},
        "5533": {"comment":"Length 5"},
        "5537": {"comment":"IX + 33 = 0"},
        "5541": {"comment":"IX + 10 and IX + 11 = 0"},
        "5549": {"comment":"IX + 22 = $FF"},
        "5553": {"comment":"IX + 23 and IX + 24 = 0"},
        "5561": {"comment":"ROM 3's STK_FETCH: DE = the string, BC = its length"},
        "5564": {"comment":"No interrupts"},
        "5565": {"comment":"The current place = the start"},
        "5571": {"comment":"The start again at IX + 12"},
        "5577": {"comment":"HL = the string's end"},
        "5579": {"comment":"At IX + 8"},
        "5585": {"comment":"B = the string's number"},
        "5588": {"comment":"C = 2 x (number - 1)"},
        "5593": {"comment":"Its slot in IY's list"},
        "5597": {"comment":"The block's address"},
        "5603": {"comment":"No carry: a 0 into IY + 16 for the string"},
        "5604": {"comment":"A bit for it"},
        "5608": {"comment":"One string fewer"},
        "5611": {"comment":"Its number"},
        "5614": {"comment":"More?"},
        "5616": {"comment":"The count dropped"},
        "5617": {"synopsis":"The tempo's delay ($0B1A), TEMPO_CODE copied to IY + 43; the mixer ($F8: tones on A-C, no\nnoise), the envelope period $FFFF.","comment":"IY + 39-40 = $0B1A, the tempo's delay"},
        "5625": {"comment":"DE = IY + 43"},
        "5633": {"comment":"TEMPO_CODE to IY + 43"},
        "5636": {"comment":"13 bytes"},
        "5641": {"comment":"Register 7, the mixer"},
        "5643": {"comment":"$F8: tones on A-C, no noise"},
        "5645": {"comment":"AY_WRITE"},
        "5648": {"comment":"Registers 11-12, the envelope period"},
        "5650": {"comment":"$FF into both"},
        "5652": {"comment":"Register 11"},
        "5655": {"comment":"Register 12"},
        "5659": {"comment":"PLAY_LOOP"},
        "5661": {"synopsis":"Copied into the shared block by PLAY_SETUP and run there with ROM 3 paged in (PLAY_TEMPO):\nRST $28 (ROM 3's calculator) and the codes stk-ten, exchange, division, a literal, division,\nend-calc, then RET: the tempo's delay from 4 x T's number."},
        "5674": {"synopsis":"Tests BREAK as ROM 3's BREAK_KEY does.\nExit: carry unless SPACE and CAPS SHIFT are both down.","comment":"Half-row SPACE to B"},
        "5678": {"comment":"Carry: SPACE up, done"},
        "5680": {"comment":"Half-row CAPS SHIFT to V"},
        "5684": {"comment":"Carry: CAPS SHIFT up"},
        "5686": {"synopsis":"The list of blocks from its pointers to the lengths (IY + 17); then PLAY_LIST_INIT's\nsettings.","comment":"BC = 17: the lengths' list"},
        "5689": {"comment":"On at PLAY_LIST_SET"},
        "5691": {"synopsis":"The list of blocks from the start (IY + 0): IY + 35 at it, IY + 34 = the ended bits, IY + 33\n= 1: the first string.","comment":"BC = 0: the blocks' list"},
        "5694": {"synopsis":"IY + 35 = HL, the strings to look at, the first string's bit.","comment":"HL = IY + BC"},
        "5698": {"comment":"IY + 35 = it"},
        "5704": {"comment":"IY + 34 = the ended bits"},
        "5710": {"comment":"IY + 33 = 1: the first string's bit"},
        "5714": {"comment":"Done"},
        "5715": {"synopsis":"IX = the block whose address is at HL.","comment":"DE = the block"},
        "5718": {"comment":"IX = it"},
        "5722": {"synopsis":"The list's place moved on to the next block.","comment":"HL = the list's place"},
        "5728": {"comment":"Two on"},
        "5730": {"comment":"Stored back"},
        "5737": {"synopsis":"Each string that has not ended: its next note (PLAY_NEXT).","comment":"The first string"},
        "5740": {"synopsis":"The next string: ended ones are passed by.","comment":"This string's ended bit: ended?"},
        "5744": {"comment":"Ended: on to the next"},
        "5746": {"comment":"IX = its block"},
        "5749": {"comment":"PLAY_NEXT"},
        "5752": {"synopsis":"The next string's bit; after the last, PLAY_NOTES.","comment":"The next string's bit; past the last?"},
        "5758": {"comment":"PLAY_LIST_NEXT"},
        "5763": {"synopsis":"The shortest length (PLAY_SHORTEST), the notes started (PLAY_START_NOTES); all ended: the AY\nsilenced, interrupts on, done.","comment":"The shortest length (PLAY_SHORTEST)"},
        "5766": {"comment":"DE kept"},
        "5767": {"comment":"PLAY_START_NOTES"},
        "5770": {"comment":"DE = the shortest again"},
        "5771": {"synopsis":"Have all the strings ended?","comment":"Every bit set: all ended?"},
        "5778": {"comment":"PLAY_SILENCE"},
        "5781": {"comment":"Interrupts on: PLAY done"},
        "5783": {"synopsis":"The shortest length waited (PLAY_WAIT), the lengths moved on (PLAY_ADVANCE), the next\nshortest; again.","comment":"One unit less"},
        "5784": {"comment":"PLAY_WAIT"},
        "5787": {"comment":"PLAY_ADVANCE"},
        "5790": {"comment":"The next shortest"},
        "5793": {"comment":"Until all have ended"},
        "5795": {"synopsis":"PLAY's command letters, searched by PLAY_FIND_LETTER (CPIR from here): H Z Y X W U V M T ) (\nN O !. Capitals only: o9c is a note name, and report k."},
        "5809": {"synopsis":"The string's next character, past spaces and ENTERs (PLAY_SKIP_SPACE).\nExit: carry at the string's end; otherwise A and the place moved on.","comment":"A = the character (PLAY_SKIP_SPACE)"},
        "5812": {"comment":"The string's end?"},
        "5813": {"comment":"The place on one"},
        "5816": {"comment":"No carry out of the low byte?"},
        "5821": {"synopsis":"A note's name: '#' sharp (+1), '$' flat (-1), any number of each; a capital A-G an octave\nhigher than the small letter; the note from PLAY_NOTE_TABLE.\nExit: A = the note within its octave, or $80 for '&' (a rest); at the string's end its bit\nis set in IY + 16. Anything else is report k."},
        "5822": {"comment":"C = the sharps less the flats"},
        "5824": {"synopsis":"The next character.","comment":"The next character"},
        "5827": {"comment":"The string's end?"},
        "5829": {"comment":"'&', a rest?"},
        "5833": {"comment":"$80: a rest"},
        "5835": {"synopsis":"Done.","comment":"HL back"},
        "5837": {"synopsis":"The string's end: its bit set in IY + 16.","comment":"This string's bit"},
        "5840": {"comment":"Into the ended bits"},
        "5846": {"comment":"Done"},
        "5848": {"synopsis":"'#': one higher.","comment":"'#'?"},
        "5852": {"comment":"One higher"},
        "5855": {"synopsis":"'$': one lower.","comment":"'$'?"},
        "5859": {"comment":"One lower"},
        "5862": {"synopsis":"A small letter (bit 5 set) as it is; a capital 12 higher.","comment":"A small letter?"},
        "5866": {"comment":"A capital: C + 12"},
        "5870": {"comment":"C = the octave's 12 added"},
        "5872": {"synopsis":"A-G only (report k otherwise): its place in the octave from PLAY_NOTE_TABLE, plus the sharps\nand flats.","comment":"Capital; 0-6 for A-G"},
        "5876": {"comment":"Below A: report k"},
        "5879": {"comment":"Past G: report k"},
        "5884": {"comment":"C kept"},
        "5885": {"comment":"Its entry in PLAY_NOTE_TABLE"},
        "5888": {"comment":"HL = PLAY_NOTE_TABLE + the note"},
        "5892": {"comment":"A = its place in the octave"},
        "5893": {"comment":"C back: the sharps less the flats"},
        "5894": {"comment":"Plus the sharps and flats"},
