        "5956": {"comment":"Ten times DE"},
        "5958": {"comment":"DE = the result"},
        "5960": {"synopsis":"Reads the current string up to its next note: BREAK stops it all (report L, after\nPLAY_SILENCE); each character: a command letter runs its routine from PLAY_COMMANDS;\nanything else is a note (PLAY_NOTE), which returns past PLAY_NEXT's loop. The string's end\nmarks it ended.","comment":"BREAK?"},
        "5965": {"comment":"Yes: silence"},
        "5969": {"comment":"Report L (code $14 in the next byte)"},
        "5973": {"synopsis":"A character.","comment":"The next character"},
        "5976": {"comment":"The end: the string has ended"},
        "5979": {"comment":"Which command?"},
        "5986": {"comment":"Its routine from PLAY_COMMANDS"},
        "5990": {"comment":"HL = the routine"},
        "5994": {"comment":"Run it; a note returns past the JR"},
        "5997": {"comment":"The next character"},
        "5999": {"comment":"A note: PLAY_RET_PAST returns here, PLAY_NEXT ends"},
        "6000": {"synopsis":"Jumps to HL."},
        "6001": {"synopsis":"'!': everything to the next '!' (or the end) is skipped.","comment":"The next character"},
        "6004": {"comment":"The end: the string has ended"},
        "6007": {"comment":"'!'?"},
        "6010": {"comment":"Skip on"},
        "6012": {"synopsis":"O n: the octave, 0-8 (report n otherwise): the base note 12 x n.","comment":"The number n (PLAY_NUMBER)"},
        "6015": {"comment":"Over 8: report n"},
        "6021": {"comment":"A = 4n, B = 4n"},
        "6025": {"comment":"B = 4n"},
        "6026": {"comment":"8n + 4n: 12n"},
        "6029": {"comment":"The octave's base note"},
        "6033": {"synopsis":"N: a separator; nothing to do."},
        "6034": {"synopsis":"'(': one bracket deeper (report d at 5): its place kept, from IX + 12.","comment":"The brackets open"},
        "6037": {"comment":"One more: 5 is report d"},
        "6043": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "6046": {"comment":"HL = its slot, IX + 12 + 2n"},
        "6052": {"comment":"The string's place kept there"},
        "6061": {"comment":"Done"},
        "6062": {"synopsis":"')': the repeat. The first time at a ')' its place is kept and the string goes back to its\n'(' (or the start); the second time it goes on, the bracket closed. With no '(' left open,\nthe repeat goes on for ever.","comment":"A = the ')' places kept less 1 ($FF: none)"},
        "6065": {"comment":"Their slots from IX + 23"},
        "6068": {"comment":"None kept: a new ')'"},
        "6072": {"comment":"HL = the last one kept"},
        "6075": {"comment":"This ')'? (low byte)"},
        "6081": {"comment":"And the high byte?"},
        "6088": {"comment":"Its second time: one fewer kept"},
        "6091": {"comment":"Any left?"},
        "6095": {"comment":"Some left: on"},
        "6096": {"comment":"Repeating for ever?"},
        "6100": {"comment":"No: done"},
        "6101": {"comment":"For ever: kept again"},
        "6105": {"comment":"Bracket 0: the string's start"},
        "6108": {"synopsis":"A new ')': kept (report d at 5), then back to the '('.","comment":"One more ')' kept"},
        "6111": {"comment":"5: report d"},
        "6117": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "6120": {"comment":"Its slot"},
        "6123": {"comment":"The place kept there"},
        "6131": {"comment":"Then back to the last '('"},
        "6132": {"comment":"A = the open brackets: back to the last '('"},
        "6135": {"synopsis":"The place back to bracket A's; one bracket less.","comment":"DE = 12: the '(' places from IX + 12"},
        "6138": {"comment":"PLAY_SLOT: HL = bracket A's kept place"},
        "6141": {"comment":"The string's place = the kept one"},
        "6147": {"comment":"The place moved"},
        "6150": {"comment":"One bracket less: any still open?"},
        "6153": {"comment":"Some still open: done"},
        "6154": {"comment":"None: the count 0, and IX + 10 bit 0 set"},
        "6163": {"synopsis":"HL = IX + DE + 2 x A: an entry of one of the block's lists.","comment":"HL = IX"},
