        "6372": {"synopsis":"H: all the strings ended at once.","comment":"IY + 16: every string's ended bit set"},
        "6377": {"synopsis":"A note, with its length before it: no digit, the current length; 1-9 a length (it becomes\nthe current one), 10-12 a triplet (three notes of the length); '_' ties more lengths to it.\nThe lengths go into the block's list (PLAY_LENGTH), the note sounds (through\nPLAY_START_NOTES); then PLAY_NEXT returns. A length of 0 or over 12 is report n; too many\ntriplet notes report o.","comment":"PLAY_IS_DIGIT: a length first?"},
        "6380": {"comment":"Not a digit: the current length"},
        "6383": {"comment":"PLAY_LEN_LIST: HL = the block's list of lengths"},
        "6386": {"comment":"PLAY_LEN_PTR: the string's pointer at the list's start"},
        "6389": {"comment":"No lengths yet (IX + 33)"},
        "6393": {"comment":"Back to the digit"},
        "6396": {"comment":"The length"},
        "6399": {"comment":"A = the length"},
        "6400": {"comment":"0: report n"},
        "6404": {"comment":"13 up: report n"},
