        "6670": {"synopsis":"Sounds note A (within the octave) on the string's channel: the octave's base added (128 or\nmore is report m); string 0 also sets the noise period (AY register 6) from it; for AY\nchannels A-C the tone period from PLAY_PERIODS (notes below 21 take $0FBE) into registers 2n\nand 2n + 1, and with the envelope in use, register 13 = the shape. Kept at IX + 0.","comment":"C = the note within its octave"},
        "6671": {"comment":"+ the octave's base"},
