        "7760": {"synopsis":"FORMAT's rates and their bit-time constants: 50 $0A88, 110 $04D4, 300 $01C3, 600 $00E0, 1200\n$006E, 2400 $0036, 4800 $0019, 9600 $000B."},
        "7792": {"synopsis":"RS232 input, channel P's input (reached from ROM 0's CHAN_P_IN, $3927, through CALL_ROM1):\none byte from the RS232 port, when one comes. With $5B66 bit 3 clear there is no input:\nreport J (ROM 3's CHAN_NO_INPUT). A byte kept from last time ($5B61 set, the byte at $5B62)\nis taken first. Otherwise BREAK stops with report L ($2AE7) and the byte is read with the\ndata in on bit 7 and the handshake out on bit 2 of the AY's I/O port A (register 14,\nRS232_RECV_7).\nExit: carry and A = the byte; no carry when none came.","comment":"Input on? ($5B66 bit 3)"},
        "7797": {"comment":"No: report J"},
        "7800": {"comment":"A byte kept from last time?"},
        "7803": {"comment":"$5B61 set?"},
