        "8046": {"synopsis":"RS232 output, channel P's output (reached from ROM 0's CHAN_P_OUT, $3921, through\nCALL_ROM1; and called for spaces at $1FF9 and $204B): with $5B66 bit 2 clear, A is sent as\nit\nis (PRINTER_OUT, at $2051); set, it is printed as text (RS232_PRINT_TXT).","comment":"As text? ($5B66 bit 2)"},
        "8052": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "8053": {"comment":"No: sent as it is (RS232_OUT)"},
        "8056": {"synopsis":"Prints A as text on an RS232 printer: - after AT or TAB, their numbers ($5B65 counts them,\nthe first kept at $5C0F); - keywords ($A3 up) through ROM 3's OUT_UDG_TOKEN, which prints\nthem back through the channel; - characters from space up (codes from $7F as '?'): sent\n(RS232_OUT, $2051), the column ($5B63) counted and a new line after the width ($5B64); -\nENTER: CR and LF, column 0; the comma control: spaces to the next column of 8; AT and TAB:\ntheir two numbers awaited; other controls below $10 nothing; colour controls: their numbers\ntaken and dropped.","comment":"The character kept"},
        "8057": {"comment":"Numbers awaited?"},
        "8060": {"comment":"Any?"},
        "8063": {"comment":"One fewer"},
        "8064": {"comment":"Stored"},
