        "8224": {"synopsis":"The numbers have arrived (A = the second): for AT the second (the column), for TAB the first\n($5C0F); for a colour nothing. The column is taken modulo the width ($5B64); 0 is a new line\n($1FD0); otherwise spaces (through $1F6E) up to it.","comment":"D = the second number"},
        "8225": {"comment":"The control: AT?"},
        "8232": {"comment":"TAB? Otherwise a colour: return"},
        "8236": {"comment":"TAB: its first number is the column"},
        "8240": {"synopsis":"Modulo the width.","comment":"A = the width: D below it?"},
        "8248": {"synopsis":"Less the width.","comment":"D = D - the width"},
        "8254": {"synopsis":"Spaces up to the column; column 0 a new line.","comment":"Column 0?"},
        "8256": {"comment":"Then a new line"},
        "8259": {"synopsis":"One space, until the printer's column ($5B63) is D.","comment":"Already at the column?"},
        "8264": {"comment":"A space through the print routine"},
        "8271": {"comment":"Until the column is reached"},
        "8273": {"synopsis":"Sends byte A to the printer (also called from $1FD7, $2149, $2156 and $331A, jumped to from\n$1F76, $1FCA and $1FDC):\n- $5B66 bit 3 clear: the parallel port (CENTRONICS_OUT);\n- otherwise the RS232 port on the AY chip's I/O port A (register 14): RS232_OUT (handshake\n  in on bit 6, data out on bit 3).\nExit: carry set (CENTRONICS_OUT).","comment":"$5B66 bit 3 clear: the parallel port?"},
        "8280": {"comment":"Then CENTRONICS_OUT"},
        "8283": {"synopsis":"Sends byte A on the RS232 port: waits for the printer's handshake (AY register 14 bit 6\nclear), testing BREAK meanwhile ($2AE7); then, interrupts off, 11 bits on bit 3 of port\n$BFFD, each a bit time ($5B5F - 2 rounds): a start bit, the eight bits low first, stop bits.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"The byte kept"},
        "8284": {"comment":"BC = $FFFD, the AY register port"},
        "8291": {"comment":"Register 14, the I/O port"},
        "8295": {"synopsis":"Waiting for the printer.","comment":"BREAK pressed? Then report L"},
        "8298": {"comment":"Handshake bit 6 still set?"},
        "8304": {"comment":"DE = the bit time ($5B5F) less 2"},
        "8314": {"comment":"The byte back, complemented"},
        "8316": {"comment":"Carry set: the start bit first"},
        "8317": {"comment":"11 bits"},
        "8319": {"comment":"No interrupts while sending"},
        "8320": {"synopsis":"One bit: carry clear for a 1 (the byte was complemented).","comment":"The count and the bits kept"},
        "8322": {"comment":"Port bits, bit 0 low"},
        "8324": {"comment":"HL = the bit time"},
        "8326": {"comment":"The AY data port"},
        "8329": {"comment":"Bit 0 or start bit (carry)?"},
        "8332": {"comment":"Bit 3 clear: a 0 on the line"},
        "8338": {"synopsis":"A 1: bit 3 set.","comment":"Bit 3 set: a 1 on the line"},
        "8344": {"synopsis":"The bit time.","comment":"Wait one bit time"},
        "8349": {"comment":"Padding for the timing"},
        "8352": {"comment":"The bits and the count back"},
        "8354": {"comment":"The next bit into carry, 0 in from the top"},
        "8356": {"comment":"Until 11 bits"},
        "8358": {"comment":"Interrupts back on"},
        "8360": {"synopsis":"Sends byte A to the parallel printer port:\n1. Waits while the printer is busy (port $0FFD bit 0 set), testing BREAK ($2AE7).\n2. The byte written to port $0FFD, then the strobe (port $1FFD bit 4, through its copy\n   $5B67) pulsed low and set high again, interrupts off meanwhile.\nExit: carry set.\nChanges: AF, BC.","comment":"The byte kept"},
        "8361": {"synopsis":"Waiting while the printer is busy.","comment":"BREAK pressed? Then report L"},
        "8364": {"comment":"The printer's status port"},
        "8367": {"comment":"Busy (bit 0 set)?"},
        "8373": {"comment":"The byte to the printer's data port"},
        "8376": {"comment":"No interrupts during the strobe"},
        "8377": {"comment":"Port $1FFD's copy"},
        "8380": {"comment":"Strobe low"},
        "8383": {"comment":"Strobe bit cleared"},
        "8387": {"comment":"Then set again"},
        "8389": {"comment":"Kept in the copy"},
        "8394": {"comment":"Interrupts back on"},
        "8395": {"comment":"Carry: sent"},
        "8397": {"comment":"Never reached"},
        "8398": {"synopsis":"COPY with nothing after it (COPY_CMD): the screen to the printer as graphics, only when\nrunning (FLAGS bit 7). The parallel port's strobe set high first ($5B67 bit 4); then 44\nstrips of 4 pixel lines from the top ($5B69 counting down from $2B): for each, COPY_CODES'\n$1B '1', $1B 'L', 0, 3 (768 dots), the 256 columns (COPY_STRIP) and a line feed; at the end\n$1B '2'. Every byte goes through PRINTER_OUT.","comment":"Checking syntax? Nothing to do"},
        "8403": {"comment":"Port $1FFD's copy"},
        "8409": {"comment":"Strobe high: the parallel port idle"},
        "8412": {"comment":"Copy kept and written"},
        "8417": {"comment":"Interrupts back on"},
        "8418": {"comment":"$5B69 = $2B: 44 strips"},
        "8423": {"synopsis":"One strip.","comment":"$1B '1', $1B 'L', 0, 3: 768 dots follow"},
        "8429": {"comment":"The strip's 256 columns"},
        "8432": {"comment":"A line feed"},
        "8438": {"comment":"The last strip done?"},
        "8445": {"comment":"The next strip up"},
        "8448": {"synopsis":"The last: $1B '2'.","comment":"$1B '2' at the end"},
        "8455": {"synopsis":"A strip's 256 columns, from x = 0 up (x = 255 - $5B68, which counts down from $FF).","comment":"$5B68 = $FF: 256 columns"},
        "8460": {"synopsis":"One column.","comment":"One column"},
        "8463": {"comment":"The last column done?"},
        "8469": {"comment":"The next column"},
        "8472": {"synopsis":"One column of the strip: its 4 pixels from y = 4 x $5B69 + 3 down (COPY_POINT), each as 2\ndots one above the other (mask D: $C0, $30, $0C, $03), make a byte, sent 3 times (768 dots\nin all).","comment":"D = the first pixel's two dots; E = 0"},
        "8475": {"comment":"C = the column count, B = the strip count"},
        "8479": {"comment":"B = 4 x strip + 3: the strip's top row"},
        "8485": {"comment":"C = x = 255 - count"},
        "8488": {"comment":"The byte so far: 0"},
        "8490": {"comment":"The mask and the place kept"},
        "8492": {"synopsis":"The next pixel down.","comment":"Pixel clear?"},
        "8497": {"comment":"Then no dots"},
        "8501": {"comment":"Set: the two dots"},
        "8502": {"synopsis":"Its two dots (E = D or 0) into the byte.","comment":"Into the byte"},
        "8505": {"comment":"The next row down"},
        "8506": {"comment":"The next two dots"},
        "8510": {"comment":"Kept again"},
        "8512": {"comment":"Until the mask runs out (4 pixels)"},
        "8514": {"comment":"The stack tidied, A = the byte"},
        "8517": {"comment":"Sent 3 times"},
        "8519": {"synopsis":"Sent three times."},
        "8521": {"comment":"The byte to the printer"},
        "8526": {"comment":"Three times"},
        "8529": {"synopsis":"Sends the bytes at HL (a count first) through PRINTER_OUT.\nChanges: AF, B, HL and what PRINTER_OUT changes.","comment":"B = the count"},
        "8531": {"synopsis":"One byte.","comment":"The next byte"},
        "8534": {"comment":"To the printer"},
        "8540": {"comment":"Until B bytes"},
        "8543": {"synopsis":"Z when the pixel at x = C, y = B is clear (ROM 3's PIXEL_BYTE, then its bit).\nChanges: AF, B, HL.","comment":"ROM 3's PIXEL_BYTE: HL = the byte, A = the bit"},
        "8546": {"comment":"B = 1-8: shifts for the mask"},
        "8548": {"comment":"A = 0, carry set"},
        "8550": {"synopsis":"The pixel's bit.","comment":"The bit moved into place"},
        "8553": {"comment":"Z when the pixel is clear"},
        "8555": {"synopsis":"COPY_128's printer control sequences, each a count then bytes, sent through COPY_SEND_CODES:\n6 bytes from $216B ($1B '1', $1B 'L', 0, 3), 1 from $2172 ($0A), 2 from $2174 ($1B '2')."},
        "8567": {"synopsis":"LPRINT (class $0E): PRINT to stream 3 (the printer).","comment":"Stream 3: the printer"},
        "8571": {"synopsis":"PRINT (class $0E): stream 2 (or LPRINT's 3) when running (ROM 3's STREAM_SELECT), the\ntemporary colours (ROM 3's COLOURS_TO_TEMP), the items (ROM 3's PRINT_LIST), then the\nstatement's end ($10B0).","comment":"Stream 2: the main screen"},
        "8573": {"synopsis":"The stream in A, when running (ROM 3's SYNTAX_Z).","comment":"Checking syntax? Then no stream (ROM 3's SYNTAX_Z)"},
        "8578": {"comment":"ROM 3's STREAM_SELECT: the stream's channel"},
        "8581": {"synopsis":"The colours and the items.","comment":"ROM 3's COLOURS_TO_TEMP"},
        "8584": {"comment":"ROM 3's PRINT_LIST: the items"},
        "8587": {"comment":"The statement's end (returns only when running)"},
        "8591": {"synopsis":"INPUT (class $0E): when running, stream 1 (the lower screen) and ROM 3's CLS_LOWER; TV_FLAG\n= 1; the items (ROM 3's INPUT_ITEM), the statement's end ($10B0), then ROM 3's INPUT_ITEMS\nfrom $20A0, past its own statement-end check.","comment":"Checking syntax? (ROM 3's SYNTAX_Z)"},
        "8596": {"comment":"Stream 1, the lower screen"},
        "8598": {"comment":"ROM 3's STREAM_SELECT"},
        "8601": {"comment":"ROM 3's CLS_LOWER"},
        "8604": {"synopsis":"TV_FLAG = 1: the lower screen; the items.","comment":"TV_FLAG = 1: the lower screen in use"},
        "8608": {"comment":"ROM 3's INPUT_ITEM: the items"},
        "8611": {"comment":"The statement's end"},
        "8614": {"comment":"ROM 3's INPUT_ITEMS from $20A0: the input finished"},
        "8618": {"synopsis":"COPY (class $0E):\n1. Nothing after it (ENTER or ':'): the screen to the printer (COPY_128).\n2. COPY EXP (token $B9) goes on at $3285.\n3. Otherwise a name (ROM 3's CLASS_A), TO (report C without it), then:\n- SCREEN$ or LPRINT: COPY_TO_SCREEN;\n- SPECTRUM FORMAT: COPY_TO_SPECTRUM;\n- another name: the statement's end ($10B0); both names, checked not empty (error $2C),\n  copied $FF-ended into bank 7 at $ED01 (the destination first, then the source; through\n  $3F63), then $2B8D with A = 0 and carry set copies the file.","comment":"The character after COPY (ROM 3's GET_CHAR)"},
        "8619": {"comment":"COPY alone? Then the screen to the printer"},
        "8629": {"comment":"EXP? COPY EXP"},
        "8634": {"comment":"Three NOPs, then the source name"},
        "8637": {"comment":"ROM 3's CLASS_A: the source name"},
        "8640": {"comment":"ROM 3's GET_CHAR"},
        "8643": {"comment":"TO?"},
        "8647": {"comment":"Report C: Nonsense in BASIC"},
        "8651": {"synopsis":"Past TO: SCREEN$, SPECTRUM or LPRINT?","comment":"Past TO (ROM 3's NEXT_SKIP)"},
        "8654": {"comment":"SCREEN$?"},
        "8659": {"comment":"SPECTRUM?"},
        "8664": {"comment":"LPRINT?"},
        "8669": {"comment":"ROM 3's CLASS_A: the destination name"},
        "8672": {"comment":"The statement's end"},
        "8675": {"comment":"ROM 3's STK_FETCH: DE = the name, BC = its length"},
        "8678": {"comment":"An empty name?"},
        "8682": {"comment":"Error $2C: Bad filename"},
        "8686": {"synopsis":"The destination name copied to $ED01 in bank 7, $FF after it; DE = where the source's goes.","comment":"HL = the name, DE = $ED01 in bank 7"},
        "8690": {"comment":"Copied into bank 7"},
        "8693": {"comment":"Bank 7 and its stack"},
        "8696": {"comment":"$FF ends the name"},
        "8699": {"comment":"DE = where the source name goes"},
        "8700": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "8703": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "8704": {"comment":"ROM 3's STK_FETCH: the source name"},
        "8707": {"comment":"An empty name?"},
        "8711": {"comment":"Error $2C: Bad filename"},
        "8715": {"synopsis":"The source name copied after it, $FF-ended; then the copy ($2B8D, A = 0, carry set).","comment":"DE = after the destination name"},
        "8717": {"comment":"Copied into bank 7"},
        "8720": {"comment":"Bank 7 and its stack"},
        "8723": {"comment":"$FF ends the name"},
        "8726": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "8729": {"comment":"A = 0, carry: a file to a file"},
        "8731": {"comment":"The copy"},
        "8735": {"synopsis":"COPY name TO SCREEN$ or TO LPRINT: the statement's end ($10B0); the name copied $FF-ended to\n$ED01 in bank 7; then $2B8D with A = the token ($AA or $E0) and carry clear: the file shown\non the screen or printed.","comment":"The token kept: SCREEN$ or LPRINT"},
        "8736": {"comment":"Past it (ROM 3's NEXT_SKIP)"},
        "8739": {"comment":"The token, in B"},
        "8740": {"comment":"The statement's end"},
        "8743": {"comment":"The token kept again"},
        "8744": {"comment":"ROM 3's STK_FETCH: the name"},
        "8747": {"comment":"DE = $ED01 in bank 7"},
        "8751": {"comment":"Copied into bank 7"},
        "8754": {"comment":"Bank 7 and its stack"},
        "8757": {"comment":"$FF ends the name"},
        "8760": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "8763": {"comment":"A = the token; NZ, no carry"},
        "8765": {"comment":"The file shown or printed"},
        "8769": {"synopsis":"COPY name TO SPECTRUM FORMAT: FORMAT ($D0) must follow (report C otherwise); the statement's\nend ($10B0); the name copied $FF-ended to $ED01 in bank 7; then $2B8D with A = 0 and carry\nclear.","comment":"Past SPECTRUM (ROM 3's NEXT_SKIP)"},
        "8772": {"comment":"FORMAT?"},
        "8776": {"comment":"Report C: Nonsense in BASIC"},
        "8780": {"synopsis":"Past FORMAT.","comment":"Past FORMAT"},
        "8783": {"comment":"The statement's end"},
        "8786": {"comment":"ROM 3's STK_FETCH: the name"},
        "8789": {"comment":"DE = $ED01 in bank 7"},
        "8793": {"comment":"Copied into bank 7"},
        "8796": {"comment":"Bank 7 and its stack"},
        "8799": {"comment":"$FF ends the name"},
        "8802": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "8805": {"comment":"A = 0, no carry"},
        "8806": {"comment":"The file converted"},
        "8810": {"synopsis":"NEW (class $0C): interrupts off and ROM 0's START_SETUP from $01B0 (CHARS onwards), which\nkeeps RAMTOP, the UDGs and the RAM disk and ends at the menu. Does not return.","comment":"Interrupts off for the restart"},
        "8811": {"comment":"ROM 0's START_SETUP from $01B0: start-up again"},
        "8816": {"synopsis":"CIRCLE (class $0E, after x and y): ',' and the radius (ROM 3's CLASS_6; report C without the\n','), the statement's end ($10B0), then ROM 3's CIRCLE_CMD from $232D, past its own checks.","comment":"The character after x, y (ROM 3's GET_CHAR)"},
        "8817": {"comment":"',' before the radius?"},
        "8821": {"comment":"Past it (ROM 3's NEXT_SKIP)"},
        "8822": {"comment":"ROM 3's CLASS_6: the radius"},
        "8825": {"comment":"The statement's end"},
        "8828": {"comment":"ROM 3's CIRCLE_CMD from $232D: the circle drawn"},
        "8832": {"synopsis":"DRAW (class $0E, after x and y): without a ',' the statement's end and a straight line (ROM\n3's LINE_DRAW); with one, the angle (ROM 3's CLASS_6), the statement's end and an arc (ROM\n3's DRAW_ARC from $2394).","comment":"The character after x, y (ROM 3's GET_CHAR)"},
        "8833": {"comment":"',' and an angle?"},
        "8837": {"comment":"The statement's end"},
        "8840": {"comment":"ROM 3's LINE_DRAW: a straight line"},
        "8844": {"synopsis":"',' and the angle: an arc.","comment":"Past the ',' (ROM 3's NEXT_SKIP)"},
        "8845": {"comment":"ROM 3's CLASS_6: the angle"},
        "8848": {"comment":"The statement's end"},
        "8851": {"comment":"ROM 3's DRAW_ARC from $2394: an arc"},
        "8855": {"synopsis":"DIM (class $0E): the array's name (ROM 3's LOOK_VARS; a name that cannot be an array is\nreport C); checking, its subscripts (ROM 3's VAR_SUBSCRIPTS) and the statement's end\n($10B0); running, ROM 3's DIM_RUN makes it.","comment":"ROM 3's LOOK_VARS: the array's name"},
        "8858": {"comment":"Not an array name? Report C"},
        "8860": {"comment":"Running? (ROM 3's SYNTAX_Z)"},
        "8865": {"comment":"Checking: the name taken as an array's"},
        "8867": {"comment":"ROM 3's VAR_SUBSCRIPTS: the subscripts checked"},
        "8870": {"comment":"The statement's end"},
        "8873": {"synopsis":"ROM 3's DIM_RUN.","comment":"ROM 3's DIM_RUN: the array made"},
        "8877": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $0B (report C, \"Nonsense in BASIC\").","comment":"Report C: Nonsense in BASIC"},
        "8881": {"synopsis":"When FLAGS2 bit 0 asks for it, the whole screen cleared (ROM 3's CLEAR_SCREEN). Called from\n$1331, $13E7 and ENTER_OK.","comment":"FLAGS2 bit 0: the screen to be cleared?"},
        "8886": {"comment":"ROM 3's CLEAR_SCREEN"},
        "8890": {"synopsis":"An edit line that starts like an expression (LINE_ENTER): it is evaluated, and its value\nreplaces it in the editor:\n1. Checked as an expression (ROM 3's SCAN_EXPR, PPC = $FFFE, FLAGS bit 7 clear): it must be\n   a number followed by ENTER, else report Q.\n2. Evaluated (FLAGS bit 7 set), the handler $5B6C = AFTER_RUN; the result's 5 bytes copied\n   from the top of the calculator stack to $5B6E.\n3. ENTER, then the number's characters (CALC_RESULT) fed to the editor as if typed.","comment":"PPC = $FFFE: an edit line"},
        "8896": {"comment":"FLAGS bit 7 clear: checking only"},
        "8900": {"comment":"CH_ADD to the line's first character"},
        "8903": {"comment":"ROM 3's SCAN_EXPR: the expression checked"},
        "8906": {"comment":"A numeric result?"},
        "8912": {"comment":"ROM 3's GET_CHAR: ENTER after it?"},
        "8917": {"comment":"FLAGS bit 7 set: running"},
        "8921": {"comment":"CH_ADD to the line's start again"},
        "8924": {"comment":"The handler: AFTER_RUN"},
        "8930": {"comment":"ROM 3's SCAN_EXPR: the expression evaluated"},
        "8933": {"comment":"A numeric result?"},
        "8939": {"comment":"DE = $5B6E, where the result goes"},
        "8942": {"comment":"HL = STKEND - 5: the result's 5 bytes"},
        "8951": {"comment":"Copied"},
        "8956": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $19 (report Q, \"Parameter error\").","comment":"Report Q: Parameter error"},
        "8960": {"synopsis":"ENTER fed to the editor (KEY_INTO_EDITOR), then the number printed into the workspace (one\nbyte of room from ROM 3's WORK_ROOM, K_CUR at it, stream -1; ROM 3's PRINT_FP), the channel\nput back (ROM 3's CHAN_SET_FLAGS), and each character fed in turn.","comment":"ENTER fed to the editor first"},
        "8965": {"comment":"ROM 3's WORK_ROOM: one byte"},
        "8971": {"comment":"K_CUR = that place"},
        "8974": {"comment":"The start kept"},
        "8975": {"comment":"CURCHL kept"},
        "8979": {"comment":"ROM 3's STREAM_SELECT: stream -1"},
        "8984": {"comment":"ROM 3's PRINT_FP: the number into the workspace"},
        "8987": {"comment":"CURCHL back (ROM 3's CHAN_SET_FLAGS)"},
        "8991": {"comment":"DE = the start"},
        "8992": {"comment":"HL = K_CUR - the start: the count"},
        "8998": {"synopsis":"One character to the editor.","comment":"The next character"},
        "8999": {"comment":"Into the editor"},
        "9002": {"comment":"The next"},
        "9003": {"comment":"Until the count runs out"},
        "9009": {"synopsis":"Feeds character A to the editor as a key (ROM 0's KEY_DISPATCH), in bank 7 on its stack\n($2B73), with stream 2; $EC0D bit 3 cleared before and after; bank 0 again ($2B4E).\nChanges: AF, BC and what KEY_DISPATCH changes; keeps DE, HL."},
        "9011": {"comment":"Bank 7 and its stack"},
        "9014": {"comment":"$EC0D bit 3 cleared"},
        "9019": {"comment":"The key kept"},
        "9020": {"comment":"ROM 3's STREAM_SELECT: stream 2"},
        "9025": {"comment":"The key back"},
        "9026": {"comment":"ROM 0's KEY_DISPATCH: the key handled"},
        "9031": {"comment":"$EC0D bit 3 cleared again"},
        "9036": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "9042": {"synopsis":"CH_ADD = E_LINE - 1, then the line's first character (RST $20).\nExit: A = the character.","comment":"CH_ADD = E_LINE - 1"},
        "9049": {"comment":"The line's first character (ROM 3's NEXT_SKIP)"},
        "9051": {"synopsis":"Whether the edit line starts with LET ($F1) and has only one statement.\nExit: Z when it does (ENTER found before any ':').","comment":"CH_ADD to the line's start"},
        "9054": {"comment":"LET?"},
        "9057": {"comment":"The line from its start"},
        "9060": {"synopsis":"The next byte: ENTER (Z) or ':' (NZ) ends it.","comment":"The next byte"},
        "9062": {"comment":"ENTER: Z"},
        "9065": {"comment":"':' ends it with NZ"},
        "9069": {"comment":"NZ"},
        "9071": {"synopsis":"Whether A is one of OPERATORS.\nExit: Z when it is; A kept.\nChanges: F, B, HL.","comment":"B = the character"},
        "9072": {"comment":"HL = OPERATORS"},
        "9075": {"synopsis":"The next operator.","comment":"The next operator"},
        "9077": {"comment":"The 0 at the end?"},
        "9080": {"comment":"Is it this one?"},
        "9083": {"comment":"Found: Z, A kept"},
        "9085": {"synopsis":"Not an operator: NZ.","comment":"NZ"},
        "9087": {"comment":"A kept"},
        "9089": {"synopsis":"OPERATOR_TEST's list: + - * / ^ = > <, the tokens <= >= <> OR AND ($C7 $C8 $C9 $C5 $C6),\nended by 0."},
        "9103": {"synopsis":"Whether A is a function keyword (a token from $A5 to $C3, other than $AC and $AD).\nExit: Z when it is; NZ otherwise, with carry below $A5.","comment":"Below $A5?"},
        "9107": {"comment":"$C4 or above?"},
        "9111": {"comment":"$AC?"},
        "9115": {"comment":"$AD?"},
        "9119": {"comment":"Z: a function keyword"},
        "9121": {"synopsis":"Not one: NZ.","comment":"NZ, carry below $A5"},
        "9124": {"synopsis":"Whether A is a letter, or '.'.\nExit: Z when it is; otherwise NUMBER_TEST.","comment":"B = the character"},
        "9125": {"comment":"A letter in either case?"},
        "9131": {"comment":"Above 'z'?"},
        "9135": {"comment":"Z: a letter"},
        "9137": {"synopsis":"Otherwise: whether a number starts here: digits (each passed with RST $20), then '.', 'E',\n'e' or an operator (OPERATOR_TEST).\nExit: Z when it does.","comment":"The character back: '.'?"},
        "9141": {"comment":"A digit?"},
        "9144": {"comment":"No: not a number"},
        "9146": {"synopsis":"Past the digits.","comment":"Past it (ROM 3's NEXT_SKIP)"},
        "9147": {"comment":"Another digit?"},
        "9152": {"comment":"'.'?"},
        "9155": {"comment":"'E'?"},
        "9158": {"comment":"'e'?"},
        "9161": {"comment":"Otherwise an operator?"},
        "9163": {"synopsis":"Not a number: NZ.","comment":"NZ"},
        "9166": {"synopsis":"Whether A is a digit.\nExit: Z when it is; NZ otherwise, with carry below '0'.","comment":"Below '0'?"},
        "9170": {"comment":"Above '9'?"},
        "9174": {"comment":"Z: a digit"},
        "9176": {"synopsis":"Not a digit: NZ.","comment":"NZ; carry below '0'"},
        "9179": {"synopsis":"PLAY (class $0E): 1 to 8 strings (ROM 3's CLASS_A each) separated by ','; more is error code\n$2B; the statement's end ($10B0); then $1571 plays them with B = the number of strings.","comment":"B = 0 strings so far"},
        "9181": {"comment":"ROM 3's GET_CHAR"},
        "9182": {"synopsis":"One string; ',' and another.","comment":"The count kept"},
        "9183": {"comment":"ROM 3's CLASS_A: one string"},
        "9186": {"comment":"The count back"},
        "9187": {"comment":"One more"},
        "9188": {"comment":"',' and another?"},
        "9192": {"comment":"Past it (ROM 3's NEXT_SKIP)"},
        "9195": {"synopsis":"B strings: at most 8.","comment":"More than 8?"},
        "9200": {"comment":"Error $2B"},
        "9204": {"synopsis":"The statement's end, then $1571.","comment":"The statement's end"},
        "9207": {"comment":"The strings played"},
        "9232": {"synopsis":"Sets +3DOS up at start-up (ROM 0's START_SETUP calls it through $3E80) and says which drives\nthere are. In bank 7 on its stack ($2B73), each ROM 2 call between DOS_STACK_SAVE ($3213)\nand DOS_STACK_BACK ($324B):\n1. Unless $5B66 bit 7 says it was done: bit 7 set, the hard disk units counted\n   (HD_COUNT_UNITS, $00A3) and the count kept at $DF9D.\n2. SETUP_ALL (DOS_JUMPS $0100) every time; \"Physical drives: \" printed.\n3. SET_ERR_HOOK ($014E) with A = $FF and HL = $0002 (ROM 2's JP_SHOW_MESSAGE).\n4. FDC_PRESENT ($0157): no disk controller: '0' floppies ($5B66 bit 4 clear). With one:\n   $5B66\n   bit 4 set and bit 5 cleared; UNIT1_PRESENT ($017B): a second drive sets bit 5 and gives\n   '2'; without one DRIVE_B_SET ($0154, C = 0, HL = $0005, ROM 2's JP_SHOW_INSERT) makes B:\n   the same unit as A:, '1'.\n5. The count, \" floppy, \", the hard disk count ($DF9D) and \" IDE\", then \"Logical drives: \"\n   (the line is full after \" IDE\") and each letter A-P whose word in the drive table at\n$E2A0\n   (bank 7) is not 0, BRIGHT 1 for the one at $5B79 (LOAD's default), BRIGHT 0 for the\n   others.\n6. Bank 0.","comment":"Bank 7 and its stack"},
        "9235": {"comment":"Onto +3DOS's stack"},
        "9238": {"comment":"$5B66 bit 7: done before?"},
        "9243": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "9245": {"comment":"Done from now on"},
        "9247": {"comment":"ROM 2's HD_COUNT_UNITS: A = the hard disks"},
        "9252": {"comment":"Kept at $DF9D"},
        "9255": {"synopsis":"Every time: ROM 2's SETUP_ALL (DOS_JUMPS $0100); \"Physical drives: \" printed.","comment":"ROM 2's SETUP_ALL"},
        "9260": {"comment":"Back to this ROM's stack"},
        "9263": {"comment":"\"Physical drives: \""},
        "9269": {"synopsis":"Set up: the disk error hook.","comment":"A = $FF: a hook set"},
        "9271": {"comment":"HL = $0002, ROM 2's JP_SHOW_MESSAGE"},
        "9274": {"comment":"ROM 2's SET_ERR_HOOK: the disk error hook"},
        "9282": {"comment":"Back"},
        "9285": {"comment":"$5B66 bit 4 clear: no disk controller yet"},
        "9290": {"comment":"Bank 7 and its stack"},
        "9293": {"comment":"ROM 2's FDC_PRESENT: a disk controller?"},
        "9301": {"comment":"'0' floppies when none answers"},
        "9303": {"comment":"No controller"},
        "9305": {"comment":"$5B66 bit 4 set: a controller"},
        "9310": {"comment":"$5B66 bit 5 cleared: no second drive yet"},
        "9312": {"comment":"Bank 7 and its stack"},
        "9315": {"comment":"ROM 2's UNIT1_PRESENT: a second drive?"},
        "9320": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "9323": {"comment":"Carry: drive B is real"},
        "9325": {"comment":"C = 0: B: is unit 0, the same drive as A:"},
        "9327": {"comment":"HL = $0005, ROM 2's JP_SHOW_INSERT"},
        "9330": {"comment":"Bank 7 and its stack"},
        "9333": {"comment":"ROM 2's DRIVE_B_SET"},
        "9341": {"comment":"'1': drive A only"},
        "9343": {"comment":"On"},
        "9345": {"synopsis":"A second drive: $5B66 bit 5 set; '2' floppies.","comment":"$5B66 bit 5 set: drive B"},
        "9350": {"comment":"'2' floppies"},
        "9352": {"synopsis":"The floppy count (A), \" floppy, \", the hard disk count and \" IDE\" with \"Logical drives: \";\nthen the drive letters in use, from the drive table at $E2A0 (bank 7).","comment":"The floppy count"},
        "9353": {"comment":"\" floppy, \""},
        "9359": {"comment":"The hard disk count, from $DF9D"},
        "9362": {"comment":"As a digit"},
        "9365": {"comment":"\" IDE\" and \"Logical drives: \""},
        "9371": {"comment":"HL = the drive table, a word a letter"},
        "9374": {"comment":"C = 'A'"},
        "9376": {"comment":"16 letters, A-P"},
        "9378": {"synopsis":"One letter: its word in the drive table 0 means no drive.","comment":"The word not 0?"},
        "9382": {"comment":"0: not shown"},
        "9384": {"comment":"LOAD's default drive ($5B79)?"},
        "9388": {"comment":"E = 0: BRIGHT 0"},
        "9392": {"comment":"E = 1: BRIGHT 1"},
        "9394": {"synopsis":"BRIGHT E, then the letter.","comment":"BRIGHT control"},
        "9397": {"comment":"E: on or off"},
        "9399": {"comment":"The letter"},
        "9401": {"synopsis":"The next letter.","comment":"The next letter"},
        "9404": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "9408": {"synopsis":"Prints the text at HL through ROM 3's PRINT_A, up to the 0 that ends it.\nExit: HL at the 0.\nChanges: AF, HL.","comment":"The 0 at the end?"},
        "9415": {"synopsis":"A program without LINE (from $0A92): an ASN here is passed over; the statement's end; then\nSE_NO_AUTORUN.","comment":"ASN?"},
        "9419": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "9420": {"synopsis":"The statement's end, then SE_NO_AUTORUN.","comment":"The statement's end"},
        "9423": {"comment":"No auto-run"},
        "9456": {"synopsis":"What the +3 BASIC editor runs when a line is entered (called from $1462): it checks the line\nand, through ENTER_HANDLER, stores or runs it:\n1. ERR_NR = $FF, DF_SZ = 2; ERR_SP points at ERROR_TO_ROM1's copy ($5B3A) and the handler\n   $5B6C at ENTER_HANDLER, so a report while checking ends there.\n2. CH_ADD to the line's first character (CH_ADD_TO_LINE). A keyword from $A5 to $C3 other\n   than $AC and $AD, '(', '-', '+', a letter, '.' or a number (KEYWORD_TEST, LETTER_TEST)\n   goes on at CALC_LINE.\n3. Otherwise $0FBE checks it, unless $EC0E (bank 7) is 4: then only a line starting with LET\n   goes on (LET_TEST); anything else returns, doing nothing.","comment":"ERR_NR = $FF: no report"},
        "9460": {"comment":"DF_SZ = 2"},
        "9464": {"comment":"ERROR_TO_ROM1's copy stacked"},
        "9468": {"comment":"ERR_SP at it"},
        "9472": {"comment":"The handler: ENTER_HANDLER"},
        "9478": {"comment":"CH_ADD to the line's first character"},
        "9481": {"comment":"A function keyword?"},
        "9484": {"comment":"Then the line is a calculation"},
        "9487": {"comment":"'('?"},
        "9492": {"comment":"'-'?"},
        "9497": {"comment":"'+'?"},
        "9502": {"comment":"A letter, '.' or a number?"},
        "9508": {"comment":"Bank 7 and its stack"},
        "9511": {"comment":"$EC0E: the editor's mode"},
        "9514": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "9517": {"comment":"Not 4? The line checked at $0FBE"},
        "9522": {"comment":"4: a single LET statement?"},
        "9525": {"comment":"Then checked at $0FBE"},
        "9528": {"comment":"Anything else: ERR_SP's entry dropped, nothing done"},
        "9530": {"comment":"Bank 7 and its stack","synopsis":"Where an error report ends (ROM 0's JP $253A at $010C, with this ROM paged in): in bank 7,\nfile 0 closed (CLOSE_FILE, DOS_JUMPS $0109) or, failing that, abandoned (CLOSE_NO_WRITE,\n$010C); then bank 0 and a jump to the handler in $5B6C (ENTER_HANDLER, AFTER_RUN ...)."},
        "9533": {"comment":"File 0"},
        "9535": {"comment":"ROM 2's CLOSE_FILE"},
        "9546": {"comment":"Closed?"},
        "9548": {"comment":"File 0"},
        "9550": {"comment":"ROM 2's CLOSE_NO_WRITE: abandoned"},
        "9561": {"synopsis":"Bank 0; on to the handler.","comment":"Bank 0"},
        "9564": {"comment":"The handler in $5B6C"},
        "9568": {"synopsis":"Where checking a line ends (GO_HANDLER): with a report pending (ERR_NR bit 7 clear) back to\nthe editor; with none, a line with a number is stored (STORE_LINE) and any other line is\nrun:\n1. ROM 3's EDIT_LINE_NO reads its number; an empty line does nothing.\n2. The screen cleared when FLAGS2 asks (CLEAR_IF_ASKED); the lower screen cleared when\n   TV_FLAG bit 6 is clear (ROM 3's CLS_LOWER); with $EC0D bit 6 clear and $EC0E = 0, ROM 0's\n   CLEAR_LOW_3.\n3. TV_FLAG bit 3 cleared, SCR_CT from S_POSN's line, FLAGS bit 7 set (running), NSPPC = 1;\n   $3E00 stacked as the end marker, ERROR_TO_ROM1's copy ($5B3A) above it under ERR_SP,\n   $5B6C = AFTER_RUN; then $1047 runs the line.","comment":"ERR_NR bit 7: no report?"},
        "9574": {"comment":"A report: back"},
        "9575": {"synopsis":"No report: CH_ADD to the line's start, its number read.","comment":"CH_ADD = E_LINE"},
        "9581": {"comment":"ROM 3's EDIT_LINE_NO: BC = the line's number"},
        "9584": {"comment":"A number?"},
        "9586": {"comment":"Then the line is stored"},
        "9589": {"comment":"ROM 3's GET_CHAR"},
        "9590": {"comment":"An empty line: nothing"},
        "9593": {"comment":"The screen cleared if FLAGS2 asks"},
        "9596": {"comment":"TV_FLAG bit 6: the lower screen kept?"},
        "9602": {"comment":"ROM 3's CLS_LOWER"},
        "9605": {"synopsis":"The line is run: TV_FLAG bit 6 cleared; in bank 7, ROM 0's CLEAR_LOW_3 when $EC0D bit 6 is\nclear and $EC0E is 0.","comment":"TV_FLAG bit 6 cleared"},
        "9609": {"comment":"Bank 7 and its stack"},
        "9612": {"comment":"$EC0D bit 6 set?"},
        "9619": {"comment":"$EC0E: the editor's mode 0?"},
        "9625": {"comment":"ROM 0's CLEAR_LOW_3"},
        "9630": {"synopsis":"Bank 0; then as $1047 expects it: TV_FLAG bit 3 cleared, SCR_CT, FLAGS bit 7, NSPPC = 1, the\nstack and ERR_SP, the handler.","comment":"Bank 0"},
        "9633": {"comment":"TV_FLAG bit 3 cleared"},
        "9638": {"comment":"SCR_CT = 25 - S_POSN's line"},
        "9646": {"comment":"FLAGS bit 7 set: running"},
        "9650": {"comment":"NSPPC = 1: the first statement"},
        "9654": {"comment":"$3E00: the end marker"},
        "9658": {"comment":"ERROR_TO_ROM1's copy above it"},
        "9662": {"comment":"ERR_SP at it"},
        "9666": {"comment":"The handler: AFTER_RUN"},
        "9672": {"comment":"The line run"},
        "9675": {"synopsis":"Where a run ends, with or without a report (the handler in $5B6C, and jumps from $139C,\n$13AA, $143E, $1446, $144E): the report printed and the editor resumed:\n1. The machine stack from RAMTOP + 1, $5B6A = $5BFF; a NOP; FLAGS bit 5 cleared.\n2. A = ERR_NR + 1, the report's code. FLAGX, X_PTR's high byte and DEFADD cleared, STRMS for\n   stream 0 = 1; ROM 3's CLEAR_EDIT_WS and CLS_LOWER; TV_FLAG bit 5 set.\n3. The code printed (ROM 3's PRINT_A_DIGIT) and a space: 0-9 as a digit, 10-28 as A-S, 29-43\n   as a lowercase letter from a; from 44 (the disk reports) no code at all.\n4. The message: ROM 3's report messages ($1391, PRINT_MESSAGE) below 29, REPORT_TABLE's\n   otherwise (PRINT_BIT7_TEXT); then REPORT_LINE.","comment":"SP = RAMTOP"},
        "9679": {"comment":"Plus 1"},
        "9680": {"comment":"$5B6A = $5BFF: the bank 7 stack reset"},
        "9686": {"comment":"A NOP, no HALT"},
        "9687": {"comment":"FLAGS bit 5 cleared: no new key"},
        "9691": {"comment":"A = ERR_NR + 1: the report's code"},
        "9695": {"synopsis":"Prints report A (REPORT_G_ROOM comes here): the editing state cleared, the code character, a\nspace and the message.","comment":"Kept"},
        "9696": {"comment":"FLAGX = 0"},
        "9702": {"comment":"X_PTR's high byte = 0"},
        "9705": {"comment":"DEFADD = 0"},
        "9708": {"comment":"STRMS for stream 0 = 1"},
        "9714": {"comment":"ROM 3's CLEAR_EDIT_WS"},
        "9717": {"comment":"FLAGX bit 5 cleared"},
        "9721": {"comment":"ROM 3's CLS_LOWER"},
        "9724": {"comment":"TV_FLAG bit 5 set: the lower screen to clear"},
        "9728": {"comment":"The code back, also in B"},
        "9730": {"comment":"0-9: a digit"},
        "9734": {"comment":"10-28: A-S"},
        "9738": {"comment":"44 up: no code printed"},
        "9742": {"comment":"29-43: a-o"},
        "9746": {"synopsis":"10-28: 7 more, so that A + '0' is A-S.","comment":"7 more: A-S"},
        "9748": {"synopsis":"The code's character (ROM 3's PRINT_A_DIGIT) and a space.","comment":"ROM 3's PRINT_A_DIGIT: A + '0'"},
        "9751": {"comment":"A space"},
        "9754": {"synopsis":"The message: 29 up from REPORT_TABLE through PRINT_BIT7_TEXT.","comment":"The code again: below 29?"},
        "9759": {"comment":"BC = the code - 29"},
        "9764": {"comment":"HL = REPORT_TABLE"},
        "9767": {"comment":"Two bytes an entry"},
        "9769": {"comment":"DE = the message"},
        "9772": {"comment":"Printed up to its bit-7 end (PRINT_BIT7_TEXT)"},
        "9777": {"synopsis":"A 48K report's message: ROM 3's messages at $1391 through PRINT_MESSAGE.","comment":"DE = ROM 3's report messages"},
        "9780": {"comment":"ROM 3's PRINT_MESSAGE: message A"},
        "9783": {"synopsis":"The rest of the report: \", \" (ROM 3's message table at $1536), the line (PPC) and the\nstatement (SUBPPC) through PRINT_BC_NUM, ROM 3's CLEAR_INPUT; then, after a report other\nthan 0 OK, CONTINUE's place: the statement after this one for 9 STOP and L BREAK, OLDPPC and\nOSPPC from NEWPPC and NSPPC or from PPC and SUBPPC; NSPPC = $FF, FLAGS bit 3 and $5B66 bit 0\ncleared; back to the editor (ROM 0's EDITOR_MAIN).","comment":"A = 0: \", \""},
        "9784": {"comment":"DE = ROM 3's table at $1536"},
        "9787": {"comment":"ROM 3's PRINT_MESSAGE"},
        "9790": {"comment":"BC = PPC"},
        "9794": {"comment":"ROM 3's PRINT_BC_NUM: the line"},
        "9797": {"comment":"':'"},
        "9800": {"comment":"BC = SUBPPC"},
        "9805": {"comment":"ROM 3's PRINT_BC_NUM: the statement"},
        "9808": {"comment":"ROM 3's CLEAR_INPUT"},
        "9811": {"comment":"Report 0 OK?"},
        "9815": {"comment":"Then no CONTINUE place"},
        "9817": {"comment":"9 STOP?"},
        "9821": {"comment":"L BREAK?"},
        "9825": {"synopsis":"9 STOP and L BREAK: CONTINUE goes on at the next statement.","comment":"SUBPPC + 1: the next statement"},
        "9828": {"synopsis":"OLDPPC and OSPPC set from NEWPPC and NSPPC, or, with NSPPC bit 7 set, from PPC and SUBPPC.","comment":"Three bytes"},
        "9831": {"comment":"DE = OSPPC, the last of them"},
        "9834": {"comment":"HL = NSPPC"},
        "9837": {"comment":"NSPPC bit 7: no jump pending?"},
        "9841": {"comment":"Then from SUBPPC"},
        "9842": {"synopsis":"The three bytes copied.","comment":"OLDPPC and OSPPC set"},
        "9844": {"synopsis":"NSPPC = $FF, FLAGS bit 3 and $5B66 bit 0 cleared; on to ROM 0's EDITOR_MAIN.","comment":"NSPPC = $FF: no jump"},
        "9848": {"comment":"FLAGS bit 3 cleared"},
        "9852": {"comment":"$5B66 bit 0 cleared"},
        "9857": {"comment":"ROM 0's EDITOR_MAIN"},
        "9862": {"synopsis":"Report G (code $10, \"No room for line\") from STORE_LINE, which stacks this as the place a\nfailed MAKE_ROOM returns to.","comment":"Code $10: report G"},
        "9864": {"comment":"BC = 0"},
        "9867": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "9870": {"synopsis":"Stores the edit line as program line BC:\n1. E_PPC = BC; in bank 7 E_PPC and $EC08 = BC too when BC is not 0.\n2. REPORT_G_ROOM stacked; the line's length from CH_ADD to WORKSP; an old line with that\n   number is removed (ROM 3's FIND_LINE, NEXT_ITEM, RECLAIM).\n3. A line holding only its ENTER is not stored: in bank 7 E_PPC becomes the line before it\n   (ROM 0's PREV_LINE_NUM).\n4. Otherwise room is made before it (ROM 3's MAKE_ROOM, PROG kept), the text copied down,\n   and its number (high byte first) and length written before it.","comment":"E_PPC = BC"},
        "9874": {"comment":"Bank 7 and its stack"},
        "9877": {"comment":"Line 0?"},
        "9881": {"comment":"E_PPC = BC"},
        "9885": {"comment":"$EC08 = BC"},
        "9889": {"synopsis":"Bank 0; the line looked for.","comment":"Bank 0"},
        "9892": {"comment":"DE = CH_ADD, the line's text"},
        "9896": {"comment":"REPORT_G_ROOM, if MAKE_ROOM fails"},
        "9900": {"comment":"HL = WORKSP - CH_ADD - 1: the length"},
        "9906": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "9907": {"comment":"HL = the number"},
        "9909": {"comment":"ROM 3's FIND_LINE: a line with this number?"},
        "9912": {"comment":"No: none to remove"},
        "9914": {"comment":"ROM 3's NEXT_ITEM: its end"},
        "9917": {"comment":"ROM 3's RECLAIM: the old line removed"},
        "9920": {"synopsis":"Only an ENTER?","comment":"BC = the length"},
        "9921": {"comment":"Only 1, its ENTER?"},
        "9926": {"comment":"Bank 7 and its stack"},
        "9929": {"comment":"HL kept"},
        "9930": {"comment":"HL = E_PPC"},
        "9933": {"comment":"ROM 0's PREV_LINE_NUM: the line before it"},
        "9938": {"comment":"E_PPC = it"},
        "9941": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "9942": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "9945": {"comment":"Done"},
        "9947": {"synopsis":"Room for the line and its four-byte head (ROM 3's MAKE_ROOM), PROG kept; the text copied;\nthe length and the number written.","comment":"The length kept"},
        "9948": {"comment":"Plus 4: number and length"},
        "9952": {"comment":"HL = before the line found"},
        "9953": {"comment":"PROG kept"},
        "9958": {"comment":"ROM 3's MAKE_ROOM"},
        "9961": {"comment":"PROG back"},
        "9965": {"comment":"BC = the length"},
        "9967": {"comment":"DE = the room's last byte"},
        "9968": {"comment":"HL = WORKSP - 2: the text's last byte"},
        "9973": {"comment":"The text copied down"},
        "9975": {"comment":"DE = E_PPC, the number"},
        "9979": {"comment":"BC = the length"},
        "9980": {"comment":"The length, high byte"},
        "9981": {"comment":"Low byte"},
        "9983": {"comment":"The number, low byte"},
        "9985": {"comment":"High byte (first in the line)"},
        "9987": {"synopsis":"REPORT_G_ROOM dropped; done.","comment":"REPORT_G_ROOM dropped"},
        "9989": {"synopsis":"This ROM's own report messages, for codes 29 up (ERR_NR $1C up): one address per code, 62\nwords for codes 29-90. Codes 29-43 print as letters a-o; from 44 no code is printed. Two\npairs share a message (\"File does not exist\" for 35 and 36, \"Bad filename\" for 44 and 45).\nCodes 29-80 point into REPORT_MSGS, codes 81-90 (the hard disk reports, from \"Invalid\npartition\") into REPORT_MSGS_2 at $35E3."},
        "10113": {"synopsis":"Report messages, the last letter with bit 7 set: MERGE error, Wrong file type, CODE error,\nToo many brackets, File already exists, Invalid name, File does not exist, Invalid device,\nInvalid baud rate, Invalid note name, Number too big, Note out of range, Out of range, Too\nmany tied notes, Bad filename, Bad parameters, Drive not found, File not found, File already\nexists, End of file found, Disk full, Directory full, File is read only, File not open, File\nalready in use, No rename between drives, Missing extent, Uncached, File too big, Disk is\nnot\nbootable, Drive in use, Drive not ready, Disk is write protected, Seek fail, CRC data error,\nNo data, Missing address mark, Unrecognised disk format, Unknown disk error, Disk has been\nchanged, Unsuitable media, Invalid attribute, Cannot copy to/from tape, Destination cannot\nbe\nwild, Destination must be drive, Drive B: is not present, +2A does not support format, Drive\nmust be A: or B:, Invalid drive, Code length error (codes 29-80 through REPORT_TABLE)."},
        "10940": {"synopsis":"Prints the text at DE through RST $10, up to and including the character with bit 7 set\n(printed without it). The same job as the 128K editor ROM's PRINT_BIT7_TEXT. Called at $262C\nwith a message from REPORT_TABLE.\nChanges: AF, DE."},
        "10943": {"comment":"DE kept round RST $10"},
        "10946": {"comment":"The same character again"},
        "10948": {"comment":"Bit 7 into carry: the last one?"},
        "10952": {"synopsis":"Stops with a report: RST $08 jumps here, and so do the CALLs at some 45 places; the byte\nafter the RST or CALL is the code (as ERR_NR holds it, one less than the report's number),\nand nothing returns. The same job as the 128K editor ROM's ERROR_128, without its paging:\n1. SP = ERR_SP; the code kept in $5B5E.\n2. A code below $1D, a report the 48K ROM knows, is raised in ROM 3: RST $28 runs $5B5D,\n   which ROM 0's start-up made $CF (RST $08), so ROM 3's error restart finds the code after\n   it at $5B5E.\n3. The +3's own codes ($1D up) go on at ERROR_128_OWN.\nEntry: the code in the byte after the call.","comment":"HL = the code's address"},
        "10953": {"comment":"The stack at ERR_SP"},
        "10957": {"comment":"The code"},
        "10958": {"comment":"After the RST $08 at $5B5D"},
        "10961": {"comment":"A 48K report (code below $1D)?"},
        "10966": {"comment":"RST $08 with the code, in ROM 3"},
        "10969": {"synopsis":"The +3's own report (code $1D up): ERR_NR = the code, X_PTR = CH_ADD, ROM 3's CALC_RESET,\nthen the return to the address at ERR_SP.","comment":"Back to the code"},
        "10970": {"comment":"ERR_NR"},
        "10973": {"comment":"X_PTR = CH_ADD"},
        "10979": {"comment":"ROM 3's CALC_RESET"},
        "10983": {"synopsis":"Tests BREAK: returns with carry unless both SPACE (port $7FFE bit 0) and CAPS SHIFT (port\n$FEFE bit 0) are down; with both down, report L (code $14). The same job as the 128K editor\nROM's BREAK_KEY. Called at $1030, $1E89, $2067 and $20A9.\nChanges: AF.","comment":"Half-row SPACE to B"},
        "10987": {"comment":"SPACE up: carry"},
        "10989": {"comment":"Half-row CAPS SHIFT to V"},
        "10993": {"comment":"CAPS SHIFT up: carry"},
        "10995": {"comment":"Both down: report L, BREAK into program"},
        "10999": {"synopsis":"RETURN (class $0E): RETURN #s,v sets the numeric variable v to the 32-bit value the channel\nof stream s gives for function 4 with B = 0 (RETURN_STREAM); otherwise the statement's end\nand RETURN_CMD.","comment":"ROM 3's GET_CHAR: '#'?"},
        "11004": {"comment":"The statement's end"},
        "11007": {"comment":"The ordinary RETURN"},
        "11010": {"synopsis":"RETURN #s,v: the stream and the variable (STREAM_AND_VAR), B = 0, then STREAM_VALUE.","comment":"The stream and the variable"},
        "11013": {"comment":"B = 0"},
        "11015": {"synopsis":"The current channel's function 4 (ROM 2's ROM0_392D_4, $0062) with B as set by the caller (0\nfor RETURN #, 2 for DIM #): it gives DE and HL, stacked as HL + 65536 x DE by the calculator\ncode at CALC_HI_LO (run through RUN_ON_STACK) and assigned to the variable (ROM 3's LET at\n$2AFF).","comment":"ROM 2's ROM0_392D_4: DE, HL"},
        "11020": {"comment":"DE kept"},
        "11021": {"comment":"BC = HL"},
        "11023": {"comment":"ROM 3's STACK_BC: the low word"},
        "11026": {"comment":"BC = DE"},
        "11027": {"comment":"ROM 3's STACK_BC: the high word"},
        "11030": {"comment":"The calculator code"},
        "11033": {"comment":"10 bytes"},
        "11036": {"comment":"Run: low + 65536 x high"},
        "11039": {"comment":"Assigned (ROM 3's LET)"},
        "11043": {"synopsis":"Reads '#s,v' for DIM #, NEXT # and RETURN #: past the '#', a number (ROM 3's CLASS_6), ','\n(report C otherwise, $22AD), a variable (ROM 3's CLASS_1) that must be numeric (FLAGS bit 6,\nreport C otherwise); the statement's end, its return kept round it; running, stream s made\ncurrent (ROM 3's FIND_INT1, CHAN_OPEN).","comment":"Past the '#'"},
        "11044": {"comment":"ROM 3's CLASS_6: the stream"},
        "11047": {"comment":"ROM 3's GET_CHAR: ','?"},
        "11050": {"comment":"No: report C"},
        "11053": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "11054": {"comment":"ROM 3's CLASS_1: the variable"},
        "11057": {"comment":"Numeric (FLAGS bit 6)?"},
        "11061": {"comment":"No: report C"},
        "11064": {"comment":"The return kept round the end"},
        "11065": {"comment":"The statement's end"},
        "11069": {"comment":"ROM 3's FIND_INT1: A = the stream"},
        "11072": {"comment":"ROM 3's CHAN_OPEN"},
        "11076": {"synopsis":"Calculator code run through RUN_ON_STACK by STREAM_VALUE (10 bytes): RST $28, stk-data\n($34; $40 $41 $00 $00, 65536), multiply ($04), addition ($0F), end-calc ($38), RET: the two\nnumbers on the stack (low, high) become low + 65536 x high."},
        "11086": {"synopsis":"Back to RAM bank 0 (paging byte $10: ROM 1, bank 0, normal screen, through PAGE_WRITE) and\nto the stack kept in $5B6A, which in turn keeps this one: the pair of BANK7_STACK. The same\njob as ROM 0's BANK0_STACK, with this ROM's paging byte. The return address goes with the\ncaller; AF and HL kept (HL through $5B58).\nChanges: AF'.","comment":"A kept in A'"},
        "11087": {"comment":"Paging byte $10: ROM 1, bank 0"},
        "11089": {"comment":"Interrupts off while the stack changes"},
        "11090": {"comment":"Paged in"},
        "11093": {"comment":"AF = the return address"},
        "11094": {"comment":"HL kept"},
        "11097": {"comment":"The other stack swapped in"},
        "11100": {"comment":"$5B6A = this stack"},
        "11104": {"comment":"SP = the other"},
        "11106": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "11109": {"comment":"The return address back"},
        "11110": {"comment":"A back"},
        "11112": {"synopsis":"Writes A to port $7FFD and to the paging byte at $5B5C. Keeps BC.","comment":"BC kept"},
        "11113": {"comment":"Port $7FFD"},
        "11118": {"comment":"Its copy"},
        "11123": {"synopsis":"Swaps the stack with the one kept in $5B6A, then pages RAM bank 7 in at $C000 (paging byte\n$17: ROM 1, bank 7, PAGE_WRITE). The same job as ROM 0's BANK7_STACK. The return address\ngoes with the caller; AF and HL kept (HL through $5B58).\nChanges: AF'.","comment":"A kept in A'"},
        "11124": {"comment":"No interrupts while the stack changes"},
        "11125": {"comment":"AF = the return address"},
        "11126": {"comment":"HL kept"},
        "11129": {"comment":"The other stack swapped in"},
        "11132": {"comment":"$5B6A = this stack"},
        "11136": {"comment":"SP = the other"},
        "11137": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "11140": {"comment":"The return address back"},
        "11141": {"comment":"Paging byte $17: ROM 1, bank 7"},
        "11146": {"comment":"Interrupts on"},
        "11147": {"comment":"A back"},
        "11149": {"synopsis":"Runs COPY \"name\" TO ... (from COPY's syntax at $221B, $223D, $2266, with the name or names\nalready in bank 7 at $ED01, each ended by $FF). A and the flags say which:\n- A = 0, Z and carry: COPY \"source\" TO \"destination\" (COPY_TO_FILE); the destination's name\n  is first at $ED01, the source's after it.\n- A = 0, Z, no carry: COPY \"file\" TO SPECTRUM FORMAT (COPY_TO_FILE, then COPY_SPECTRUM).\n- A = $AA (SCREEN$) or $E0 (LPRINT), NZ: the file's bytes printed on stream 2 or 3: opened\n  as file 0 for reading, read a byte at a time ($0118) until end of file ($19), each printed\n  through ROM 3's PRINT_A; for SCREEN$ the control codes other than ENTER become spaces.\nA is kept at $C00C (bank 7). +3DOS errors go to DOS_FAIL.\nExit: bank 0 and the machine stack (BANK0_STACK).","comment":"Bank 7 and its stack"},
        "11152": {"comment":"$C00C = the kind"},
        "11155": {"comment":"Flags kept"},
        "11156": {"comment":"A file, or SCREEN$: stream 2"},
        "11158": {"comment":"LPRINT?"},
        "11160": {"comment":"Stream 3"},
        "11164": {"synopsis":"Stream 2, the upper screen."},
        "11166": {"synopsis":"The stream opened in bank 0 (ROM 3's STREAM_SELECT), then bank 7 again; Z goes on at\nCOPY_TO_FILE.","comment":"Bank 0 for ROM 3"},
        "11169": {"comment":"ROM 3's STREAM_SELECT"},
        "11172": {"comment":"Bank 7 again"},
        "11175": {"comment":"Z: to a file"},
        "11178": {"comment":"The name at $ED01"},
        "11181": {"comment":"File 0, reading"},
        "11184": {"comment":"Open it; with a header if it has one"},
        "11190": {"comment":"+3DOS $0106, OPEN_BY_NAME"},
        "11198": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "11201": {"synopsis":"One byte of the file, by +3DOS $0118 (FILE_READ_BYTE): C = the byte, or the end of the file.","comment":"File 0"},
        "11206": {"comment":"+3DOS $0118, FILE_READ_BYTE"},
        "11214": {"comment":"A byte?"},
        "11216": {"comment":"Not end of file ($19): an error"},
        "11223": {"synopsis":"For SCREEN$, codes below $20 other than ENTER become a space.","comment":"SCREEN$?"},
        "11228": {"comment":"A = the byte"},
        "11231": {"comment":"ENTER kept"},
        "11235": {"comment":"Below $20?"},
        "11239": {"comment":"A space instead"},
        "11241": {"synopsis":"The byte printed in bank 0 (ROM 3's PRINT_A); bank 7 again for the next.","comment":"Bank 0"},
        "11244": {"comment":"ROM 3's PRINT_A"},
        "11247": {"comment":"Bank 7 again"},
        "11252": {"synopsis":"End of the file: file 0 closed (+3DOS $0109), bank 0, done.","comment":"File 0"},
        "11257": {"comment":"+3DOS $0109, CLOSE_FILE"},
        "11265": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "11268": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "11272": {"synopsis":"COPY to a file (Z), bank 7 paged in, carry kept on the stack for the SPECTRUM FORMAT test:\n1. $C002 = $ED01, the destination's name, copied to $C010 (COPY_NAME); the source's name\n   follows it.\n2. The default drive (+3DOS $012D with A = $FF) into $C005 and $C004, the destination's and\n   the source's drives, unless a name starts with a drive (SKIP_DRIVE, DRIVE_LETTER).\n3. No carry: COPY_SPECTRUM. Otherwise $C000 = the source's name, copied to $C022.","comment":"Carry kept: SPECTRUM FORMAT when clear"},
        "11273": {"comment":"The destination's name"},
        "11276": {"comment":"$C002 = its address"},
        "11279": {"comment":"Copied to $C010"},
        "11285": {"comment":"HL = the source's name, after it"},
        "11286": {"comment":"$FF: read the default drive"},
        "11291": {"comment":"+3DOS $012D, DRIVE_DEFAULT"},
        "11299": {"comment":"Both drives the default for now"},
        "11305": {"comment":"A drive in the destination's name?"},
        "11313": {"comment":"Its letter into $C005"},
        "11319": {"synopsis":"HL = the source's name; no carry goes to COPY_SPECTRUM; otherwise $C000 = the source's name,\ncopied to $C022, with its drive letter into $C004.","comment":"The source's name"},
        "11320": {"comment":"Carry back"},
        "11321": {"comment":"No carry: TO SPECTRUM FORMAT"},
        "11324": {"comment":"$C000 = the source's name"},
        "11327": {"comment":"Copied to $C022"},
        "11333": {"comment":"A drive in the source's name?"},
        "11341": {"comment":"Its letter into $C004"},
        "11347": {"synopsis":"The copy begins:\n1. SCR_CT set non-zero (from A), so the listing does not stop to ask 'scroll?'; a new line.\n2. $C00B (wildcard seen), $C00F (files copied) and $C00C cleared.\n3. A wildcard in the destination is report code $49 'Destination cannot be wild'.\n4. The temporary file's name M:VAXNSUZ.$$$ (TEMP_NAME) to $C04E.\n5. No wildcard in the source: one file (COPY_ONE), then COPY_FILES_DONE. With one:\n   COPY_WILD.","comment":"SCR_CT: no 'scroll?' for a while"},
        "11350": {"comment":"A new line"},
        "11353": {"comment":"No wildcard yet"},
        "11357": {"comment":"No files copied"},
        "11363": {"comment":"The destination"},
        "11366": {"comment":"A ? or * in it?"},
        "11375": {"comment":"Bank 0 for the report"},
        "11378": {"comment":"Report code $49, Destination cannot be wild"},
        "11382": {"synopsis":"The temporary file's name to $C04E (14 bytes, TEMP_NAME); a wildcard in the source?","comment":"M:VAXNSUZ.$$$ and $FF"},
        "11393": {"comment":"The source"},
        "11396": {"comment":"A ? or * in it?"},
        "11403": {"comment":"Wild: many files"},
        "11405": {"comment":"One file"},
        "11408": {"comment":"Then the count"},
        "11411": {"synopsis":"A wild source: the destination must be a drive alone (report code $4A otherwise); then the\nmatching files, two catalogue slots at a time.","comment":"The destination's name"},
        "11414": {"comment":"Past its drive"},
        "11417": {"comment":"Nothing after the drive?"},
        "11422": {"comment":"Bank 0 for the report"},
        "11425": {"comment":"Report code $4A, Destination must be drive"},
        "11429": {"synopsis":"The second catalogue slot ($C041) cleared, so the first search starts from no name.","comment":"Slot 2, 13 bytes"},
        "11435": {"synopsis":"One byte cleared."},
        "11439": {"synopsis":"The last name found ($C041) into the first slot ($C034), and the next matching file looked\nfor: +3DOS $011E (CATALOGUE) with two slots. The first search must find one (+3DOS error $17\notherwise); the next is copied (COPY_CAT_FOUND); none left is COPY_FILES_DONE.","comment":"The last name found"},
        "11442": {"comment":"Into slot 1, where the search starts"},
        "11450": {"comment":"The source's pattern"},
        "11453": {"comment":"B = 2 slots, C = 0"},
        "11456": {"comment":"The buffer"},
        "11462": {"comment":"+3DOS $011E, CATALOGUE"},
        "11470": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "11473": {"comment":"The first search?"},
        "11478": {"comment":"No: on"},
        "11480": {"comment":"Not any more"},
        "11482": {"comment":"+3DOS error $17 if none at all"},
        "11484": {"comment":"B = 1: only slot 1, nothing found?"},
        "11488": {"comment":"B back"},
        "11489": {"synopsis":"B - 1 = names found after the first slot: none is COPY_FILES_DONE. Otherwise the name in\nslot 2 (8 characters to a space, '.', 3 more, $FF) goes after the source's drive in $C022,\nthe destination is cut back to its drive, and the file copied (COPY_ONE); then the next.","comment":"None after slot 1: done"},
        "11492": {"comment":"The source's name"},
        "11495": {"comment":"Past its drive"},
        "11498": {"comment":"DE = where the name goes"},
        "11499": {"comment":"Slot 2's name"},
        "11502": {"comment":"Up to 8 characters"},
        "11507": {"comment":"Slot 2's type"},
        "11510": {"comment":"A '.'"},
        "11514": {"comment":"Up to 3 characters"},
        "11519": {"comment":"$FF ends it"},
        "11522": {"comment":"The destination"},
        "11525": {"comment":"Past its drive"},
        "11528": {"comment":"Cut back to the drive alone"},
        "11530": {"comment":"This file copied"},
        "11533": {"comment":"The next"},
        "11536": {"synopsis":"Every file copied: the temporary file deleted (+3DOS $0124); then '  1 file copied.' or the\ncount and ' files copied.'; SCR_CT = $17; bank 0.","comment":"M:VAXNSUZ.$$$"},
        "11542": {"comment":"+3DOS $0124, FILE_DELETE"},
        "11550": {"comment":"The files copied"},
        "11553": {"comment":"Just one?"},
        "11554": {"comment":"MSG_1_COPIED"},
        "11559": {"comment":"The count back"},
        "11560": {"comment":"HL = the count"},
        "11563": {"comment":"A new line"},
        "11566": {"comment":"Leading zeros as spaces"},
        "11568": {"comment":"The count printed"},
        "11571": {"comment":"MSG_N_COPIED"},
        "11574": {"synopsis":"The message printed; SCR_CT = $17; bank 0.","comment":"The message"},
        "11577": {"comment":"SCR_CT = $17"},
        "11582": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "11586": {"synopsis":"Copies one file, the source's name at $C022 and the destination's at $C010 (bank 7):\n1. The same name both sides is report code $30 'File already exists'.\n2. A destination that is a drive alone gets the source's name after its drive.\n3. The free space of M: (+3DOS $0121), in K and 63 at most, times 1024 into $C007; under 2K\n   sets $C009 (no room for the temporary file) and SCR_CT = $FF.\n4. Two drives alone, neither M:, are copied whole (COPY_DISK); otherwise the file\n   (COPY_NAMED).\nThe copy goes through RAM bank 7 at $ED11, 2K at a time.","comment":"The destination"},
        "11589": {"comment":"The source"},
        "11592": {"synopsis":"The names compared, a character at a time, up to their $FF.","comment":"The same character?"},
        "11596": {"comment":"The end of both?"},
        "11601": {"comment":"Bank 0 for the report"},
        "11604": {"comment":"Report code $30, File already exists"},
        "11608": {"synopsis":"The next pair of characters."},
        "11612": {"synopsis":"The names differ: is the destination a drive alone?","comment":"The destination"},
        "11615": {"comment":"Past its drive"},
        "11619": {"comment":"Nothing after the drive?"},
        "11623": {"comment":"Where its name goes"},
        "11630": {"comment":"The source's name"},
        "11633": {"comment":"Past its drive"},
        "11636": {"comment":"DE = the destination's"},
        "11637": {"synopsis":"The source's name after the destination's drive, up to its $FF.","comment":"One character"},
        "11639": {"comment":"Its $FF copied: done?"},
        "11646": {"synopsis":"The room on M:, the RAM disk, for the temporary file: +3DOS $0121 (DRIVE_FREE) in K, 63 at\nmost, times 1024 into $C007.","comment":"Room on M: assumed"},
        "11650": {"comment":"Drive M:"},
        "11655": {"comment":"+3DOS $0121, DRIVE_FREE: HL = the K free on M:"},
        "11663": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "11666": {"comment":"Over 255K?"},
        "11670": {"comment":"63K at most"},
        "11673": {"synopsis":"Over 63K counts as 63K.","comment":"64K or more?"},
        "11681": {"synopsis":"HL = the K times 1024 into $C007; under 2K: SCR_CT = $FF and $C009 = 1, the copy goes\ndirect.","comment":"HL = K x 256"},
        "11684": {"comment":"x 4: bytes"},
        "11686": {"comment":"$C007 = the room in bytes"},
        "11689": {"comment":"2K, one buffer"},
        "11693": {"comment":"At least 2K?"},
        "11697": {"comment":"SCR_CT = $FF","synopsis":"No room on M: (DRIVE_FREE failed, or under 2K): SCR_CT = $FF and $C009 = 1, the copy goes\ndirect."},
        "11702": {"comment":"No room on M:"},
        "11707": {"synopsis":"$C00A (destination open) and $C006 (source ended) cleared; two drives alone, with no name\nafter either, are error $30 (File already exists; there is no whole-disk copy), through\nERROR_128 in bank 0.","comment":"Destination not open yet"},
        "11711": {"comment":"Source not ended"},
        "11714": {"comment":"The destination"},
        "11720": {"comment":"A name after its drive?"},
        "11725": {"comment":"The source"},
        "11731": {"comment":"A name after its drive?"},
        "11736": {"comment":"Bank 0 and the machine stack"},
        "11739": {"comment":"Error $30: no whole-disk copy"},
        "11743": {"synopsis":"A named file: SCR_CT = $FF; the source's name printed, padded with spaces to 17 columns.\nWith M: on either side or no room on M:, copied direct (COPY_DIRECT); otherwise through a\ntemporary file on M: (COPY_VIA_M).","comment":"The source's name"},
        "11753": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "11756": {"comment":"DE = its start"},
        "11757": {"comment":"HL = start, DE = past its end"},
        "11761": {"comment":"17 less the length"},
        "11766": {"synopsis":"One space."},
        "11774": {"comment":"The destination on M:?"},
        "11781": {"comment":"No room on M:?"},
        "11787": {"comment":"The source on M:?"},
        "11795": {"synopsis":"Direct: the source opened as file 0 for reading (no header kept apart: E = 2), the\ndestination's name printed and opened as file 1 for writing (D = 2, E = 4: created without a\nheader, an old one erased); then COPY_DIR_LOOP.","comment":"The source"},
        "11798": {"comment":"File 0, reading"},
        "11801": {"comment":"Open as it is, the header as data"},
        "11807": {"comment":"+3DOS $0106, OPEN_BY_NAME"},
        "11818": {"comment":"The destination"},
        "11822": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "11826": {"comment":"File 1, writing"},
        "11829": {"comment":"Create headerless; erase an old one"},
        "11835": {"comment":"+3DOS $0106, OPEN_BY_NAME"},
        "11846": {"comment":"The destination is open"},
        "11851": {"synopsis":"2K of file 0 read into bank 7 at $ED11 (+3DOS $0112, FILE_READ); at its end ($19) $C006 is\nset, file 0 closed and DE = the bytes read; the bytes written to file 1 (+3DOS $0115,\nFILE_WRITE); again until the end, then COPY_CLOSE_DEST.","comment":"File 0, bank 7"},
        "11854": {"comment":"2K"},
        "11857": {"comment":"At $ED11"},
        "11863": {"comment":"+3DOS $0112, FILE_READ"},
        "11871": {"comment":"All 2K read?"},
        "11873": {"comment":"Not end of file ($19): an error"},
        "11878": {"comment":"The source has ended"},
        "11883": {"comment":"DE = the bytes not read"},
        "11884": {"comment":"File 0"},
        "11889": {"comment":"+3DOS $0109, CLOSE_FILE"},
        "11901": {"comment":"DE = the bytes read"},
        "11910": {"synopsis":"All 2K read."},
        "11913": {"synopsis":"DE bytes from bank 7 at $ED11 to file 1, none when DE is 0.","comment":"Nothing to write?"},
        "11917": {"comment":"From $ED11"},
        "11920": {"comment":"File 1, bank 7"},
        "11926": {"comment":"+3DOS $0115, FILE_WRITE"},
        "11937": {"synopsis":"The source not ended: the next 2K; ended: COPY_CLOSE_DEST.","comment":"The source ended?"},
        "11947": {"synopsis":"Through M:: the source opened as file 0 for reading, as in COPY_DIRECT; then COPY_M_ROUND.","comment":"The source"},
        "11950": {"comment":"File 0, reading"},
        "11953": {"comment":"Open as it is, the header as data"},
        "11959": {"comment":"+3DOS $0106, OPEN_BY_NAME"},
        "11970": {"synopsis":"One round through the RAM disk: the temporary file (TEMP_NAME, $C04E) opened as file 2 for\nreading and writing, an old one erased; $C00D = 0. Then the source read into it 2K at a time\n(COPY_M_IN_LOOP) while the room on M: lasts, and written out to the destination\n(COPY_M_OUT).","comment":"M:VAXNSUZ.$$$"},
        "11973": {"comment":"File 2, reading and writing"},
        "11976": {"comment":"Create headerless; erase an old one"},
        "11982": {"comment":"+3DOS $0106, OPEN_BY_NAME"},
        "11993": {"comment":"No bytes in it yet"},
        "11999": {"synopsis":"2K of the source (file 0) into bank 7 at $ED11; at its end $C006 set, file 0 closed, DE =\nthe bytes read.","comment":"File 0, bank 7"},
        "12002": {"comment":"2K"},
        "12005": {"comment":"At $ED11"},
        "12011": {"comment":"+3DOS $0112, FILE_READ"},
        "12019": {"comment":"All 2K read?"},
        "12021": {"comment":"Not end of file ($19): an error"},
        "12026": {"comment":"The source has ended"},
        "12031": {"comment":"DE = the bytes not read"},
        "12032": {"comment":"File 0"},
        "12037": {"comment":"+3DOS $0109, CLOSE_FILE"},
        "12049": {"comment":"DE = the bytes read"},
        "12058": {"synopsis":"All 2K read."},
        "12061": {"synopsis":"DE bytes from $ED11 into the temporary file (file 2), none when DE is 0.","comment":"Nothing to write?"},
        "12066": {"comment":"From $ED11"},
        "12069": {"comment":"File 2, bank 7"},
        "12075": {"comment":"+3DOS $0115, FILE_WRITE"},
        "12087": {"synopsis":"$C00D += the bytes; another 2K while the source goes on and $C00D + 2K still fits the room\non M: ($C007).","comment":"The bytes in the temporary file"},
        "12094": {"comment":"And 2K more"},
        "12099": {"comment":"The room on M:"},
        "12102": {"comment":"The source ended?"},
        "12108": {"comment":"Another 2K still fits?"},
        "12112": {"synopsis":"The source's drive flushed (+3DOS $0142); the temporary file rewound (+3DOS $0136); the\ndestination opened as file 1 for writing, its name printed, when not open yet ($C00A).","comment":"The source's drive"},
        "12115": {"comment":"A capital"},
        "12120": {"comment":"+3DOS $0142, FLUSH_DRV_FILES"},
        "12131": {"comment":"File 2"},
        "12133": {"comment":"Pointer 0"},
        "12141": {"comment":"+3DOS $0136, FILE_POS_SET"},
        "12149": {"comment":"The destination open?"},
        "12155": {"comment":"The destination"},
        "12159": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "12163": {"comment":"File 1, writing"},
        "12166": {"comment":"Create headerless; erase an old one"},
        "12172": {"comment":"+3DOS $0106, OPEN_BY_NAME"},
        "12183": {"comment":"The destination is open"},
        "12188": {"synopsis":"2K of the temporary file into bank 7 at $ED11 and on to the destination (file 1), until\n$C00D, less 2K each time, runs out.","comment":"At $ED11"},
        "12191": {"comment":"2K"},
        "12194": {"comment":"File 2, bank 7"},
        "12200": {"comment":"+3DOS $0112, FILE_READ"},
        "12208": {"comment":"All 2K read?"},
        "12213": {"comment":"Not end of file ($19): an error"},
        "12218": {"comment":"HL = the bytes read"},
        "12224": {"synopsis":"DE = the bytes read, written to file 1.","comment":"DE = the bytes"},
        "12225": {"comment":"File 1, bank 7"},
        "12228": {"comment":"From $ED11"},
        "12234": {"comment":"+3DOS $0115, FILE_WRITE"},
        "12245": {"comment":"The bytes left"},
        "12248": {"comment":"Less 2K"},
        "12254": {"comment":"Fewer than 2K were left: done"},
        "12256": {"comment":"None left?"},
        "12263": {"synopsis":"The round done: the temporary file closed (+3DOS $0109), the destination's drive flushed\n(+3DOS $0142); another round until the source has ended, then the temporary file deleted\n(+3DOS $0124).","comment":"File 2"},
        "12268": {"comment":"+3DOS $0109, CLOSE_FILE"},
        "12276": {"comment":"The destination's drive"},
        "12279": {"comment":"A capital"},
        "12284": {"comment":"+3DOS $0142, FLUSH_DRV_FILES"},
        "12295": {"comment":"The source ended?"},
        "12302": {"comment":"M:VAXNSUZ.$$$"},
        "12308": {"comment":"+3DOS $0124, FILE_DELETE"},
        "12316": {"synopsis":"The destination (file 1) closed (+3DOS $0109), a new line, and one more file counted in\n$C00F.","comment":"File 1"},
        "12321": {"comment":"+3DOS $0109, CLOSE_FILE"},
        "12332": {"comment":"A new line"},
        "12335": {"comment":"One more file copied"},
        "12340": {"synopsis":"Looks through the name at HL, up to its $FF, for a ? or *: either sets $C00B to 1 (bank 7).\nEntry: HL = the name.\nExit: HL past the $FF.\nThe DJNZ goes back to the LD B, which sets 17 again, so the count never runs out and the\nerror $14 at $3052 is never reached.\nChanges: AF, B, HL.","comment":"Reset by the DJNZ too"},
        "12342": {"comment":"A ?"},
        "12347": {"comment":"A wildcard seen"},
        "12354": {"synopsis":"A *?","comment":"A *?"},
        "12358": {"comment":"A wildcard seen"},
        "12365": {"synopsis":"The next character; $FF ends the name."},
        "12366": {"comment":"$FF: the end?"},
        "12368": {"comment":"Back to $3034: B is 17 again"},
        "12370": {"comment":"+3DOS error $14, never reached"},
        "12375": {"synopsis":"Copies up to B characters from HL to DE, stopping at a space (catalogue names are padded\nwith spaces).\nExit: HL and DE past the last copied.\nChanges: AF, B, DE, HL.","comment":"A space ends it"},
        "12385": {"synopsis":"The drive letter before the ':' (HL is past it, from SKIP_DRIVE) into (DE), as a capital,\nwhen it is one of A-Z.\nChanges: AF, HL.","comment":"Back to the character before ':'"},
        "12387": {"comment":"Its capital"},
        "12396": {"comment":"Kept as the drive"},
        "12398": {"synopsis":"Looks for a ':' among the first three characters of the name at HL.\nExit: Z with HL past the ':' when one is there; NZ with HL at the name's start when none (or\nthe $FF comes first). DE = the start.\nChanges: AF, B, DE, HL.","comment":"DE = the start"},
        "12400": {"comment":"Empty name?"},
        "12406": {"synopsis":"One character: ':'? $FF?","comment":"A ':'?"},
        "12411": {"comment":"The $FF?"},
        "12417": {"synopsis":"No drive: NZ, HL = the start.","comment":"NZ"},
        "12419": {"comment":"HL = the start"},
        "12421": {"synopsis":"Z, HL past the ':'."},
        "12423": {"synopsis":"Copies the name at HL to DE, up to and including its $FF.\nExit: HL and DE past the $FF.\nThe DJNZ goes back to the LD B, which sets 17 again, so the error $14 at $3092 is never\nreached.\nChanges: AF, B, DE, HL.","comment":"Reset by the DJNZ too"},
        "12429": {"comment":"The $FF copied?"},
        "12432": {"comment":"Back to $3087: B is 17 again"},
        "12434": {"comment":"+3DOS error $14, never reached"},
        "12439": {"synopsis":"Done."},
        "12440": {"synopsis":"Clears the screen (ROM 3's CLS_CMD) and selects stream 2 (ROM 3's STREAM_SELECT). Nothing in\nthis ROM calls it or jumps here.","comment":"ROM 3's CLS_CMD"},
        "12443": {"comment":"Stream 2"},
        "12445": {"comment":"ROM 3's STREAM_SELECT"},
        "12449": {"synopsis":"COPY \"name\" TO SPECTRUM FORMAT, with the name at $C010 (bank 7):\n1. A wildcard in it is report code $49.\n2. Its type replaced by '.HED' (HED_TYPE): the 4 characters go over the '.', or over the $FF\n   when it has no type.\n3. The file opened as file 0 for reading (E = 1, with its header if it has one), the new\n   name as file 1 for writing with a new header (D = 1), an old one erased (E = 4).\n4. Copied a byte at a time (+3DOS $0118, $011B), counted in $C00D.\n5. File 0 closed, the drive at $C005 flushed; the new file's header (+3DOS $010F) made CODE:\n   type 3, the length $C00D, the address 0; file 1 closed; bank 0.\nFrom COPY_TO_FILE with carry clear.","comment":"No wildcard yet"},
        "12450": {"comment":"Destination not open"},
        "12456": {"comment":"The name"},
        "12459": {"comment":"A ? or * in it?"},
        "12468": {"comment":"Bank 0 for the report"},
        "12471": {"comment":"Report code $49, Destination cannot be wild"},
        "12475": {"synopsis":"The '.' or the $FF in the name."},
        "12478": {"comment":"Not used: no DJNZ follows"},
        "12480": {"synopsis":"One character: '.'? $FF?","comment":"A '.'?"},
        "12486": {"comment":"The $FF?"},
        "12489": {"synopsis":"Back onto it; '.HED' written there (4 bytes); then the two files opened.","comment":"Back onto the '.' or $FF"},
        "12490": {"comment":"DE = where the type goes"},
        "12491": {"comment":"'.HED'"},
        "12499": {"comment":"The name as given"},
        "12502": {"comment":"File 0, reading"},
        "12505": {"comment":"With its header if it has one"},
        "12511": {"comment":"+3DOS $0106, OPEN_BY_NAME"},
        "12522": {"comment":"The name with .HED"},
        "12525": {"comment":"File 1, writing"},
        "12528": {"comment":"Create with a header; erase an old one"},
        "12534": {"comment":"+3DOS $0106, OPEN_BY_NAME"},
        "12545": {"comment":"The destination is open"},
        "12550": {"comment":"No bytes yet"},
        "12556": {"synopsis":"One byte from file 0 (+3DOS $0118, FILE_READ_BYTE); end of file ($19) is SPEC_HEADER.","comment":"File 0"},
        "12561": {"comment":"+3DOS $0118, FILE_READ_BYTE"},
        "12569": {"comment":"A byte?"},
        "12571": {"comment":"Not end of file ($19): an error"},
        "12576": {"comment":"End of file"},
        "12578": {"synopsis":"The byte (C) to file 1 (+3DOS $011B, FILE_WRITE_BYTE), $C00D counting; the next.","comment":"File 1, the byte in C"},
        "12583": {"comment":"+3DOS $011B, FILE_WRITE_BYTE"},
        "12591": {"comment":"One more byte"},
        "12598": {"comment":"Written: the next"},
        "12600": {"comment":"Failed: an error"},
        "12603": {"synopsis":"File 0 closed; the drive at $C005 flushed; file 1's header made CODE, length $C00D, address\n0; file 1 closed; bank 0.","comment":"File 0"},
        "12608": {"comment":"+3DOS $0109, CLOSE_FILE"},
        "12619": {"comment":"The drive"},
        "12625": {"comment":"+3DOS $0142, FLUSH_DRV_FILES"},
        "12633": {"comment":"File 1"},
        "12638": {"comment":"+3DOS $010F, HEADER_BYTES: IX at them"},
        "12649": {"comment":"Type 3, CODE"},
        "12654": {"comment":"The length"},
        "12663": {"comment":"The address 0"},
        "12670": {"comment":"File 1"},
        "12675": {"comment":"+3DOS $0109, CLOSE_FILE"},
        "12686": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "12690": {"synopsis":"'.HED' and $FF: COPY_SPECTRUM's new type. It copies only the first 4 bytes."},
        "12695": {"synopsis":"A +3DOS call failed, or COPY found an error, with the +3DOS error number in A (bank 7 paged\nin):\n1. Files 2, 1 and 0 closed (+3DOS $0109), each abandoned (+3DOS $010C) when closing fails.\n2. A new line; the destination ($C010) deleted when it was opened ($C00A), and the temporary\n   file M:VAXNSUZ.$$$ deleted (+3DOS $0124).\n3. Bank 0, stream 2 (ROM 3's STREAM_SELECT), then the report from the +3DOS error through\n   $0EB6 (the byte $FF after the CALL tells it to use A).\nNothing returns.","comment":"The error kept"},
        "12696": {"comment":"Files 2, 1 and 0"},
        "12698": {"synopsis":"File B - 1 closed; abandoned when that fails.","comment":"The count kept"},
        "12699": {"comment":"B = the file"},
        "12704": {"comment":"+3DOS $0109, CLOSE_FILE"},
        "12713": {"comment":"Closed?"},
        "12718": {"comment":"+3DOS $010C, CLOSE_NO_WRITE"},
        "12726": {"synopsis":"The next file down."},
        "12729": {"comment":"A new line"},
        "12732": {"comment":"Was the destination opened?"},
        "12738": {"comment":"Its name"},
        "12744": {"comment":"+3DOS $0124, FILE_DELETE"},
        "12752": {"synopsis":"The temporary file deleted; bank 0, stream 2, and the report.","comment":"M:VAXNSUZ.$$$"},
        "12758": {"comment":"+3DOS $0124, FILE_DELETE"},
        "12766": {"comment":"The error back"},
        "12767": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "12770": {"comment":"The report for +3DOS error A"},
        "12774": {"synopsis":"Prints the characters at HL through RST $10, bit 7 cleared, up to a $00 or $FF (not\nprinted); codes below $20 are skipped.\nExit: HL past the end.\nChanges: AF, HL.","comment":"The next character"},
        "12776": {"comment":"$00 ends it"},
        "12778": {"comment":"$FF ends it"},
        "12781": {"comment":"Bit 7 off"},
        "12783": {"comment":"A control code? Skipped"},
        "12790": {"synopsis":"Waits for a key: clears FLAGS bit 5, waits until the interrupt sets it again, and takes\nLAST_K. Nothing in this ROM calls it or jumps here.\nExit: A = the key.\nChanges: AF, HL.","comment":"FLAGS"},
        "12793": {"comment":"No key yet"},
        "12795": {"synopsis":"Until FLAGS bit 5 says a key came.","comment":"A new key?"},
        "12799": {"comment":"Taken"},
        "12801": {"comment":"LAST_K"},
        "12805": {"synopsis":"The temporary file COPY uses on the RAM disk: 'M:VAXNSUZ.$$$' and $FF, 14 bytes, copied to\n$C04E (bank 7) by COPY_TEMP_NAME."},
        "12819": {"synopsis":"Called before each +3DOS call (CALL $3F00), with bank 7 paged in: $5B7D-$5BFF (131 bytes)\nsaved to $E77D-$E7FF in bank 7 and the stack moved to $5BFF, its old place kept at $E602;\nthe return address moved with it. AF, BC, DE and HL kept (through $E606-$E60C). Interrupts\non at the end. DOS_STACK_BACK undoes it.","comment":"No interrupts while the stack moves"},
        "12820": {"comment":"HL kept"},
        "12823": {"comment":"AF kept"},
        "12828": {"comment":"DE kept"},
        "12832": {"comment":"BC kept"},
        "12836": {"comment":"$5B7D-$5BFF"},
        "12839": {"comment":"To $E77D-$E7FF"},
        "12845": {"comment":"Copied, top down"},
        "12847": {"comment":"BC = the return address"},
        "12848": {"comment":"The stack's place kept"},
        "12852": {"comment":"SP = $5BFF"},
        "12856": {"comment":"The return address on it"},
        "12857": {"comment":"BC back"},
        "12861": {"comment":"DE back"},
        "12865": {"comment":"AF back"},
        "12870": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "12875": {"synopsis":"Called after each +3DOS call: $5B7D-$5BFF copied back from $E77D-$E7FF (bank 7) and the\nstack put back from $E602, the return address moved with it ($E604). AF, BC, DE and HL kept,\nso the call's carry and A come through. Interrupts on at the end.","comment":"No interrupts while the stack moves"},
        "12876": {"comment":"HL kept"},
        "12879": {"comment":"AF kept"},
        "12884": {"comment":"DE kept"},
        "12888": {"comment":"BC kept"},
        "12892": {"comment":"The return address kept"},
        "12896": {"comment":"$E77D-$E7FF"},
        "12899": {"comment":"Back to $5B7D-$5BFF"},
        "12907": {"comment":"The old stack back"},
        "12911": {"comment":"The return address on it"},
        "12915": {"comment":"BC back"},
        "12919": {"comment":"DE back"},
        "12923": {"comment":"AF back"},
        "12928": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "12933": {"synopsis":"COPY EXP [INVERSE] (from COPY's syntax at $21B7): the screen to the printer as a grey-scale\npicture, turned sideways:\n1. $ED16 (bank 7) = 0, or $FC after INVERSE, which flips the dots.\n2. $10B0: syntax checking ends here.\n3. Bit 4 of port $1FFD (and $5B67) set; bank 7, interrupts off; $1B '3' and the byte at\n   $5B7B sent (PRINTER_BYTE).\n4. The 32 character columns from the right ($401F down), each in 4 passes of 2 pixel columns\n   (D = 1, 4, 16, 64): a pass sends DUMP_LINE_CODES, then the 192 pixel rows from the top, 4\n   bytes each (DUMP_BYTE).\n5. $1B '@'; interrupts on; bank 0.","comment":"No INVERSE yet"},
        "12934": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "12937": {"comment":"$ED16 = the dot flip"},
        "12940": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "12943": {"comment":"ROM 3's NEXT_SKIP: after EXP"},
        "12946": {"comment":"INVERSE?"},
        "12950": {"comment":"The dots flipped"},
        "12958": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "12961": {"synopsis":"The next character.","comment":"ROM 3's NEXT_SKIP"},
        "12964": {"synopsis":"The statement's end ($10B0); running: the picture printed.","comment":"Syntax checking ends here"},
        "12967": {"comment":"Bit 4 of port $1FFD set"},
        "12982": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "12986": {"comment":"$1B '3' and $5B7B"},
        "13003": {"comment":"Top right of the screen"},
        "13006": {"comment":"32 character columns"},
        "13008": {"synopsis":"One character column, from the right: D = 1, the first pass.","comment":"The column kept"},
        "13009": {"comment":"Pixel mask: bits 0 and 1"},
        "13011": {"synopsis":"One pass, two pixel columns: the line codes (CR, LF, $1B 'L', 768), then 192 rows."},
        "13013": {"comment":"DUMP_LINE_CODES"},
        "13021": {"comment":"The column's top kept"},
        "13022": {"synopsis":"One screen byte (DUMP_BYTE), then the next pixel row down: within the cell, the next cell\nrow, the next third, to $5800.","comment":"4 bytes for the 2 pixels"},
        "13025": {"comment":"The pixel row in the cell"},
        "13028": {"comment":"Down one"},
        "13029": {"comment":"Was it row 7?"},
        "13033": {"comment":"Back to the cell's top"},
        "13037": {"comment":"The next cell row"},
        "13041": {"comment":"Still in this third?"},
        "13043": {"comment":"The next third"},
        "13047": {"comment":"Past the bottom?"},
        "13051": {"comment":"The column's top"},
        "13052": {"comment":"The next two pixel columns"},
        "13056": {"comment":"Four passes done?"},
        "13058": {"comment":"The column"},
        "13059": {"comment":"The next one left"},
        "13063": {"comment":"$1B '@'"},
        "13073": {"comment":"Interrupts on"},
        "13074": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "13078": {"synopsis":"Sends A to the printer through $2051, in bank 0 with interrupts on; then bank 7 again and\ninterrupts off.\nChanges: AF'.","comment":"Interrupts on for the printer"},
        "13079": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "13082": {"comment":"A to the printer"},
        "13085": {"comment":"Bank 7 again"},
        "13090": {"synopsis":"Sends the bytes at HL to the printer (PRINTER_BYTE) up to a $FF.","comment":"The next byte"},
        "13091": {"comment":"$FF ends them"},
        "13102": {"synopsis":"The 4 printer bytes for two pixels of the screen byte at HL, mask D and D x 2: each pixel's\ncolour (ink when set, paper when clear, BRIGHT adding 8) picks a 3 x 4 dot pattern from\nDUMP_GREY_DOTS; the first goes in bits 5-7, the second in bits 2-4 of the 4 bytes at $ED11\n(bank 7), which are sent XOR $ED16 (INVERSE).\nChanges: BC.","comment":"AF, HL and DE kept"},
        "13106": {"comment":"E = the cell's attribute"},
        "13110": {"comment":"$ED11-$ED14 cleared"},
        "13113": {"comment":"The first pixel's pattern"},
        "13116": {"comment":"Moved up 3"},
        "13119": {"comment":"The second pixel"},
        "13121": {"comment":"Its pattern"},
        "13124": {"comment":"Both moved up 2"},
        "13127": {"comment":"4 bytes"},
        "13132": {"synopsis":"One byte, XOR $ED16, to the printer."},
        "13135": {"comment":"The INVERSE flip"},
        "13139": {"comment":"To the printer"},
        "13151": {"synopsis":"E = the attribute of the cell holding the screen byte at HL; H becomes the attribute\naddress's high byte.\nChanges: E, H."},
        "13152": {"comment":"The third: bits 3-4 of H"},
        "13155": {"comment":"To bits 0-1"},
        "13161": {"comment":"$58 up: the attributes"},
        "13164": {"comment":"E = the attribute"},
        "13167": {"synopsis":"Clears the 4 bytes at $ED11."},
        "13173": {"synopsis":"One byte."},
        "13180": {"synopsis":"Shifts the 4 bytes at $ED11 left 3 bits each."},
        "13187": {"synopsis":"One byte."},
        "13199": {"synopsis":"Shifts the 4 bytes at $ED11 left 2 bits each."},
        "13204": {"synopsis":"One byte."},
        "13212": {"synopsis":"ORs the dot pattern of one pixel into the 4 bytes at $ED11: the pixel is (HL) AND D; set\ntakes the ink (E bits 0-2), clear the paper (bits 3-5); E bit 6 (BRIGHT) adds 8. The\ncolour's offset from DUMP_GREY_INDEX, its 4 bytes from DUMP_GREY_DOTS.\nChanges: AF, B."},
        "13214": {"comment":"Pixel set?"},
        "13216": {"comment":"A = the attribute"},
        "13217": {"comment":"Set: the ink"},
        "13219": {"comment":"Clear: the paper"},
        "13225": {"synopsis":"The colour in bits 0-2; BRIGHT adds 8.","comment":"The colour"},
        "13227": {"comment":"BRIGHT?"},
        "13231": {"comment":"8-15"},
        "13233": {"synopsis":"The pattern's offset (DUMP_GREY_INDEX), and its 4 bytes ORed in.","comment":"DUMP_GREY_INDEX"},
        "13240": {"comment":"E = the offset"},
        "13241": {"comment":"DUMP_GREY_DOTS"},
        "13245": {"comment":"4 bytes"},
        "13250": {"synopsis":"One byte ORed in."},
        "13260": {"synopsis":"DUMP_PIXEL's offsets into DUMP_GREY_DOTS for colours 0-15 (BRIGHT adding 8): 0, 4, 8 ... 60,\neach colour times 4."},
        "13276": {"synopsis":"COPY EXP's dot patterns, 4 bytes for each colour 0-15 (BRIGHT adding 8), 3 dots in bits 0-2\nof each: the darker the colour, the more dots. Black and bright black have all 12; white has\n7; bright white none."},
        "13340": {"synopsis":"Sent at the start of each pass of COPY EXP (PRINTER_CODES): CR, LF, $1B 'L' and the count\n$0300 (768 bytes, 192 rows of 4), ended by $FF."},
        "13347": {"synopsis":"CAT of the tape (from $065E, for a name starting 'T:'): lists the headers on the tape until\nBREAK (SPACE and CAPS SHIFT both down). Room for a 17-byte header made in the workspace (ROM\n3's WORK_ROOM) with IX at it; for each header loaded (ROM 3's LD_BYTES, flag 0) a line:\n- a program: the name in quotes, LINE and its number when it has one, '(BASIC)';\n- a number array: DATA and its letter with '()'; a string array: the letter with '$()';\n- otherwise CODE, the start and the length.\nA load that fails is tried again.","comment":"17 bytes"},
        "13350": {"comment":"ROM 3's WORK_ROOM"},
        "13353": {"comment":"IX = the header's room"},
        "13356": {"synopsis":"A new line, then the next header."},
        "13358": {"comment":"ROM 3's PRINT_A"},
        "13361": {"synopsis":"BREAK (SPACE and CAPS SHIFT both down) ends the list.","comment":"Half-row SPACE to B"},
        "13365": {"comment":"SPACE up?"},
        "13368": {"comment":"Half-row CAPS SHIFT to V"},
        "13372": {"comment":"CAPS SHIFT up?"},
        "13375": {"comment":"Both down: done"},
        "13376": {"synopsis":"A header from the tape: flag 0, 17 bytes, loading (ROM 3's LD_BYTES); failed: again.","comment":"Flag 0: a header"},
        "13378": {"comment":"17 bytes"},
        "13381": {"comment":"Load, not verify"},
        "13384": {"comment":"ROM 3's LD_BYTES"},
        "13389": {"comment":"Failed: again"},
        "13393": {"comment":"A quote"},
        "13398": {"comment":"10 characters of name"},
        "13400": {"synopsis":"One character of the name.","comment":"Header bytes 1-10"},
        "13412": {"comment":"Quote, space"},
        "13418": {"comment":"The type"},
        "13421": {"comment":"A program?"},
        "13425": {"comment":"Header byte 14, the line's high byte"},
        "13428": {"comment":"$80: no LINE?"},
        "13432": {"comment":"'LINE '"},
        "13438": {"comment":"The line number"},
        "13447": {"comment":"A space"},
        "13452": {"synopsis":"'(BASIC) ' and the next.","comment":"'(BASIC) '"},
        "13460": {"synopsis":"Type 1, a number array: 'DATA ', its letter (header byte 14), '() '.","comment":"Type 1?"},
        "13464": {"comment":"'DATA '"},
        "13470": {"comment":"The array's name byte"},
        "13473": {"comment":"As a capital letter"},
        "13480": {"comment":"'() '"},
        "13489": {"synopsis":"Type 2, a string array: 'DATA ', its letter, '$() '.","comment":"Type 2?"},
        "13493": {"comment":"'DATA '"},
        "13499": {"comment":"The array's name byte"},
        "13502": {"comment":"As a capital letter"},
        "13509": {"comment":"'$() '"},
        "13518": {"synopsis":"Any other type: 'CODE ', the start (header bytes 13-14), ',' and the length (bytes 11-12).","comment":"'CODE '"},
        "13524": {"comment":"The start"},
        "13533": {"comment":"A comma"},
        "13538": {"comment":"The length"},
        "13550": {"synopsis":"Prints the text at HL through ROM 3's PRINT_A, up to a $00.\nExit: HL at the $00.\nChanges: AF, HL.","comment":"The next character"},
        "13551": {"comment":"$00 ends it"},
        "13559": {"synopsis":"Prints BC as a number: ROM 3's STACK_BC, then PRINT_FP.","comment":"ROM 3's STACK_BC"},
        "13562": {"comment":"ROM 3's PRINT_FP"},
        "13566": {"synopsis":"TAPE_CAT's texts, each ended by $00: $34FE '\" ', $3501 '(BASIC) ', $350A 'DATA ', $3510\n'CODE ', $3516 '$() ' (and from $3517 '() '), $351B 'LINE '."},
        "13601": {"synopsis":"OPEN # (class $0C, after a number, ',' and a string): attaches stream s to the channel the\nstring names through ROM 2's STREAM_OPEN ($0056): \"K\", \"S\", \"P\" or a longer \"x>name\" channel\n(ROM 2 decides). A failure is reported with ROM 2's error code (STREAM_RESULT).","comment":"ROM 3's STK_FETCH: DE = the text, BC = its length"},
        "13604": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "13606": {"comment":"ROM 3's FIND_INT1: A = the stream"},
        "13609": {"comment":"Back"},
        "13611": {"comment":"ROM 2's STREAM_OPEN"},
        "13616": {"synopsis":"Carry clear after STREAM_OPEN or STREAM_CLOSE: error A (FILE_ERR_SET); carry set: done.","comment":"Failed: error A"},
        "13620": {"synopsis":"CLOSE # (class $0C, after a number): closes stream s through ROM 2's STREAM_CLOSE ($0059);\na failure is reported with its error code (STREAM_RESULT).","comment":"ROM 3's FIND_INT1: A = the stream"},
        "13623": {"comment":"ROM 2's STREAM_CLOSE"},
        "13628": {"comment":"Its result"},
        "13630": {"synopsis":"GO TO (class $0E): GO TO #s,p sets the position of stream s's channel to p (GO_TO_STREAM);\notherwise a number (ROM 3's CLASS_6), the statement's end and ROM 3's GO TO at $1E67.","comment":"ROM 3's GET_CHAR: '#'?"},
        "13633": {"comment":"Yes: GO_TO_STREAM"},
        "13635": {"comment":"ROM 3's CLASS_6: the line"},
        "13638": {"comment":"The statement's end"},
        "13641": {"comment":"ROM 3's GO TO"},
        "13645": {"synopsis":"GO TO #s,p: two numbers (NEXT_CLASS_8), the statement's end; p split into low and high\nwords by the calculator code at CALC_SPLIT (RUN_ON_STACK); stream s made current (ROM 3's\nCHAN_OPEN); then the channel's function 4 with B = 1, HL = the low word and DE = the high\n(ROM 2's ROM0_392D_4, $0062).","comment":"Past '#': the stream and the position"},
        "13648": {"comment":"The statement's end"},
        "13651": {"comment":"The calculator code"},
        "13654": {"comment":"13 bytes"},
        "13657": {"comment":"Run: p split, the stream on top"},
        "13660": {"comment":"ROM 3's FIND_INT1: A = the stream"},
        "13663": {"comment":"ROM 3's CHAN_OPEN"},
        "13666": {"comment":"ROM 3's FIND_INT2: the high word"},
        "13670": {"comment":"ROM 3's FIND_INT2: the low word"},
        "13674": {"comment":"HL = the low word"},
        "13675": {"comment":"DE = the high word"},
        "13676": {"comment":"B = 1"},
        "13678": {"comment":"ROM 2's ROM0_392D_4"},
        "13684": {"synopsis":"DISK_SETUP's \"Physical drives: \", $00."},
        "13702": {"synopsis":"DISK_SETUP's \" floppy, \", $00."},
        "13712": {"synopsis":"DISK_SETUP's \" IDE\" and \"Logical drives: \" as one text, $00-ended: \" IDE\" fills the line,\nso the second part starts a new one."},
        "13733": {"synopsis":"FORMAT_TO_RUN's question: \"Really format hard disk (Y/N)?\", $00."},
        "13764": {"synopsis":"MOVE_BIN's question: \"Really delete partition (Y/N)?\", $00."},
        "13795": {"synopsis":"The rest of REPORT_TABLE's messages, the last letter with bit 7 set: Invalid partition,\nPartition already exists, Not implemented, Partition open, Out of partition handles, Not a\nswap partition, Drive already mapped, Out of XDPBs, No swap partition, Invalid device (codes\n81-90, ERR_NR $50-$59)."},
        "13972": {"synopsis":"Prints the $00-ended question at HL (PRINT_TEXT_0) and waits for N or Y (FLAGS bit 5,\nLAST_K,\neither case); other keys are ignored. The lower screen is then cleared (ROM 3's CLS_LOWER).\nExit: A = 'N' or 'Y'.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"The question"},
        "13975": {"comment":"FLAGS bit 5: no key yet"},
        "13980": {"synopsis":"Until a key: N or Y?","comment":"A key?"},
        "13984": {"comment":"Taken"},
        "13986": {"comment":"LAST_K, as a capital"},
        "13991": {"comment":"N?"},
        "13995": {"comment":"Y?"},
        "13997": {"comment":"Neither: again"},
        "13999": {"synopsis":"N or Y: the lower screen cleared.","comment":"Kept"},
        "14000": {"comment":"ROM 3's CLS_LOWER"},
        "14005": {"synopsis":"FORMAT TO u,n[,m] running (from FORMAT_TO): asks \"Really format hard disk (Y/N)?\" (N ends);\nprobes unit u (ROM 2's HD_UNIT_PROBE, $01A2, into $ED11 in bank 7; error A unless it gives\n$42) and takes its cylinders (the probe's bytes 1 and 256), heads (byte 3) and sectors per\ntrack (byte 6); m, when not 0, must be below the cylinders (report B) and takes their place,\nwith bit 7 of the heads set; then ROM 2's PART_TABLE_NEW ($00B2) with A = u, BC = n, IX =\nthe cylinders, H = the heads and L = the sectors. A +3DOS error is reported through\nFILE_ERROR_A.","comment":"ROM 3's CLS_LOWER"},
        "14008": {"comment":"\"Really format hard disk (Y/N)?\""},
        "14014": {"comment":"The answer kept"},
        "14015": {"comment":"BC = 0: no m"},
        "14018": {"comment":"A third number ($5B66 bit 6)?"},
        "14025": {"comment":"ROM 3's FIND_INT2: BC = m"},
        "14028": {"synopsis":"n and u from the calculator stack; N ends here.","comment":"m kept"},
        "14029": {"comment":"ROM 3's FIND_INT2: BC = n"},
        "14032": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "14033": {"comment":"ROM 3's FIND_INT1: A = u"},
        "14036": {"comment":"C = u"},
        "14037": {"comment":"HL = n"},
        "14038": {"comment":"DE = m"},
        "14039": {"comment":"The answer: N?"},
        "14043": {"comment":"n, u and m kept"},
        "14046": {"comment":"The probe's bank: 7"},
        "14048": {"comment":"HL = the buffer"},
        "14051": {"comment":"Bank 7 and its stack"},
        "14054": {"comment":"Onto +3DOS's stack"},
        "14057": {"comment":"ROM 2's HD_UNIT_PROBE"},
        "14062": {"comment":"$42: the unit answered?"},
        "14064": {"comment":"Carry clear"},
        "14066": {"comment":"No: error A"},
        "14069": {"comment":"IX = the probe's bytes"},
        "14073": {"comment":"H = the heads"},
        "14076": {"comment":"L = the sectors per track"},
        "14079": {"comment":"E = the cylinders' low byte"},
        "14082": {"comment":"IX + 256"},
        "14084": {"comment":"D = the high byte"},
        "14087": {"comment":"Back to this ROM's stack"},
        "14090": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "14093": {"comment":"HL = m, the geometry kept"},
        "14094": {"comment":"m below the cylinders?"},
        "14097": {"comment":"No: report B"},
        "14100": {"comment":"m back: 0?"},
        "14103": {"comment":"Yes: all the cylinders"},
        "14105": {"comment":"DE = m"},
        "14106": {"comment":"The geometry"},
        "14107": {"comment":"Bit 7 of the heads set"},
        "14109": {"comment":"On"},
        "14111": {"synopsis":"m = 0: the geometry back, DE = the probe's cylinders.","comment":"The geometry"},
        "14112": {"synopsis":"The table laid out: ROM 2's PART_TABLE_NEW ($00B2) with A = u, BC = n, IX = the cylinders.","comment":"C = u"},
        "14113": {"comment":"A = u"},
        "14114": {"comment":"BC = n"},
        "14115": {"comment":"IX = the cylinders"},
        "14118": {"comment":"Bank 7 and its stack"},
        "14121": {"comment":"Onto +3DOS's stack"},
        "14124": {"comment":"ROM 2's PART_TABLE_NEW"},
        "14129": {"comment":"Back to this ROM's stack"},
        "14132": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "14135": {"comment":"Done"},
        "14136": {"synopsis":"A +3DOS error in A (FILE_ERROR_A with $FF). Also from CAT_TAB_FAIL.","comment":"Error A"},
        "14140": {"synopsis":"NEW (class $0E): NEW DATA \"name\",size or NEW EXP \"name\",size makes a hard disk partition\n(NEW_PARTITION); NEW alone is the statement's end and NEW_CMD.","comment":"ROM 3's GET_CHAR: DATA?"},
        "14145": {"comment":"EXP?"},
        "14149": {"comment":"The statement's end"},
        "14152": {"comment":"The ordinary NEW"},
        "14155": {"synopsis":"NEW DATA or NEW EXP: the token stacked (ROM 3's STACK_A), past it, the name (ROM 3's\nCLASS_A), ',' (report C otherwise) and the size in megabytes (ROM 3's CLASS_6); the\nstatement's end. Running: the size (FIND_INT2), the name (PART_NAME_ARG, which must name a\npartition: error $59 for a device) to $EF98 in bank 7, the token back: type 2 for EXP (a\nswap partition), 3 for DATA, at $EFA8. The size must be 1-16 (report B otherwise).","comment":"ROM 3's STACK_A: the token kept"},
        "14158": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "14159": {"comment":"ROM 3's CLASS_A: the name"},
        "14162": {"comment":"ROM 3's GET_CHAR: ','?"},
        "14165": {"comment":"No: report C"},
        "14168": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "14169": {"comment":"ROM 3's CLASS_6: the size"},
        "14172": {"comment":"The statement's end"},
        "14175": {"comment":"ROM 3's FIND_INT2: BC = the size"},
        "14178": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "14179": {"comment":"The name: a partition?"},
        "14182": {"comment":"A device: error $59"},
        "14185": {"comment":"D = the unit, kept"},
        "14186": {"comment":"ROM 3's FIND_INT1: A = the token"},
        "14189": {"comment":"Back"},
        "14190": {"comment":"HL = the size"},
        "14191": {"comment":"EXP?"},
        "14193": {"comment":"Type 2, a swap partition"},
        "14198": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "14200": {"comment":"DATA: type 3"},
        "14205": {"synopsis":"Bank 7: the type at $EFA8; the size checked: 1-16.","comment":"Bank 7 and its stack"},
        "14208": {"comment":"The type into the entry"},
        "14211": {"comment":"Size below 17?"},
        "14216": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "14218": {"synopsis":"Report B (code $0A, Integer out of range), in bank 0: a size out of range, or FORMAT TO's m\nnot below the cylinders.","comment":"Bank 0"},
        "14221": {"comment":"Report B: Integer out of range"},
        "14225": {"synopsis":"Size 0 is report B; otherwise the 29 bytes of PART_PARAMS to $EFB8 (the entry's bytes $20\nup, the drive's parameters) and the values that hang on the size: for 1-4 MB blocks of 2K\n(BSH 4, BLM $0F, EXM 0, AL0 $FF, size x 512 blocks); 5-8 MB 4K ($05, $1F, 1, $F0, size x\n256); 9-16 MB 8K ($06, $3F, 3, $C0, size x 128).","comment":"Size 0?"},
        "14227": {"comment":"Yes: report B"},
        "14229": {"comment":"The unit and the size kept"},
        "14231": {"comment":"PART_PARAMS"},
        "14234": {"comment":"To the entry's bytes $20 up"},
        "14237": {"comment":"29 bytes"},
        "14242": {"comment":"The size again"},
        "14244": {"comment":"DE = size x 256"},
        "14247": {"comment":"Up to 4 MB?"},
        "14252": {"comment":"Up to 8 MB?"},
        "14256": {"comment":"9-16: DE = size x 128"},
        "14260": {"comment":"BSH 6, BLM $3F"},
        "14263": {"comment":"EXM 3"},
        "14265": {"comment":"AL0 $C0"},
        "14269": {"synopsis":"5-8 MB: 4K blocks.","comment":"BSH 5, BLM $1F"},
        "14272": {"comment":"EXM 1"},
        "14274": {"comment":"AL0 $F0"},
        "14278": {"synopsis":"1-4 MB: 2K blocks, DE = size x 512.","comment":"DE = size x 512"},
        "14280": {"comment":"BSH 4, BLM $0F"},
        "14283": {"comment":"EXM 0"},
        "14285": {"comment":"AL0 $FF"},
        "14287": {"synopsis":"The values into the parameters: BSH and BLM at $EFBA, EXM at $EFBC, AL0 at $EFC1, the last\nblock (DE - 1) at $EFBD; $EFCA = size x 16 (low byte), for 16 MB $FF with the last block\n$07F7.","comment":"BSH, BLM"},
        "14291": {"comment":"AL0"},
        "14294": {"comment":"EXM"},
        "14298": {"comment":"DE = the last block"},
        "14299": {"comment":"B = the size"},
        "14300": {"comment":"A = size x 16"},
        "14301": {"synopsis":"Adding 16 for each megabyte.","comment":"16 more"},
        "14305": {"comment":"Wrapped to 0 (16 MB)?"},
        "14308": {"comment":"Then $FF"},
        "14309": {"comment":"... and the last block $07F7"},
        "14312": {"synopsis":"$EFCA and the last block set; the partition's last sector, size x 2048 - 1, at $EFAF-$EFB1;\nthen ROM 2's PART_NEW ($00B8) with the entry at $EF98.","comment":"$EFCA"},
        "14315": {"comment":"The last block"},
        "14319": {"comment":"HL = the size"},
        "14320": {"comment":"x 8"},
        "14323": {"comment":"Less 1"},
        "14324": {"comment":"The entry's last sector, high bytes"},
        "14327": {"comment":"Low byte $FF"},
        "14332": {"comment":"A = the unit"},
        "14334": {"comment":"HL = the entry"},
        "14337": {"comment":"Onto +3DOS's stack"},
        "14340": {"comment":"ROM 2's PART_NEW"},
        "14345": {"comment":"Back to this ROM's stack"},
        "14348": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "14350": {"comment":"A = the unit"},
        "14351": {"comment":"Filled with $E5"},
        "14353": {"comment":"Blocks $1F down to 0: the directory"},
        "14357": {"comment":"Onto +3DOS's stack"},
        "14360": {"comment":"ROM 2's PART_ERASE"},
        "14365": {"synopsis":"Back to this ROM's stack, then NEW_PART_DONE (also FORMAT_TO_RUN's failed probe).","comment":"Back to this ROM's stack"},
        "14368": {"synopsis":"Bank 0; carry: done; otherwise the +3DOS error in A (FILE_ERROR_A).","comment":"Bank 0"},
        "14371": {"comment":"Done"},
        "14372": {"comment":"Error A"},
        "14376": {"synopsis":"Takes a partition or device name from the calculator stack (ROM 3's STK_FETCH): \"u>name\"\nwith u 0 or 1 is a partition of hard disk unit u, a name without \">\" one of unit 0, \"2>\" to\n\"4>\" a device. An empty name is error $2C; a digit from 5 (or not a digit) error $59.\nExit: a partition: Z, D = the unit, the name (BC characters) at $EF98 in bank 7 with 16\nspaces after it; a device: NZ, carry, D = 2-4.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"ROM 3's STK_FETCH"},
        "14379": {"comment":"Empty?"},
        "14383": {"comment":"Error $2C: Bad filename"},
        "14387": {"synopsis":"A '>' second: the first is the unit or device.","comment":"The second character"},
        "14390": {"comment":"'>'?"},
        "14392": {"comment":"Unit 0 when not"},
        "14396": {"comment":"The digit"},
        "14397": {"comment":"Past \"u>\""},
        "14399": {"comment":"Two characters less"},
        "14401": {"comment":"0?"},
        "14405": {"comment":"1?"},
        "14409": {"comment":"D = 2-4: a device"},
        "14410": {"comment":"Below 5: return, NZ and carry"},
        "14413": {"synopsis":"Stops with error $59 (Invalid device): a unit digit from 5, or a device where a partition is\nneeded.","comment":"Error $59: Invalid device"},
        "14417": {"synopsis":"A partition of unit A: the name to $EF98 in bank 7 (COPY_TO_BANK7). A = the length, 16 at\nmost, but BC keeps the whole length.","comment":"The unit kept"},
        "14418": {"comment":"BC = the length"},
        "14421": {"comment":"Over 16?"},
        "14425": {"comment":"A = 16 (not used further)"},
        "14427": {"synopsis":"The name copied; 16 spaces after it, in bank 7 with interrupts off; the paging byte back.","comment":"HL = the name"},
        "14428": {"comment":"DE = $EF98 in bank 7"},
        "14431": {"comment":"Copied ($3F63)"},
        "14434": {"comment":"Interrupts off"},
        "14435": {"comment":"Bank 7, through port $7FFD"},
        "14445": {"comment":"HL = past the name"},
        "14446": {"comment":"16 spaces"},
        "14448": {"synopsis":"One space.","comment":"A space"},
        "14451": {"comment":"16?"},
        "14454": {"comment":"The paging byte back"},
        "14459": {"comment":"Interrupts on"},
        "14460": {"comment":"D = the unit; Z"},
        "14462": {"synopsis":"MOVE (class $0E, after the first string): what follows chooses:\n- FOR: MOVE \"old\" FOR \"new\" renames a partition (MOVE_FOR);\n- IN: MOVE \"x:\" IN \"partition\" [ASN] gives the drive letter to a partition (MOVE_IN);\n- OUT: MOVE \"x:\" OUT [ASN] takes the letter away (MOVE_OUT);\n- BIN: MOVE \"partition\" BIN deletes a partition (MOVE_BIN);\n- TO: MOVE \"a\" TO \"b\": the second string (ROM 3's CLASS_A), the statement's end, MOVE_CMD;\n- anything else: report C.","comment":"ROM 3's GET_CHAR"},
        "14463": {"comment":"FOR?"},
        "14468": {"comment":"IN?"},
        "14472": {"comment":"OUT?"},
        "14476": {"comment":"BIN?"},
        "14480": {"comment":"TO?"},
        "14482": {"comment":"No: report C"},
        "14485": {"comment":"Past TO"},
        "14486": {"comment":"ROM 3's CLASS_A: the new name"},
        "14489": {"comment":"The statement's end"},
        "14492": {"comment":"The file renamed"},
        "14495": {"synopsis":"MOVE \"x:\" IN \"partition\" [ASN]: the partition's name, ASN (ASN_OPTION), the statement's end;\nrunning, the partition found (ROM 2's PART_FIND_NAME, $00B5) unless a device was named, the\nletter (DRIVE_ARG) and ROM 2's LETTER_MAP ($00F1) with A = the unit or device, BC = the\nentry and L = the letter. With ASN ($5B66 bit 6) LETTER_MAP also keeps the letter on the\ndisk.","comment":"Past IN"},
        "14496": {"comment":"ROM 3's CLASS_A: the partition"},
        "14499": {"comment":"ASN?"},
        "14502": {"comment":"The statement's end"},
        "14505": {"comment":"The partition's name"},
        "14508": {"comment":"A = the unit or device, kept"},
        "14510": {"comment":"A device: no entry to find"},
        "14512": {"comment":"HL = the name"},
        "14515": {"comment":"Bank 7 and its stack"},
        "14518": {"comment":"Onto +3DOS's stack"},
        "14521": {"comment":"ROM 2's PART_FIND_NAME: BC = the entry"},
        "14526": {"comment":"Back to this ROM's stack"},
        "14529": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "14532": {"comment":"Not found: error A"},
        "14534": {"synopsis":"The drive letter (DRIVE_ARG), then ROM 2's LETTER_MAP.","comment":"The entry kept"},
        "14535": {"comment":"L = the letter"},
        "14538": {"comment":"BC = the entry"},
        "14539": {"comment":"A = the unit or device"},
        "14540": {"comment":"Bank 7 and its stack"},
        "14543": {"comment":"Onto +3DOS's stack"},
        "14546": {"comment":"ROM 2's LETTER_MAP"},
        "14551": {"comment":"Back to this ROM's stack"},
        "14554": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "14557": {"comment":"Done"},
        "14558": {"synopsis":"A +3DOS error in A (FILE_ERROR_A with $FF).","comment":"Error A"},
        "14562": {"synopsis":"MOVE \"x:\" OUT [ASN]: ASN (ASN_OPTION), the statement's end; running, the letter (DRIVE_ARG)\nand ROM 2's LETTER_UNMAP ($00F4); with ASN ($5B66 bit 6) it is taken from the disk too.","comment":"Past OUT"},
        "14563": {"comment":"ASN?"},
        "14566": {"comment":"The statement's end"},
        "14569": {"comment":"L = the letter"},
        "14572": {"comment":"Bank 7 and its stack"},
        "14575": {"comment":"Onto +3DOS's stack"},
        "14578": {"comment":"ROM 2's LETTER_UNMAP"},
        "14583": {"comment":"Back to this ROM's stack"},
        "14586": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "14589": {"comment":"Failed: error A"},
        "14592": {"synopsis":"MOVE \"partition\" BIN: the statement's end; running, \"Really delete partition (Y/N)?\"\n(ASK_YES_NO); the name (PART_NAME_ARG; a device is error $59); N ends; the partition found\n(ROM 2's PART_FIND_NAME, $00B5) and given back to free space (ROM 2's PART_FREE, $00BE).","comment":"Past BIN"},
        "14593": {"comment":"The statement's end"},
        "14596": {"comment":"\"Really delete partition (Y/N)?\""},
        "14602": {"comment":"The answer kept"},
        "14603": {"comment":"The partition's name"},
        "14606": {"comment":"A device: error $59"},
        "14609": {"comment":"The answer: N?"},
        "14613": {"comment":"A = the unit, kept"},
        "14615": {"comment":"HL = the name"},
        "14618": {"comment":"Bank 7 and its stack"},
        "14621": {"comment":"Onto +3DOS's stack"},
        "14624": {"comment":"ROM 2's PART_FIND_NAME: BC = the entry"},
        "14629": {"comment":"Back to this ROM's stack"},
        "14632": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "14635": {"comment":"Not found: error A"},
        "14637": {"comment":"A = the unit"},
        "14638": {"comment":"Bank 7 and its stack"},
        "14641": {"comment":"Onto +3DOS's stack"},
        "14644": {"comment":"ROM 2's PART_FREE"},
        "14649": {"comment":"Back to this ROM's stack"},
        "14652": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "14655": {"comment":"Done"},
        "14656": {"synopsis":"A +3DOS error in A (FILE_ERROR_A with $FF).","comment":"Error A"},
        "14660": {"synopsis":"An ASN may follow: $5B66 bit 6 set when it does (and CH_ADD past it), cleared when not.\nExit: A = the character after the operands (or ASN).\nChanges: AF, HL.","comment":"ROM 3's GET_CHAR"},
        "14661": {"comment":"$5B66 bit 6 cleared: no ASN"},
        "14666": {"comment":"ASN?"},
        "14669": {"comment":"Yes: bit 6 set"},
        "14671": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "14673": {"synopsis":"Takes a drive name from the calculator stack (ROM 3's STK_FETCH): two characters, a letter\nA-P (either case) and ':' (error $4E, Invalid drive, otherwise).\nExit: L = the letter, as a capital.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, L.","comment":"ROM 3's STK_FETCH"},
        "14676": {"comment":"Two characters?"},
        "14682": {"comment":"The second: ':'?"},
        "14688": {"comment":"The first, as a capital"},
        "14692": {"comment":"Below A?"},
        "14696": {"comment":"Above P?"},
        "14700": {"comment":"L = the letter"},
        "14702": {"synopsis":"Stops with error $4E (Invalid drive).","comment":"Error $4E: Invalid drive"},
        "14706": {"synopsis":"SPECTRUM (class $0E):\n- SPECTRUM alone: the statement's end and SPECTRUM_CMD (48 BASIC);\n- SPECTRUM INK, PAPER, FLASH, BRIGHT or ATTR n [ASN]: the +3 BASIC editor's colours\n(SPECTRUM_COLOUR), B = the bit position + 1 and C = the largest value: INK 1/7, PAPER 4/7,\nFLASH 8/1, BRIGHT 7/1, ATTR 1/$FF;\n- SPECTRUM \"name\": the statement's end; running, the name to $C04E in bank 7, $FF after it,\nand ROM 2's SNAP_LOAD ($00FD) loads and runs the snapshot; it returns only on failure\n(PART_FAIL).","comment":"ROM 3's GET_CHAR"},
        "14707": {"comment":"ATTR?"},
        "14709": {"comment":"Bit 0 up, at most 255"},
        "14714": {"comment":"INK?"},
        "14716": {"comment":"Bit 0 up, at most 7"},
        "14721": {"comment":"PAPER?"},
        "14723": {"comment":"Bit 3 up, at most 7"},
        "14728": {"comment":"FLASH?"},
        "14730": {"comment":"Bit 7, at most 1"},
        "14735": {"comment":"BRIGHT?"},
        "14737": {"comment":"Bit 6, at most 1"},
        "14742": {"comment":"ENTER?"},
        "14746": {"comment":"':'?"},
        "14748": {"comment":"No: a name"},
        "14750": {"synopsis":"SPECTRUM alone: the statement's end, then SPECTRUM_CMD.","comment":"The statement's end"},
        "14753": {"comment":"To 48 BASIC"},
        "14756": {"synopsis":"SPECTRUM \"name\": a snapshot loaded and run (ROM 2's SNAP_LOAD).","comment":"ROM 3's CLASS_A: the name"},
        "14759": {"comment":"The statement's end"},
        "14762": {"comment":"ROM 3's STK_FETCH"},
        "14765": {"comment":"HL = the name"},
        "14766": {"comment":"To $C04E in bank 7"},
        "14769": {"comment":"Copied ($3F63)"},
        "14772": {"comment":"Bank 7 and its stack"},
        "14775": {"comment":"$FF after it"},
        "14778": {"comment":"HL = the name"},
        "14781": {"comment":"Onto +3DOS's stack"},
        "14784": {"comment":"ROM 2's SNAP_LOAD: back only on failure"},
        "14789": {"comment":"Back to this ROM's stack"},
        "14792": {"comment":"Error A"},
        "14795": {"synopsis":"SPECTRUM INK ... ATTR n [ASN]: n (ROM 3's CLASS_6), ASN (ASN_OPTION), the statement's end;\nrunning, n must not be above C (report K otherwise); n and the mask C moved up B - 1 bits;\nthe bits replaced in $EC11 and $EC0F (bank 7, the editor's attributes). With ASN the\nresult and ATTR_P are also written into the hard disk (DEFAULTS_TO_DISK).","comment":"B and C kept"},
        "14796": {"comment":"Past the keyword"},
        "14797": {"comment":"ROM 3's CLASS_6: n"},
        "14800": {"comment":"ASN?"},
        "14803": {"comment":"B and C back"},
        "14804": {"comment":"The statement's end"},
        "14807": {"comment":"Kept round it"},
        "14808": {"comment":"ROM 3's FIND_INT1: A = n"},
        "14812": {"comment":"D = n"},
        "14813": {"comment":"Above C?"},
        "14817": {"comment":"Report K: Invalid colour"},
        "14821": {"synopsis":"n and the mask moved up a bit, B - 1 times.","comment":"Moved enough?"},
        "14824": {"comment":"n up a bit"},
        "14826": {"comment":"The mask too"},
        "14830": {"synopsis":"In bank 7: the bits replaced in $EC11, and the result copied to $EC0F; with ASN on to\nDEFAULTS_TO_DISK with H = it.","comment":"Bank 7 and its stack"},
        "14833": {"comment":"C = NOT the mask"},
        "14836": {"comment":"$EC11's other bits"},
        "14840": {"comment":"n in"},
        "14841": {"comment":"$EC11 and $EC0F set"},
        "14847": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "14850": {"comment":"ASN ($5B66 bit 6)?"},
        "14855": {"comment":"No: done"},
        "14856": {"comment":"H = the attribute"},
        "14857": {"comment":"A = 0: unit 0"},
        "14858": {"comment":"Written into the disk"},
        "14861": {"synopsis":"CAT #n followed by something other than ',', the end or EXP: TAB (CAT_TAB) or ASN (CAT_ASN);\nanything else is report C.","comment":"TAB?"},
        "14865": {"comment":"ASN?"},
        "14870": {"comment":"Report C: Nonsense in BASIC"},
        "14874": {"synopsis":"CAT without '#' and not at the end: EXP (CAT_ALL), ASN (CAT_ASN), TAB (CAT_TAB) or a name\n(CAT_NAME).","comment":"EXP?"},
        "14879": {"comment":"ASN?"},
        "14884": {"comment":"TAB?"},
        "14886": {"comment":"No: a name"},
        "14889": {"synopsis":"CAT TAB [EXP]: lists the partitions of both hard disk units. Past TAB; EXP sets $5B66 bit 6\n(the start and end of each partition shown too); the statement's end. Running, in bank 7,\nfor unit 0 then 1: \"IDE unit u\"; the probe (ROM 2's HD_UNIT_PROBE): \" (cylinders/heads/\nsectors)\" or \" (not detected)\"; then each entry of the partition table (ROM 2's\nPART_ENTRY_READ, $00C4, into $EF98) from 0: the unused ones (type 0) counted, the others\nprinted (CAT_TAB_NAME); the table's end (error $38) prints the count and \" free partition\nentries\"; error $16 goes to the next unit, any other is reported (PART_FAIL).","comment":"Past TAB"},
        "14890": {"comment":"EXP?"},
        "14894": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "14895": {"comment":"$5B66 bit 6 set: EXP"},
        "14900": {"synopsis":"The statement's end; running, the two units in bank 7.","comment":"The statement's end"},
        "14903": {"comment":"Bank 7 and its stack"},
        "14906": {"comment":"Two units"},
        "14908": {"synopsis":"One unit: A = 0 or 1. \"IDE unit \", the digit, then the probe.","comment":"The unit counter kept"},
        "14909": {"comment":"A = 2 - B: the unit"},
        "14912": {"comment":"DE = 0: no unused entries yet"},
        "14916": {"comment":"The unit kept"},
        "14917": {"comment":"\"IDE unit \""},
        "14923": {"comment":"The unit back"},
        "14925": {"comment":"C = the unit"},
        "14926": {"comment":"The digit"},
        "14931": {"comment":"The probe's bank: 7"},
        "14933": {"comment":"HL = the buffer"},
        "14936": {"comment":"Onto +3DOS's stack"},
        "14939": {"comment":"ROM 2's HD_UNIT_PROBE"},
        "14944": {"comment":"Back to this ROM's stack"},
        "14947": {"comment":"$42: the unit answered?"},
        "14949": {"comment":"Carry clear"},
        "14951": {"comment":"No: \" (not detected)\""},
        "14953": {"comment":"IX = the probe's bytes"},
        "14957": {"comment":"\" (\""},
        "14963": {"comment":"The cylinders: bytes 1 and 256"},
        "14973": {"comment":"No blanks"},
        "14975": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "14978": {"comment":"'/'"},
        "14983": {"comment":"The heads: byte 3"},
        "14990": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "14993": {"comment":"'/'"},
        "14998": {"comment":"The sectors per track: byte 6"},
        "15005": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "15008": {"comment":"')'"},
        "15013": {"comment":"ENTER"},
        "15018": {"synopsis":"The partition table from entry 0.","comment":"Entry 0"},
        "15021": {"synopsis":"Entry BC of the unit read into $EF98 (ROM 2's PART_ENTRY_READ); an error ends the unit\n(CAT_TAB_ERROR). Type 0, unused, is counted; any other is printed (CAT_TAB_NAME).","comment":"A = the unit"},
        "15023": {"comment":"HL = $EF98"},
        "15026": {"comment":"Onto +3DOS's stack"},
        "15029": {"comment":"ROM 2's PART_ENTRY_READ"},
        "15034": {"comment":"Back to this ROM's stack"},
        "15037": {"comment":"Failed: the end or an error"},
        "15040": {"comment":"IX = the entry"},
        "15044": {"comment":"Its type: 0, unused?"},
        "15049": {"comment":"No: printed"},
        "15051": {"comment":"One more unused"},
        "15056": {"comment":"The next entry"},
        "15059": {"synopsis":"No answer: \" (not detected)\" and ENTER; the table is still read.","comment":"\" (not detected)\", ENTER"},
        "15065": {"comment":"On"},
        "15067": {"synopsis":"A partition: its 16-character name ($00 shown as '~'), a space, its size: from the entry's\nbytes $17-$1A, sectors, halved to K when below 65536 (\"K \"), else divided by 2048 to\nmegabytes (\"Mb \"); then its type (CAT_TAB_TYPE).","comment":"The entry kept"},
        "15068": {"comment":"HL = the name"},
        "15071": {"comment":"16 characters"},
        "15073": {"synopsis":"One character of the name.","comment":"The character"},
        "15075": {"comment":"$00?"},
        "15078": {"comment":"Then '~'"},
        "15080": {"synopsis":"Printed; the next.","comment":"Printed"},
        "15083": {"comment":"All 16?"},
        "15086": {"comment":"A space"},
        "15091": {"comment":"HL = bytes $18-$19"},
        "15097": {"comment":"E = byte $1A"},
        "15100": {"comment":"Below 65536 sectors?"},
        "15104": {"comment":"HL = bytes $17-$18"},
        "15108": {"comment":"Plus 1, halved: the K"},
        "15113": {"comment":"Blanks before the digits"},
        "15115": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "15118": {"comment":"\"K \""},
        "15121": {"comment":"On"},
        "15123": {"synopsis":"64K sectors or more: bytes $18-$1A divided by 8, megabytes, and \"Mb \".","comment":"A collects the bits shifted out"},
        "15124": {"comment":"E:H:L / 2"},
        "15131": {"comment":"/ 4"},
        "15138": {"comment":"/ 8"},
        "15144": {"comment":"Blanks before the digits"},
        "15146": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "15149": {"comment":"\"Mb \""},
        "15152": {"synopsis":"The size's text printed; then the type's name: 1 \"system\", 2 \"swap\", 3 \"data \", 4 \"CPM\nPhys\", 5 \"Boot HW\", $0F \"Movie\", $10 \"FAT16\", $20 \"UZIX\", $FE \"*BAD*\", $FF \"FREE\", $3x \"Disk\nImg\", $4x \"CPM Img\", any other \"unknown\".","comment":"\"K \" or \"Mb \""},
        "15155": {"comment":"The type"},
        "15158": {"comment":"1: \"system\""},
        "15165": {"comment":"2: \"swap\""},
        "15172": {"comment":"3: \"data \""},
        "15179": {"comment":"4: \"CPM Phys\""},
        "15186": {"comment":"5: \"Boot HW\""},
        "15193": {"comment":"$0F: \"Movie\""},
        "15200": {"comment":"$10: \"FAT16\""},
        "15207": {"comment":"$20: \"UZIX\""},
        "15214": {"comment":"$FE: \"*BAD*\""},
        "15221": {"comment":"$FF: \"FREE\""},
        "15228": {"comment":"$3x: \"Disk Img\""},
        "15237": {"comment":"$4x: \"CPM Img\""},
        "15244": {"comment":"Any other: \"unknown\""},
        "15247": {"synopsis":"The type's name printed; a data partition (type 3) with a drive letter (byte $3C) shows it\nand ':'.","comment":"Printed"},
        "15250": {"comment":"Type 3?"},
        "15257": {"comment":"A drive letter (byte $3C)?"},
        "15263": {"comment":"The letter"},
        "15266": {"comment":"':'"},
        "15271": {"synopsis":"ENTER; with EXP, \"Start: \" cylinder,head \" End: \" cylinder,head (bytes $11-$13 and $14-$16)\nand ENTER.","comment":"ENTER"},
        "15276": {"comment":"EXP ($5B66 bit 6)?"},
        "15281": {"comment":"No: the next"},
        "15283": {"comment":"\"Start: \""},
        "15289": {"comment":"The first cylinder"},
        "15300": {"comment":"','"},
        "15305": {"comment":"The first head"},
        "15315": {"comment":"\" End: \""},
        "15321": {"comment":"The last cylinder"},
        "15332": {"comment":"','"},
        "15337": {"comment":"The last head"},
        "15347": {"comment":"ENTER"},
        "15352": {"synopsis":"The entry back; the next.","comment":"The entry back"},
        "15353": {"synopsis":"The next entry, until BC wraps to 0.","comment":"The next entry"},
        "15356": {"comment":"More?"},
        "15359": {"synopsis":"The end of the table: the count of unused entries and \" free partition entries\", two ENTERs.","comment":"The unit dropped"},
        "15360": {"comment":"HL = the unused entries"},
        "15361": {"comment":"No blanks"},
        "15363": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "15366": {"comment":"\" free partition entries\""},
        "15372": {"synopsis":"The next unit; after both, bank 0.","comment":"The unit counter"},
        "15373": {"comment":"Another unit?"},
        "15377": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "15381": {"synopsis":"PART_ENTRY_READ failed: error $38 is the table's end (CAT_TAB_FREE); $16 ends the unit with\nno count; another is reported (PART_FAIL).","comment":"$38: the table's end?"},
        "15385": {"comment":"$16?"},
        "15389": {"comment":"The unit and count dropped"},
        "15391": {"comment":"The next unit"},
        "15393": {"synopsis":"Bank 0, then the +3DOS error in A reported (PART_DOS_ERROR). From CAT_TAB, CAT_ASN and\nSPECTRUM_SNAP.","comment":"Bank 0"},
        "15396": {"comment":"Error A"},
        "15399": {"synopsis":"CAT TAB's text: \"Mb \", $00."},
        "15403": {"synopsis":"CAT TAB's text: \"K \", $00."},
        "15406": {"synopsis":"CAT TAB's text: \" free partition entries\", two ENTERs, $00."},
        "15432": {"synopsis":"CAT TAB's text: \"IDE unit \", $00."},
        "15442": {"synopsis":"CAT TAB's text: \"swap\", $00."},
        "15447": {"synopsis":"CAT TAB's text: \"data \", $00."},
        "15453": {"synopsis":"CAT TAB's text: \"*BAD*\", $00."},
        "15459": {"synopsis":"CAT TAB's text: \"FREE\", $00."},
        "15464": {"synopsis":"CAT TAB's text: \"unknown\", $00."},
        "15472": {"synopsis":"CAT TAB's text: \" End: \", $00."},
        "15479": {"synopsis":"CAT TAB's text: \" (\", $00."},
        "15482": {"synopsis":"CAT TAB's text: \" (not detected)\", ENTER, $00."},
        "15499": {"synopsis":"CAT TAB's text: \"CPM Phys\", $00."},
        "15508": {"synopsis":"CAT TAB's text: \"Boot HW\", $00."},
        "15516": {"synopsis":"CAT TAB's text: \"Movie\", $00."},
        "15522": {"synopsis":"CAT TAB's text: \"FAT16\", $00."},
        "15528": {"synopsis":"CAT TAB's text: \"UZIX\", $00."},
        "15533": {"synopsis":"CAT TAB's text: \"Disk Img\", $00."},
        "15542": {"synopsis":"CAT TAB's text: \"CPM Img\", $00."},
        "15550": {"synopsis":"NEW_PARTITION's 29 bytes copied to $EFB8 (the new entry's bytes $20-$3C, the drive's\nparameters), before the values that hang on the size are written over them: $00 $02 $00 $00\n$00 $00 $00 $FF $01 $00 $00 $80 $00 $00 $02 $03 $00 $00 $80 $00 $00 $02 and seven $00."},
        "15579": {"synopsis":"CAT ASN: past ASN, the statement's end; running, in bank 7, for each letter A-P ROM 2's\nLETTER_DESCRIBE ($00F7) into 18 bytes at $EF98: a letter in use is printed with ':', a\nspace, the 18 bytes and ENTER. A failure is reported (PART_FAIL).","comment":"Past ASN"},
        "15580": {"comment":"The statement's end"},
        "15583": {"comment":"Bank 7 and its stack"},
        "15586": {"comment":"16 letters"},
        "15588": {"comment":"From A"},
        "15590": {"synopsis":"One letter: what it stands for.","comment":"Kept"},
        "15592": {"comment":"BC = the 18 bytes"},
        "15595": {"comment":"Onto +3DOS's stack"},
        "15598": {"comment":"ROM 2's LETTER_DESCRIBE"},
        "15603": {"comment":"Back to this ROM's stack"},
        "15606": {"comment":"Failed: error A"},
        "15609": {"comment":"Z: no drive for it"},
        "15611": {"comment":"L = the letter"},
        "15613": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "15617": {"comment":"':'"},
        "15622": {"comment":"A space"},
        "15627": {"comment":"The description"},
        "15630": {"comment":"18 characters"},
        "15632": {"synopsis":"One character of the description.","comment":"Printed"},
        "15637": {"comment":"All 18?"},
        "15639": {"comment":"ENTER"},
        "15644": {"synopsis":"The next letter; after P, bank 0.","comment":"The letter and count back"},
        "15646": {"comment":"The next letter"},
        "15649": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "15653": {"synopsis":"MOVE \"old\" FOR \"new\": the new name (ROM 3's CLASS_A), the statement's end; running, the new\nname (empty: error $2C; 16 characters at most) to $C04E in bank 7; the old one\n(PART_NAME_ARG;\na device is error $59) found (ROM 2's PART_FIND_NAME, $00B5); the new name padded with\nspaces\nto 17 bytes and given to the entry (ROM 2's PART_RENAME, $00C1).","comment":"Past FOR"},
        "15654": {"comment":"ROM 3's CLASS_A: the new name"},
        "15657": {"comment":"The statement's end"},
        "15660": {"comment":"ROM 3's STK_FETCH"},
        "15663": {"comment":"BC = its length"},
        "15666": {"comment":"Empty?"},
        "15669": {"comment":"Error $2C: Bad filename"},
        "15673": {"synopsis":"16 characters at most.","comment":"Over 16?"},
        "15677": {"comment":"16"},
        "15679": {"synopsis":"The new name to $C04E in bank 7; the old one found.","comment":"The length kept"},
        "15680": {"comment":"HL = the name"},
        "15681": {"comment":"To $C04E in bank 7"},
        "15684": {"comment":"Copied ($3F63)"},
        "15687": {"comment":"The old name"},
        "15690": {"comment":"A = the unit"},
        "15691": {"comment":"A device: error $59"},
        "15694": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "15695": {"comment":"HL = the old name"},
        "15698": {"comment":"Bank 7 and its stack"},
        "15701": {"comment":"Onto +3DOS's stack"},
        "15704": {"comment":"ROM 2's PART_FIND_NAME: BC = the entry"},
        "15709": {"comment":"Back to this ROM's stack"},
        "15712": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "15715": {"comment":"Not found: error A"},
        "15717": {"comment":"A = the unit"},
        "15718": {"comment":"E = the new name's length"},
        "15719": {"comment":"Bank 7 and its stack"},
        "15722": {"comment":"HL = past the new name"},
        "15726": {"comment":"D = the unit"},
        "15727": {"comment":"17 - the length: the spaces"},
        "15730": {"synopsis":"One space after the new name.","comment":"A space"},
        "15733": {"comment":"All?"},
        "15736": {"comment":"A = the unit"},
        "15737": {"comment":"HL = the new name"},
        "15740": {"comment":"Onto +3DOS's stack"},
        "15743": {"comment":"ROM 2's PART_RENAME"},
        "15748": {"comment":"Back to this ROM's stack"},
        "15751": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "15754": {"comment":"Done"},
        "15755": {"synopsis":"A +3DOS error in A (FILE_ERROR_A with $FF).","comment":"Error A"},
        "15759": {"synopsis":"Writes the editor's attribute H and ATTR_P into the bytes kept for entry 0 of unit A's\npartition table (A = 0 from SPECTRUM_COLOUR): byte 8 = H, byte 9 = ATTR_P, through ROM 2's\nPART_BYTE_SET ($00D6) twice.","comment":"BC = 0: entry 0"},
        "15761": {"comment":"Byte 8"},
        "15763": {"comment":"Bank 7 and its stack"},
        "15766": {"comment":"Onto +3DOS's stack"},
        "15769": {"comment":"ROM 2's PART_BYTE_SET: byte 8 = H"},
        "15774": {"comment":"H = ATTR_P"},
        "15778": {"comment":"Byte 9"},
        "15780": {"comment":"Unit 0, entry 0"},
        "15783": {"comment":"ROM 2's PART_BYTE_SET: byte 9"},
        "15788": {"comment":"Back to this ROM's stack"},
        "15791": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "15795": {"synopsis":"Calculator code run through RUN_ON_STACK by GO_TO_STREAM (13 bytes): RST $28, exchange\n($01), st-mem-1 ($C1), delete ($02), stk-data ($34; $40 $41 $00 $00, 65536), n-mod-m ($32),\nget-mem-1 ($E1), end-calc ($38), RET: the stream s and position p on the stack become p\nmod 65536, INT (p / 65536) and s on top."},
        "16000": {"synopsis":"Calls the address in the word after the CALL in ROM 0, keeping AF, BC and HL (parked at\n$5B56, $5B54 and $5B52): the word is read into HL and the return address stepped past it;\nbit 4 of the paging byte $5B5C (port $7FFD) is cleared with interrupts off, which pages ROM\n0 in, and the code goes on at $3EA2 in ROM 0's copy (its CALL_ROM1); CALL_ROM0_BACK is\npushed as the return, AF, BC and HL are restored and the RET jumps to the address. The\nreturn runs ROM 0's $3EB5, which sets the bit again and comes back here at $3EC5. ROM 0 has\nthe same routine here with the bit set. Called at $1351, $1407, $226B, $2342, $2599, $2681\nand $26CD.","comment":"HL parked"},
        "16003": {"comment":"BC parked"},
        "16007": {"comment":"AF parked"},
        "16009": {"comment":"At $5B56"},
        "16012": {"comment":"The word after the CALL"},
        "16013": {"comment":"BC = the address"},
        "16017": {"comment":"Return address stepped past it"},
        "16018": {"comment":"HL = the address"},
        "16020": {"comment":"Bit 4 of port $7FFD cleared: ROM 0"},
        "16023": {"comment":"Bit 4 cleared"},
        "16026": {"comment":"Copy and port, no interrupts"},
        "16032": {"comment":"ROM 0 in: on at $3EA2 there"},
        "16034": {"comment":"From here in ROM 0"},
        "16035": {"comment":"The way back first"},
        "16039": {"comment":"Then the address"},
        "16040": {"comment":"AF, BC and HL back"},
        "16044": {"comment":"AF from $5B56"},
        "16045": {"comment":"BC from $5B54"},
        "16049": {"comment":"HL from $5B52"},
        "16052": {"comment":"To the address"},
        "16053": {"synopsis":"Where a routine of this ROM called through ROM 0's CALL_ROM1 returns: bit 4 of $5B5C (port\n$7FFD) cleared again with interrupts off, which pages ROM 0 back in, keeping AF and BC; the\ncode after the OUT at $3EC3 runs in ROM 0. This ROM's own calls through CALL_ROM0 come back\nby ROM 0's copy and run $3EC5-$3EC8 here.","comment":"AF and BC kept"},
        "16055": {"comment":"Bit 4 of port $7FFD cleared: ROM 0"},
        "16058": {"comment":"Bit 4 cleared"},
        "16061": {"comment":"Copy and port, no interrupts"},
        "16067": {"comment":"ROM 0 in: on at $3EC5 there"},
        "16069": {"comment":"From here in ROM 0"},
        "16070": {"comment":"BC and AF back"},
        "16073": {"synopsis":"COPY_FILES_DONE's message for one file: ENTER, '  1 file copied.', two ENTERs, ended by $00\n(PRINT_NAME)."},
        "16093": {"synopsis":"COPY_FILES_DONE's message after the count of files: ' files copied.', two ENTERs, ended by\n$00."},
        "16128": {"synopsis":"Calls the address in the word after the CALL in ROM 2 (+3DOS; the word is a DOS_JUMPS\nentry), keeping AF, BC and HL (parked at $5B56, $5B54 and $5B52): the word is read into BC,\nthe return address stepped past it and CALL_ROM2_BACK stacked as the routine's return; bit 4\nof $5B5C (port $7FFD) is cleared, and that OUT, at $3F24, pages ROM 0 in, whose copy of\nthese\nbytes sets bit 2 of $5B67 (port $1FFD), which pages ROM 2 in; the code goes on at $3F33\nthere: the address pushed, AF, BC and HL restored and the RET jumps to the address. ROMs 0\nand 2 have the same bytes here. Called some 95 times, each between DOS_STACK_SAVE and\nDOS_STACK_BACK.","comment":"HL parked"},
        "16131": {"comment":"BC parked"},
        "16135": {"comment":"AF parked"},
        "16137": {"comment":"At $5B56"},
        "16140": {"comment":"The word after the CALL"},
        "16141": {"comment":"BC = the address"},
        "16145": {"comment":"Return address stepped past it"},
        "16146": {"comment":"The way back first: CALL_ROM2_BACK"},
        "16150": {"comment":"HL = the address"},
        "16152": {"comment":"Bit 4 of port $7FFD cleared: ROM 0"},
        "16155": {"comment":"Bit 4 cleared"},
        "16158": {"comment":"Copy and port, no interrupts"},
        "16164": {"comment":"ROM 0 in: on at $3F26 there"},
        "16166": {"comment":"From here in ROM 0: bit 2 of $1FFD set"},
        "16169": {"comment":"Bit 2 set"},
        "16174": {"comment":"Port $1FFD"},
        "16177": {"comment":"ROM 2 in: on at $3F33 there"},
        "16179": {"comment":"From here in ROM 2"},
        "16180": {"comment":"Then the address"},
        "16181": {"comment":"AF, BC and HL back"},
        "16185": {"comment":"AF from $5B56"},
        "16186": {"comment":"BC from $5B54"},
        "16190": {"comment":"HL from $5B52"},
        "16193": {"comment":"To the address"},
        "16194": {"synopsis":"The way back from ROM 2 to this ROM, keeping AF and BC: ROM 2 clears bit 2 of port $1FFD\n(and $5B67), which pages ROM 0 in, whose copy runs $3F52-$3F5D and sets bit 4 of port $7FFD\n(and $5B5C), which pages this ROM back in for the RET at $3F62.","comment":"BC and AF kept"},
        "16196": {"comment":"Bit 2 of port $1FFD cleared: ROM 0"},
        "16199": {"comment":"Bit 2 cleared"},
        "16202": {"comment":"Copy and port, no interrupts"},
        "16208": {"comment":"ROM 0 in: on at $3F52 there"},
        "16210": {"comment":"From here in ROM 0: bit 4 set"},
        "16213": {"comment":"Bit 4 set"},
        "16218": {"comment":"Port $7FFD"},
        "16221": {"comment":"ROM 1 in: on at $3F5F here"},
        "16223": {"comment":"From here in this ROM"},
        "16224": {"comment":"AF and BC back"},
        "16227": {"synopsis":"Copies BC bytes from HL in RAM bank 0 to DE in RAM bank 7, a byte at a time, flipping port\n$7FFD between $10 (bank 0) and $17 (bank 7) with BC' = $7FFD; then the paging byte $5B5C\nwritten back. Only ROM 1 has this; ROMs 0 and 2 are unused here. Interrupts off while it\nruns, on at the end.\nEntry: HL = the source, DE = the destination, BC = the count (not 0).\nChanges: AF, AF', BC = 0, DE, HL, BC'.","comment":"No interrupts while banks flip"},
        "16229": {"comment":"BC' = port $7FFD"},
        "16233": {"synopsis":"One byte: read in bank 0, written in bank 7."},
        "16234": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "16239": {"comment":"The byte"},
        "16240": {"comment":"Kept in A'"},
        "16242": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "16248": {"comment":"Written"},
        "16251": {"comment":"Count down"},
        "16256": {"comment":"The paging byte back"},
        "16264": {"comment":"Interrupts on"},
        "16266": {"synopsis":"Copies BC bytes from HL in RAM bank 7 to DE in RAM bank 0, as COPY_TO_BANK7 the other way;\nthen the paging byte $5B5C written back. Called at $0BA1.\nEntry: HL = the source, DE = the destination, BC = the count (not 0).\nChanges: AF, AF', BC = 0, DE, HL, BC'.","comment":"No interrupts while banks flip"},
        "16268": {"comment":"BC' = port $7FFD"},
        "16272": {"synopsis":"One byte: read in bank 7, written in bank 0."},
        "16273": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "16278": {"comment":"The byte"},
        "16279": {"comment":"Kept in A'"},
        "16281": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "16287": {"comment":"Written"},
        "16290": {"comment":"Count down"},
        "16295": {"comment":"The paging byte back"},
        "16303": {"comment":"Interrupts on"},
        "16305": {"synopsis":"CAT_FREE_DRIVE's \"K free\", ENTER, $00."},
        "16313": {"synopsis":"CAT_NO_FILES's \"No files found\", ENTER, $00."},
        "16329": {"synopsis":"ERASE_ASK's \"Erase \", $00."},
        "16336": {"synopsis":"ERASE_ASK's \" ? (Y/N)\", $00."}
      }
    }
  },
